window.FWN_MADAMS_IDENTITIES_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MADAMS_IDENTITIES_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":501,"title":"Chapter 501 - Still Want Sister Nian to Take Off Her Skin","paragraphs":["Wei Dongshan looked surprised and frowned. “Is this Qiao Nian delusional?”","The night breeze in October was cold. Wei Ling adjusted her shawl and answered him with a fake smile, “She doesn’t care about us because she has a powerful background. She’s fearless, so of course she’s arrogant.”","“She has a backer? What backer?” Wei Dongshan looked puzzled. “I looked at her profile. She’s just an ordinary high school student. Her grades are not bad. She studied at Rao City Middle School and was in Class A. You might not know it since you’re in Beijing all year round. No.1 Middle School is the best school in Rao City. Class A is the top class in No.1 Middle School. Every year, No.1 Middle School will be able to enter many key universities. 80% of them are students from this class...”","“She didn’t get into Class A with her grades.”","Wei Ling couldn’t be bothered to explain to him that Qiao Nian had gone to Beijing to participate in the Qing University enrollment examination and did not manage to get in.","She only reminded him implicitly, “She has the backing of the Jiang family. You’ve always heard of Old Master Jiang’s name. It’s not difficult for that Old Master to send her to the top class of a No.1 Middle School.”","The surname Jiang was very common, but there was only one Jiang family in the top circle in Rao City. It was the Jiang family that had moved to Beijing to develop ten years ago.","He was stunned for a moment. He didn’t expect there to be such a relationship behind this little high school student.","“She’s from the Jiang family?”","“...Half. She’s not considered a real member of the Jiang family. Speaking of which, I still have some ties with this Qiao Nian.” Wei Ling used a cold tone to simply tell him about the real daughter of the Qiao family. In the end, she said in a deep voice, “I don’t think the Jiang family put much effort into her. They didn’t even bring her back to Beijing when the college entrance examination was coming up. It looks like they only let her have a name on the genealogy. The Jiang family values that Jiang Xianrou the most.”","“...But this has nothing to do with us. Even if the Jiang family values her, she can forget about easily beating Wei Qi up this time. I don’t want her to fight with her life, but I want her to at least be skinned alive!”","When Wei Ling said this, the fox fur coat couldn’t hide her murderous expression. He could tell that she had been really angered by Qiao Nian.","With that, she swallowed her anger and looked up at Wei Dongshan. “Is that Cai Gang still protecting Qiao Nian?”","At the mention of Cai Gang, Wei Dongshan couldn’t help but frown in frustration.","“Ah, his attitude is still the same. He’s arguing that this case is still under investigation. They can’t close the case in a hurry. They have to investigate clearly...”","When Wei Ling heard this, she couldn’t hide her anger anymore. She clenched her fists and said angrily, “Wei Qi is lying in the hospital bed and can’t get out. What do they want to investigate?”","“The hospital said he has a light injury. I just called a familiar lawyer. The lawyer said the same thing. A light injury does not constitute criminal responsibility. He insisted on protecting the person who hit him. There’s nothing we can do about it.”","Wei Dongshan was also angry. Cai Gang’s actions were undoubtedly a slap in his face on his territory. However, he had asked the lawyer, and the lawyer had the same intention. They could ask Qiao Nian for compensation.","When did the Wei family ever lack money?","They wanted to hack the culprit into pieces as a warning to others!","Who wanted compensation of 180,000 yuan?","“The results of the injury analysis are easy to handle. It’s not like there’s only one hospital in the city. I’ll immediately arrange for someone to transfer Wei Qi to another hospital and do a new diagnosis.” Wei Ling had already made plans. She narrowed her eyes and asked him, “How long will it take for Cai Gang to investigate?”","Wei Dongshan wasn’t even 1.8 meters tall. He was only 1.78 meters tall. Wearing a suit, he still looked neat and tidy. At this moment, he pushed the gold-framed glasses on his nose bridge, and his eyes behind the glasses were cold. “He said he wants three days.”"]},{"number":502,"title":"Chapter 502 - If I Said I Didn’t Notice the Message, Will You Believe Me?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","“Three days?” Wei Ling was dissatisfied and frowned immediately. She looked at him coldly and said, “Let Cai Gang know I’ll only give him one day. I’ll supervise him while he investigates. If he still cannot produce the results by tomorrow night, I’ll look for his superiors and ask them to investigate instead, and at the same time, investigate him!”","With the strength of the Wei Family behind her, she naturally had the confidence to say this.","This circle followed the law of the jungle. The big fish would eat the smaller fishes, and in turn, the smaller fishes would eat the shrimps.","Naturally, the big fish would have the absolute right to speak within the circle. Cai Gang had never stepped foot into the real world before and insisted on fighting against Wei Ling for the sake of the Jiang Family. The Jiang Family had some influence, but this was true for the Wei Family too. In fact, the Wei Family had more influence than the Jiang Family!","This time, she had to stand up for Wei Qi!","Wei Dongshan had long been dissatisfied with Cai Gang’s behavior of always finding excuses to dodge his responsibility. After he heard that, the corner of his mouth raised slightly, and he immediately said, “Okay. I’ll inform him.”","...","In the interrogation room.","Qiao Nian had just sent Wei Ling away when Cai Gang came in holding a cell phone.","He spoke with someone briefly and then handed the cell phone to her, saying, “Miss Qiao, there’s a video call meant for you. Please answer it.”","“Oh? Who is calling me?”","Cai Gang hesitated, not daring to respond. He slipped the cell phone into her hand and said, “It’s just a phone call, Miss Qiao. Please take a look at it and you will know.”","“...”","Qiao Nian was relaxedly leaned back in her chair. Su Huaiyuan hadn’t arrived yet, and she wasn’t able to leave. Now Cai Gang was insisting that she answer the phone. She wondered why the person didn’t call her directly and instead called Cai Gang to pass the call to her.","Seeing Gu San’s face, she was surprised, and her temples jumped up a little.","Gu San wasn’t the main point. The main point was the person standing beside him!","Ye Wangchuan.","She now understood why Cai Gang hesitated and did not dare to say who was calling just now.","“Miss Qiao, are you alright?” Gu San immediately asked nervously when he saw her. The worry on his face did not seem fake.","“I’m fine.”","Her voice was hoarse.","She was initially leaning against the back of her chair with her long legs stretched out casually. But when she realized who was calling, she sat up straight and held onto the cell phone. Looking up, she saw Cai Gang slipping away very quickly. He gave her a sign and said, “Take your time. I’ll head out first.”","Before Qiao Nian could stop him, he had already left the room.","“How did you guys think of calling Officer Cai?” she lowered her gaze and asked calmly.","Gu San was worried that she was alone at the police station and would be bullied by the others. But seeing her complacent and not seeming like she was being bullied by anyone, he felt more reassured and his heart grew lighter. He looked around, hesitated for a moment, and said, “Master Wang was afraid that your cell phone had been confiscated and that we wouldn’t be able to reach you. Therefore, we decided to call Cai Gang and ask him to pass his cell phone to you instead.”","In fact, the reason was that Master Wang had sent a message to Miss Qiao asking her where she was, but she didn’t reply.","Master Wang thought that her cell phone had been confiscated and thought of such a way to contact her.","Looking at Qiao Nian’s attitude, it was obvious that her freedom was not restricted. The reason she did not reply to Master Wang’s message was likely because she didn’t feel like replying!","He lit a candle for Master Wang in his heart.","His expression bitter, he then asked her a question, “Miss Qiao, could you check your cell phone?”","Picking up her cell phone from the table, Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes. Sure enough, there was a message from Ye Wangchuan.","She opened the message.","[Ye Wangchuan: Where are you?]","Silence ensued for a couple of seconds.","Qiao Nian put down her cell phone and looked up with dark and translucent eyes, then spoke with sincerity. “If I said I didn’t notice the message, will you believe me?”"]},{"number":503,"title":"Chapter 503 - He Was the Worm in His Own Stomach","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Gu San subconsciously turned his head to look at the man next to him and almost blurted out what was on his mind. Fortunately, he managed to hold onto his words and swallowed them silently.","Restless, Qiao Nian pressed down on the rim of her cap. Although she didn’t know how to explain it to him, she felt that it was necessary. “Someone came in to talk to me just now. I was preoccupied with the conversation and did not check my cell phone.”","She didn’t finish her sentence.","Messages asking her where she was or what she was doing were usually regarded as junk. If these messages were sent by people she was not familiar with, she wouldn’t even bother replying to them.","However, if it was sent by Ye Wangchuan, she would most likely reply to him.","Qiao Nian was very irritable. She didn’t know why she subconsciously felt that she would reply to him. She pursed her lips and raised her eyes.","“I did not intentionally forget to reply to you.”","Seeing that she was all right, Ye Wangchuan felt relieved. He couldn’t bring himself to quarrel with her over the fact that she didn’t reply to his message. It was a small matter. He raised his eyebrows, looked at her with burning eyes, and asked, “Someone was looking for you?”","At this question, a trace of ridicule flashed on Qiao Nian’s face. It was obvious that she didn’t take it seriously by how relaxed she looked. “More than one person came to find me. Two or three groups of people came here already.”","Ye Wangchuan changed the direction the cell phone was facing; he could now see her more clearly. He was expressionless and looked slightly cold, so she couldn’t tell if he was angry or not.","“Why were they looking for you?”","Seeing that he didn’t harp on the message, Qiao Nian relaxed. Then, her eyes became cold. Although she was sitting casually, her eyes were still wild. “It was nothing much. They said that there’s still time for me to cry and regret my actions. They also persuaded me to admit my mistakes, then they would be willing to let me go.”","Gu San was speechless. Hearing her speak so casually and seeing the vigor on her face, his lips twitched.","Miss Qiao, I know you aren’t afraid, but could you give some face to the Wei Family and restrain yourself a little?","If the Wei Family saw Miss Qiao’s careless attitude now, they would be very angry!","He didn’t know that Qiao Nian had already made Wei Ling angry. She was so angry that her chest hurt and she had difficulty breathing for some time.","Seeing her casual attitude towards this matter, the corners of Ye Wangchuan’s mouth lifted, forming a smile. He was relieved.","His eyes could peer into someone’s heart. While Gu San was still worrying and looking like a fool, he had already understood what Qiao Nian was trying to say.","“Do you have something that could implicate Wei Qi?” he casually asked.","Most of the time, the tone of his voice was very similar to Qiao Nian’s. He had a very casual tone of speaking. It was as though there were many things in this world that he couldn’t be bothered about. Even when he was investigating the illegal area, Gu San noticed that he was able to do it with ease and with a lazy attitude.","Only when it came to matters concerning Qiao Nian did Gu San could see a caring look on his face.","Gu San silently looked away. He felt as though he didn’t have a place in this video call. He was no better than the background around them.","This was because he could not understand what Master Wang was talking about.","Although Wei Qi wasn’t hardworking, he was still a member of the Wei Family. No matter how influential Miss Qiao was, she only knew people from Rao City. How could she have gotten her hands on information that could implicate him?","The people from the Wei Family weren’t fools. If Wei Qi had done something bad, they would have covered up his misdeeds already. They wouldn’t have let people find out about it!","“...”","Qiao Nian didn’t expect him to be so observant.. He managed to guess that she had something to implicate Wei Qi in her possession before she even told him about it."]},{"number":504,"title":"Chapter 504 - Sister Nian Had Already Found Someone to Pick Her Up","paragraphs":["Not denying it, she then explained briefly, “I asked someone to help me look into an interesting thing that I found.”","This was as good as admitting that she had something against Wei Qi in her possession.","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were very deep, and it was hard to decipher what he could be thinking about. His deep eyes were dark and beautiful.","“Can you send it to me so I can take a look?”","Qiao Nian didn’t think that it was such a big deal and agreed without much consideration. “Okay, I’ll send it to you later.”","Ye Wangchuan briefly acknowledged and changed his posture. “I’ll arrive in Rao City at one o’clock in the morning. Do you want me to send someone to pick you up first?”","He wanted to pick her up in person. However, the plane would arrive in Rao City very late. The nights in Rao City were very cold, and he didn’t want Qiao Nian to suffer in the police station.","The way he did things was always very direct. In recent years, as he matured, his temperament had mellowed a little and he had restrained his temper. However, his sense of oppression still remained.","If he were to pick her up personally, even if Wei Ling was given ten times the courage, she wouldn’t dare to hold Qiao Nian back from leaving.","However, Qiao Nian said, “You don’t have to rush back on my account. I have already found someone else to pick me up. He’s already on his way here.”","“As far as I know, Chairman Yuan is overseas on a business trip.” It wasn’t that Ye Wangchuan doubted her, but he was mainly worried that she chose to not tell him about her problems.","Qiao Nian was very stubborn sometimes. After interacting with her for such a long time, he knew that she was unwilling to trouble people unnecessarily. She was used to solving everything by herself. Even if she got hurt in the process, she wouldn’t want to bother other people.","Ye Wangchuan’s thin lips closed into a thin line. He couldn’t decide if Qiao Nian’s character was considered good or bad. Everyone had their own personality. He respected her strengths and weaknesses. He was hoping that she could lower her guard and put her trust in him a little bit more.","Qiao Nian didn’t expect him to be aware of Yuan Yongqin’s itinerary. Her eyebrows raised up in surprise, but she was not angry. She also didn’t realize that Ye Wangchuan’s behavior was actually an invasion of her privacy. She spoke calmly. “I didn’t look for Aunt Yuan. I called Old Master Su.","“If there are no problems, he should be here in an hour.”","Standing by the side, acting as though he was part of the background, Gu San’s lips twitched violently when he heard this.","When someone like Su Huaiyuan went to Beijing, even people from the top circles would treat him with great care and attention.","Why was Miss Qiao addressing him like he was her neighbor?","Ye Wangchuan didn’t expect her to ask Su Huaiyuan to pick her up. Furthermore, he didn’t expect him to agree to a high school student’s request.","Although he didn’t know the relationship between the two of them, he was completely relieved to hear that Su Huaiyuan was picking her up. He spoke briefly to Qiao Nian before hanging up the call.","...","In the car.","Gu San was waiting for him to end the call.","After holding in his words for such a long time, he was finally able to air his thoughts. He patted his chest and said in a panic, “Master Wang, what’s the relationship between Miss Qiao and Old Master Su? Old Master Su is even willing to pick her up. The weather is very cold. If two people have an ordinary relationship, they may not be willing to go out in this weather.”","However, the main point was that the person picking her up was Su Huaiyuan!","He was a very influential and powerful man. Unlike Master Nie, he held onto real authority. Many people wanted to get to know this man, and many others were also interested in talking to him.","Miss Qiao..."]},{"number":505,"title":"Chapter 505 - Miss Qiao Seemed Like She Wanted Wei Qi to Die","paragraphs":["Ye Wangchuan ignored him and waited for Qiao Nian to send him a message.","He then heard his cell phone ring.","Qiao Nian had messaged him sooner than he had expected.","She had sent him a document.","“Master Wang, is it Miss Qiao?” When he saw him looking at his cell phone, Gu San also leaned over. He then said, “She really has something against Young Master Wei? Impossible.”","He didn’t believe that Qiao Nian could get her hands on any important evidence against Wei Qi. He believed that she would only be able to collect information on trivial matters.","Who would have thought that he would be so surprised when he saw the message? His eyes suddenly widened and his mouth opened unconsciously. He couldn’t help but blurt out, “Oh my goodness. Master Wang, this is incredible.”","After taking a glance at the documents that Qiao Nian had sent them, he didn’t know what kind of expression to make. He was so surprised that he only managed to whisper. “I think that the Wei Family just wanted to bully Miss Qiao a little and make her cry. But it seems like Miss Qiao wants Wei Qi to die!”","The Wei Family just wanted to bully Qiao Nian a little. They just wanted to make her cry, but it seemed like Qiao Nian wanted Wei Qi to die. Ye Wangchuan finished reading the documents. His expression was calm and not as exaggerated as Gu San’s expression. However, he was equally shocked. He didn’t expect Qiao Nian to have such documents in her hands. These documents could make the Wei Family and Wei Qi overwrought. Furthermore, she had a whole folder of such documents.","He glanced at the folder’s size.","It was 1GB large.","Gu San was right. These documents were more than enough to end Wei Qi’s life. However...","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were very dark as he suddenly said, “What’s the Wei Family doing right now?”","Gu San was still thinking about the documents when he heard the question. He thought for a while and said, “They haven’t taken any action recently. Besides revoking Miss Qiao’s student status, there hasn’t been any news from them. I think it might be because Cai Gang is there, so they cannot take actions against Miss Qiao recklessly. Speaking of this, I remember something I need to tell you.”","“What is it?” Ye Wangchuan’s voice was low, sounding like the gurgling of water in clear spring. It sounded very good.","Gu San was almost distracted by his voice. He had to pinch his hand and palm before he came back to his senses. He then said, “I don’t know where the principal of Qing University heard the news from, but he now knows that Miss Qiao’s student status has been revoked. He’s going around looking for someone to restore Miss Qiao’s student status.”","Glancing at Ye Wangchuan’s reaction, he swallowed his saliva and continued, “However, because of the matter regarding Wei Qi, the Wei Family is adamant about revoking Miss Qiao’s student status. Both sides are now locked in a stalemate, and Miss Qiao is unable to transfer her student files over.”","In other words, Qiao Nian’s student status was still revoked.","Looking at the Wei Family’s actions, it seemed like they were not willing to let Miss Qiao off easily.","Ye Wangchuan clasped his hands on the seat. He narrowed his eyes slightly as he leaned back in the seat, looking as though he was taking a break.","Gu San didn’t know what he was thinking of and did not dare to disturb him. He calmed down and grew quiet.","After a while, Gu San heard him speak in a low voice. “Don’t worry about going to the airport for now and turn the car around.”","Ye Wangchuan raised his eyebrows slightly. His calm expression often caused people to misunderstand, thinking that he was a well-tempered man.","However, when you looked at his eyes carefully, you would be able to spot the pressure he exerted from its depths. Looking at the slightly red tails of his eyes, anyone would be able to tell that he wasn’t a person to be taken lightly.","Ye Wangchuan fiddled with the prayer beads on his wrist. It seemed like this would calm him down, but his narrowed eyes were cold and cruel. This made people feel frightened and oppressed.","“I’m going to pay a visit to the Wei Family.”"]},{"number":506,"title":"Chapter 506 - Even if He Wanted to Plead for Forgiveness, He Wasn’t Even Able to Meet","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, in the Wei Family.","Jiang Weishang sat in the reception hall. He had already drunk three cups of tea and was looking at the bottom of the fourth. No matter how good he was at containing his anger, he couldn’t help but close the corners of his mouth tightly in anger as he quietly put the teacup back on the table.","The Wei family servant was very discerning. Every time he was about to finish a cup of tea, the servant would immediately pour him a new cup. The servant would ensure that the guest would always have a cup of tea to drink.","They were using a type of tea called Yuqian Longjing. The tea leaves were put in boiling water. The green tea leaves floated and fell in the antique tea set, emitting bursts of aroma.","In the past, Old Master Jiang would have been very interested in drinking the tea calmly, slowly enjoying the taste of the Longjing tea. However, he felt as though a thousand ants were crawling all over his body. He was in no mood to enjoy the tea now. Seeing his cup being filled again, he couldn’t wait any longer and said, “Excuse me, is President Wei still busy?”","He had received a call from Jiang Li at nine o’clock in the evening, saying that Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi and was brought to the police station.","After receiving the call, he rushed over to the Wei Family’s house. It was already eleven o’clock, but Wei Ying had yet to come out to meet him.","After sixty years in this circle, it was obvious that the other party did not give them any face and always hung on to their every action.","However, it was their family’s fault this time. Even if they were to ignore him and not give him any face, all he could do was bear with it.","“About this...” The servant didn’t dare to speak recklessly. Embarrassed, he bowed his head and hesitated for a moment before explaining, “Old Master Jiang, I’m sure you’re also aware that the Old Master is ill. The eldest daughter is still taking care of him. I don’t know whether she’s free right now.”","It had already been two hours. Even if Wei Ying was still busy, knowing that guests were waiting for her, she could have come down in her spare time.","Wei Ying had put on airs for the whole two hours. She clearly didn’t want to meet him.","Old Master Jiang was noble his whole life. He put his teacup down again. He could no longer wait. He lifted his heavy eyebrows as he interrupted the servant. “Please help me ask President Wei how long she will take to finish her work and how much longer do I have to wait to see her!”","His back was straight, and his aura from when he was younger was still there.","The servant turned pale and did not dare to speak anymore. He hurriedly said, “I’ll go check right away.”","...","Half an hour later, he returned home.","The Jiang Family, including Jiang Zongnan, Tang Wanru, and Jiang Xianrou, were all there.","When Jiang Zongnan saw him return, he quickly stood up and looked anxious. “Dad, how did it go? Did you get to meet Wei Ying? What did the Wei Family say?”","Old Master Jiang had been running around the whole night. He was old and tired. He didn’t look well. He shook his head when he heard the question.","“Dad, why are you shaking your head? What do you mean by that?” Jiang Zongnan only saw him shake his head but did not hear any explanation. Stunned, he asked, “They don’t want to forgive Nian Nian?”","This result was just as he expected.","Wei Ying had given birth to her youngest son Wei Qi when she was almost thirty years old. She spoiled him badly, which caused the Young Master Wei to have such a character, so unafraid of anything.","He never expected any interaction between his family and the Wei Family. He didn’t expect to receive a call from Jiang Li saying that Qiao Nian had beat up Wei Qi!","She even broke three of his ribs, sending him to the hospital!","When he thought of this, he felt that it was so unimaginable that his eyebrows jumped in surprise. He couldn’t imagine something like this happening to his family.","He had contacts within the business district. If Qiao Nian had beaten up any other person, he could have found a way to help her out. However, the person she beat up was Wei Qi.","He really didn’t know how to help her."]},{"number":507,"title":"Chapter 507 - Not Being Able to Take the College Entrance Examination Is a Big Deal","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","They could only see if Old Master Jiang could think of a way to communicate privately with the Wei family. Would they let this matter go lightly on account of the two families?","Of course, they would definitely compensate when they needed to. They would also apologize when they needed to. As long as Wei Ying could let them off easily, any conditions could be negotiated!","He was just afraid that the Wei family wouldn’t give him face!","Old Master Jiang didn’t look well. If not for the fact that his body had become much stronger than before, he would have collapsed from anxiety tonight. At this moment, he was relying on his mental strength to support himself. When he heard this, he said with an ugly expression, “No. I didn’t see anyone.”","“You went out at nine. How could you...” Jiang Zongnan was halfway through his sentence when he saw his tired expression and swallowed his words. Anxious and angry, he said furiously, “What does the Wei family mean? Nian Nian hit someone, but I know her personality. She’s not the kind of person who would cause trouble for nothing. There must be a reason why she hit Wei Qi. He might not be innocent. You went personally to apologize, but they didn’t even want to meet you. What’s the meaning of this attitude?”","Old Master Jiang waved his hand, indicating that he should stop talking. He said unhappily, “No matter why she made a move, the Wei family only focuses on one thing—she hit someone! We have nothing to say. Moreover, Wei Qi is still lying in the hospital bed. There are both witnesses and material evidence. The Wei family has the confidence to pursue the matter, but we’re still standing our ground.”","Jiang Zongnan held his breath and felt a little helpless. His hands hung weakly by his sides as he looked at him. “Then, what should we do? We can’t just watch as Nian Nian is locked up in the police station...”","“Brother is still holding a seminar overseas and doesn’t know about this. If he finds out, this matter will probably blow up even more.”","He was referring to Qiao Nian’s father.","Jiang Zongjin had never given up on searching for his daughter all these years. When he finally found Qiao Nian, he couldn’t wait to give her the best things in the world.","If he knew about this, he would probably go all out to protect her.","Jiang Zongnan was his biological brother and had grown up together with him. Although he didn’t treat Qiao Nian as his biological daughter, he at least treated her as his biological niece. He took care of her from the bottom of his heart. Frowning, he said in discomfort, “... Before Big Brother comes back, we can’t just watch as his daughter is locked up.”","“One more thing.”","Jiang Zongnan didn’t know if he should say it or not, but with the situation being like this, he had to say it. He said in a deep voice to Old Master Jiang, “I just heard from Jiang Li that Nian Nian’s student status has been revoked by Wei Dongshan.”","“What?” Old Master Jiang’s reaction was huge. His expression changed immediately. “What happened?”","Jiang Zongnan said in a low voice, “I heard that the police station is delaying the case, and Wei Dongshan has found a way to cancel Nian Nian’s school records...”","Old Master Jiang’s eyebrows twitched violently as he said anxiously, “If she’s disqualified, she won’t be able to take the college entrance examination. She won’t be able to apply for university...”","Wasn’t it a joke that Qiao Nian had been expelled with her perfect grades?!","Tang Wanru was wearing a buttoned velvet dress today. The weather was getting colder, so she had a shawl over her shoulders, making her look elegant. When she heard this, her eyes flashed with disdain.","Qiao Nian’s grades weren’t good enough to get into university. Was there a difference if she was disqualified?"]},{"number":508,"title":"Chapter 508 - A Slap in the Face","paragraphs":["She pursed her lips and said indifferently, “After all, Qiao Nian hit someone. It’s understandable that they want to cancel her education. There’s nothing we can do...”","She was right, but she was too calm and did not seem to care.","Jiang Zongnan frowned and looked at her. “You don’t understand. Nian Nian can’t be disqualified. She...”","Jiang Xianrou was beside them as well. When she saw her grandfather and father getting anxious over Qiao Nian’s matter, she felt the same way as Tang Wanru. She even felt some disdain and contempt. When she heard this, she interrupted, “I don’t understand, either. Dad, why can’t she be disqualified?”","In her opinion, Qiao Nian was in the wrong this time. No matter the reason, Qiao Nian shouldn’t have been reckless and hurt someone.","Why couldn’t they sit down and have a good chat?","It was fine if she made a move, but now she was sent to the police station and still needed her family to worry about her. What a troublemaker!","“I don’t think her grades are good, either. I don’t know if she will be able to enter university in the future. Compared to her disqualification, I think it’s better to be worried about what the Wei family will do to let this go!”","Jiang Zongnan heard her say in a light tone, “Qiao Nian’s grades are not necessarily good. I wonder if she will be able to enter university in the future.” He felt an inexplicable sense of mockery. If someone else had said this to him, he might have sneered. However, the person who said this was his biological daughter. He couldn’t bring himself to laugh.","Looking at their indifferent attitudes, he knew that they had never taken Nian Nian seriously from the beginning. They even looked down on her from the bottom of their hearts...","Veins popped out on his forehead as he said anxiously, “Do you know that Nian Nian scored full marks for this year’s Qing University examination?!”","Both Tang Wanru and Jiang Xianrou were stunned by his words.","Jiang Xianrou’s heart skipped a beat as she instinctively held her mother’s arm tightly. Her eyelids twitched. “Dad, are you joking with me? This joke isn’t funny at all.”","She had been very confident in her grades since she was young. Not many people her age had better grades than her, let alone those outside.","From the bottom of her heart, she did not treat her newly found cousin as her competitor. How promising could a person from a small city be?","However, her heart had indeed skipped a beat earlier, and she became a little nervous.","“The Headmaster of Qing University told your grandfather personally. Do you think I’m joking with you?” Jiang Zongnan felt his head hurt even more when he saw her unconsciously showing contempt. Taking advantage of this opportunity, he decided to make his attitude clear. “Nian Nian has been admitted to the Qing University’s Traditional Chinese Medicine Department. This is already a done deal. When the college entrance examination ends and the files are released, Qing University will transfer her files in...”","Before the college entrance examination ended, no school was allowed to privately obtain student records. Therefore, it had been like this for a long time. Be it the students who were guaranteed admission or those who were admitted for the college entrance examination, they were all waiting for the college entrance examination to end before receiving their admission notices.","It was the same for the students participating in Qing University’s joint examination.","During this period, if the students could freely choose if they wanted to take the college entrance examination or not, they could choose to enroll in another school after the college entrance examination ended.","Of course, she would only be taking the college entrance examination and not filling in her application. In the end, she would still have to study at the school and major that she had been guaranteed."]},{"number":509,"title":"Chapter 509 - A New Test Result","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Jiang Zongnan said, “No other student scored full marks in Qing University’s joint examination. You’re already in your third year, so you should know very well how difficult the joint examination questions in your school are. Nian Nian was able to score full marks in such a difficult situation. Tell me, how shocking is her talent in studies? If she’s disqualified, Qing University won’t be able to recruit her! That’s why your grandfather and I are so anxious.”","Jiang Xianrou didn’t hear what he said after hearing that Qiao Nian scored full marks and was even admitted to the Traditional Chinese Medicine Faculty.","Although she didn’t understand why Qiao Nian didn’t get admitted to the Clinical Department but was chosen by the worst faculty in Qing University, she couldn’t accept it when her father told her in a serious tone that Qiao Nian had successfully entered Qing University!","“... If Nian Nian hadn’t encountered such a thing, we would have been anxious too if you had encountered such a thing today. That’s the same reason!” Jiang Zongnan said firmly.","Jiang Xianrou was in a daze and her heart was in a mess. She didn’t pay attention to what he was saying and could only listen to his words.","However, Tang Wanru heard him clearly. Furthermore, they had been married for many years. She immediately understood what her husband meant. Qiao Nian was also a part of the family. In his heart, he treated the two of them equally!","She couldn’t stand this. One was her biological daughter, and the other was a niece they had just found. How could they be the same?","However, in front of Old Master Jiang, she didn’t dare to argue with him directly. She could only suppress the discomfort in her heart and purse her lips. Her face was pale, and she was unwilling to speak.","However, she sneered in her heart. She wanted to watch the show!","So what if she got into Qing University? So what if she got full marks? Not to mention the Traditional Chinese Medicine Department, just the fact that Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi up this time meant that the Wei family wouldn’t let this matter rest. Old Master had personally gone to the Wei family to plead for leniency, but he had been rejected. She didn’t believe that there was still room for negotiation in this matter. Therefore, a rock was a rock. No matter how much she supported it, it was ultimately a useless thing!","Old Master Jiang didn’t care what the people in the family thought. His mind raced as he made up his mind. He planned to risk his face to beg for help.","“I’ll visit the Wei family again tomorrow. They’ll have to see me eventually.”","...","In the police station, Wei Ling had already gotten the latest injury report. She took the items and walked to Cai Gang, who was still there. She expressionlessly slapped the report in front of him and raised her chin slightly, indicating for him to take a look.","“Chief Cai, this is the new report on Wei Qi’s injuries that I got the provincial hospital to appraise. Take a look?”","When Cai Gang saw that she had come up with a new injury report, his heart skipped a beat. He picked up the leather bag in front of him and said quickly, “Isn’t there an injury report at the city hospital? Madam Shen, why did you get another...”","“Heh.” Wei Ling sneered and crossed her arms. Her fox fur coat made her face look more domineering, and the corners of her ears were sharp. She said calmly, “The results of just one hospital are not worth looking at. It’s better to find a few more hospitals to take a look at. Chief Cai, let’s see the results first!”","Cai Gang would read it even without her saying so.","He didn’t look at the densely packed projects and indicators. He couldn’t understand those things. He flipped straight to the last page.","The report was written in an exacerbated script: “Based on the patient’s disability results, we believe the patient is at level ten.”","These words looked light and weightless, but Cai Gang could feel the cold sweat on his back."]},{"number":510,"title":"Chapter 510 - Elder Su Came to Pick Her Up Personally","paragraphs":["He looked up.","Wei Ling looked at him with disdain and deliberately asked casually, “Chief Cai, Wei Qi was beaten up to a level 10 handicap. How do you think this matter should be judged?”","The level of disability referred to a person’s disability. It was determined by the severity of the disability. Generally, disability was divided into levels ranging from one to ten.","Level 10 disability sounded serious, but Level 1 was actually the most serious.","Level 10 was similar to light injuries.","Most of the time, the hospital could not determine if the injured belonged to a level 10 disability or light injuries. If the light injuries were serious, they could be written as a level 10 disability. If the level 10 disability was light, it could also be written as light injuries.","However, in the end, if Wei Qi was only slightly injured, then Qiao Nian wasn’t breaking the law. She only needed to compensate and apologize.","But if Wei Qi was disabled, it would be hard to say.","Wei Ling had grasped this point accurately, so she got someone to send Wei Qi to the provincial hospital and came up with a new injury report. Initially, she wanted the report to make his condition more serious, but she didn’t know how Qiao Nian did it. No matter what, the provincial hospital refused to write anything more serious. They told her that they could at most come up with a level 10 disability report, or it would be a light injury...","Coming back to her senses, she stopped thinking about it and said in a deep voice, “Previously, you said that you guys didn’t investigate clearly and couldn’t close the case rashly. Now that the injury analysis has been done, Wei Qi has been beaten until he’s disabled. As for me, I don’t like to make things difficult for others. I want an explanation right now. Tell me, can you close the case and seek justice for my brother?”","“This...”","The case definitely couldn’t be closed. Closing the case was equivalent to admitting that Qiao Nian had intentionally hurt someone.","Being pressured by her, Cai Gang really didn’t know how to find an excuse to absolve Qiao Nian, but he definitely had to think of a way to protect her. He said in a low voice, “The test results from the city hospital said that it was a light injury, but Madam Shen’s test results showed that it’s a level 10 disability. I don’t know which hospital’s results are accurate...”","“It seems like Chief Cai won’t shed a tear until he sees the coffin.” Wei Ling snorted coldly. “Don’t beat around the bush. I’m not that easy to deceive. According to your rules, the results will definitely be based on the higher-ranking hospital. If the provincial hospital says that Wei Qi is disabled, then he is. If you don’t even know how to handle such a simple case, I can only get someone who knows how to handle it!”","She wanted to transfer Qiao Nian away.","“No!” Cai Gang objected without hesitation.","Wei Ling had given him enough face. Seeing that he was being stubborn and still wanted to shield Qiao Nian, she didn’t want to waste time with him. She was about to tell Wei Dongshan to find someone to replace Cai Gang when Wei Dongshan hurried in with an ugly expression.","“What’s wrong?”","Wei Dongshan walked quickly to her, his face turning green. He first looked at Cai Gang, then looked at her. A little dispirited, he said, “Elder Su is here. His car is outside. He wants to take Qiao Nian away...”","He had really seen a ghost today. With Elder Su’s status, why would he especially come over for an ordinary high school student? Furthermore, when he spoke to him, his attitude was very firm, and there was no room for negotiation. Even when he suggested that Qiao Nian had injured Wei Qi, the other party did not care at all. He wasn’t afraid of becoming enemies with the Wei family at all. It was that kind of attitude. He wanted her!","Wei Ling frowned. “Which Elder Su?”","“Su Huaiyuan.”","Wei Ling was stunned.","Wei Dongshan looked at her in frustration with an obscure gaze. “Isn’t she just an ordinary high school girl? How does she know Elder Su?”"]},{"number":511,"title":"Chapter 511 - It Couldnt Be That She Knew Elder Su By Herself","paragraphs":["Wei Ling was flustered. She didn’t understand why Su Huaiyuan would interfere in this matter either, but Cai Gang was still here. Not wanting to weakness in front of him, she pinched her palms and pursed her lips. Her expression was bad as she said, “Perhaps it’s because of the Jiang family...”","Even she didn’t believe her own words.","Su Huaiyuan wasn’t an ordinary person. The Jiang family didn’t have the right to order him around.","If she didn’t believe it herself, how could Wei Dongshan believe it?","“Why haven’t we heard of any dealings between the Jiang family and Elder Su before?”","Wei Ling forced herself to stay awake and said weakly, “The circle is only that big. As long as you’re willing to find someone, you can always build some connections. Elder Jiang was famous for being sociable when he was young. It’s not strange that he found someone on this level.”","“I think Elder Su’s attitude...”","Wei Ling interrupted him and said firmly, “It can’t be that she knows Elder Su herself. I don’t believe it. That’s too incredulous!”","“...” Wei Dongshan didn’t say anything else. He pursed his lips and stood there, looking rather unhappy.","His intuition told him that Su Huaiyuan knew Qiao Nian, not because of anyone, but because he had come here specifically for her.","At this thought, he felt frustrated again. He regretted his rash intervention in this matter.","...","Su Huaiyuan’s car was parked outside the police station. Since he didn’t come in himself, he got the chauffeur to help him bail Qiao Nian out.","After a while, Qiao Nian came out of the police station.","She didn’t bring anything with her except a hoodie. Her clothes were messy, and some places were stained with blood. They draped loosely over her body and did not look proper.","Fortunately, her temperament did not belong to the obedient type.","Her bandit aura seemed to have become stronger.","The driver kept peeking at her throughout the journey as if he wanted to see through her.","He had no choice. He had never seen Elder Su so concerned about anyone before. In order to bail out this Miss Qiao, Elder Su had taken a two-hour car ride back from the neighboring city. He had even postponed the meeting the next day. This wasn’t something that could be done with ordinary connections. He just didn’t know what relationship this Miss Qiao had with Elder Su. Anyway, he had never heard of Elder Su having such a big granddaughter...","Soon, the Su family’s chauffeur led her to the front of the car. Even though he was skeptical, he still said respectfully, “Miss Qiao, please get in first.”","...","Su Huaiyuan was also in the car. The backseat of the extended Mercedes-Benz was very spacious, enough for two people to sit in.","The moment Qiao Nian got into the car, Su Huaiyuan quickly sized her up and asked in concern, “Nian Nian, are you okay?”","Qiao Nian hadn’t rested well the entire day. She had examinations, taken a plane, and had been locked in the interrogation room for a few hours. Now, she looked exhausted.","Her eyes were filled with redness, and one could vaguely see traces of blood. She held the brim of her hoodie and relaxed her tense back as she leaned back. After stretching her body slightly, she shook her head and pursed her lips. “I’m okay. Chief Cai is here. They didn’t make things difficult for me.”","Su Huaiyuan was worried that someone with poor judgment would make things difficult for her. When he heard that she was fine, he felt relieved and revealed a relaxed expression. “It’s good that you’re fine. I was worried about you on the way here. I wanted to ask you about it, but I was afraid that it would be inconvenient for you to answer the phone. Fortunately, you’re fine.”","Driving in front, when the Su family’s chauffeur heard this, he stole a glance through the rearview mirror.","Wasn’t that right? Elder Su had been urging him to drive faster the entire journey. He looked like he wanted to grow wings and fly over.","Qiao Nian could hear the concern in his voice. Her eyes warmed and her anger dissipated by more than half. Supporting her forehead, she said guiltily, “I’m sorry for making you worry. I...”"]},{"number":512,"title":"Chapter 512 - When You Think That You’re on the Fifth Floor, Sister Nian Is in the","paragraphs":["“Why are you talking about giving favors? Didn’t I say before that we shouldn’t be so calculative about these things? If you’re so calculative, you’ll make us feel distant from each other.”","Su Huaiyuan knew she didn’t like to owe people anything, especially favors. However, she didn’t care much if people owed her something.","“You better not give me any more pills. I haven’t finished the pills you gave me in the past. I’ll let you know when I finish them.”","Qiao Nian was a little helpless. She hadn’t said that she was compensating him with pills, but she did have this thought before!","Seeming to know what she was thinking, Su Huaiyuan smiled. “You haven’t said anything, but I guessed your thoughts.”","He paused and added, “I didn’t do much. Even if you give me more pills, I will feel bad about accepting such a valuable gift from you. If you really want to thank me, you can treat me to a meal at Waterside Loft in the future.”","He said half-jokingly, “It’s not easy to reserve a table there without you since you’re the boss. I’ve not eaten there for a long time, and I miss the chef’s cooking.”","The Su family chauffeur was driving and listening to the gossip attentively. He was mainly curious about their relationship. Hearing this, his foot shook and he almost stepped on the accelerator. Luckily, he composed himself quickly and didn’t make such a big mistake!","When he recovered from his shock, he looked at Qiao Nian through the rearview mirror with a complicated expression!","How old was this girl?","She was at most 18 or 19 years old, and she was still studying.","He just followed Old Master Su’s orders to pick someone up. He thought that the person was a lazy second-generation aristocrat that didn’t study properly and liked causing trouble outside.","He was a little confused now.","The Su family was located in the neighboring city. However, he drove Su Huaiyuan all year round and often followed him around, so how could he not know about Waterside Loft?","Waterside Loft was a private restaurant that specialized in Cantonese cuisine. It was famous for its delicious food and elegant environment. It was hard to get a reservation there.","It was famous even in the neighboring city.","Many people would drive to Rao City to have a meal there. This was how famous Waterside Loft was in the area.","It was said that the boss of Waterside Loft had a very good relationship with the Cheng Feng Corporation. He initially thought that he was a middle-aged man in his forties. He didn’t expect that... The boss behind the famous Waterside Loft was a high school student who just turned 18 years old!","Sure enough, this world was unbelievable.","You think that you’re on the fifth floor, but someone else is already in the atmosphere. You won’t ever reach her level no matter how high you jump!","Qiao Nian didn’t notice the driver’s reaction. The air condition in the car was very strong. A little uncomfortable, after seeking Su Huaiyuan’s advice, she opened one-third of the window to let some fresh air in.","With the fresh air flowing in, she felt a little drowsy and nodded without thinking much. “Sure, just tell me when you want to go.”","“It’s a deal, then.”","Su Huaiyuan was elated. Suddenly, he thought of something. “By the way, why did you beat Wei Qi?”","He received a text message from Qiao Nian and immediately asked someone to check what had happened.","After some investigation, he received a huge scare.","Qiao Nian actually beat Wei Qi up!","This was not a small matter.","Wei Ying was well known for fighting with someone over minor details. Wei Qi was her youngest son, whom she gave birth to when she was over 30 years old. Since she gave birth to a son at an old age, he was extremely precious to her.","Now that Qiao Nian had beaten him up, the Wei family wouldn’t let it go lightly."]},{"number":513,"title":"Chapter 513 - Ridiculous","paragraphs":["Worried, he muttered, “How are you going to resolve this matter?”","Qiao Nian hadn’t rested well, so her eyes were dry and uncomfortable. She simply opened the window a little more and let in a cold gust of wind. Hearing his question, she casually replied, “I’ll wait and see.”","Wait and see?","What was good about that?","Seeing that she looked rather indifferent, Su Huaiyuan became anxious. Pursing his lips, he asked solemnly, “How about I help out?”","The night air was cold and windy. Qiao Nian started to have a headache after being exposed to the wind and closed the window. Feeling a headache, she leaned on the back of the chair, lowered her head, and massaged her temples. Her tone was a little irritable as she replied. “I didn’t mean that.”","“Huh?” Su Huaiyuan didn’t understand her.","He said worriedly, “It doesn’t look like the Wei Family will treat you kindly. They will definitely demand an explanation from you. Sigh, you aren’t clear about the situation in Beijing.","“This Wei Qi is Wei Ying’s youngest son and is usually spoiled. If you hit him, even if he doesn’t give you trouble, I’m afraid that the Wei Family won’t let it go so easily. It isn’t good to provoke them...”","It wasn’t good to provoke the Wei Family.","Wei Ying was famous for being difficult to deal with.","Not only did she have a bad temper, but she was also extremely calculative.","Anyone who understood the families in Beijing did not want to provoke her. Wei Ying had almost no empathy, and she wouldn’t let anyone go easily, even if the person was young and insensible.","Su Huaiyuan truly cared about Qiao Nian. After thinking about it, he said, “I’ll go to Beijing tomorrow.”","“No need.”","Qiao Nian looked up with her black and wild eyes and patiently explained to him, “What I mean is to wait and see their attitudes before reacting. I’m not afraid that they’ll cause trouble for me.”","Su Huaiyuan was silent for a second, thinking that he heard wrongly. He looked at Qiao Nian’s expression carefully. The girl wearing a hoodie had an indifferent expression, and it didn’t seem like she was joking.","He was at a loss for words and didn’t know how to react.","He couldn’t help but feel that her expression wasn’t quite right.","That was the Wei Family!","The younger generation members, Wei Dongshan and Wei Ling, didn’t dare to be presumptuous in front of him, but he had to be careful around Wei Ying, not to mention Old Master Wei who was still alive!","The Wei Family was wealthy and powerful. It wasn’t an exaggeration to call them a noble family. Now that Nian Nian had hit Wei Qi, not only was she unafraid, but she even wanted for him to apologize...","This was ridiculous!","Su Huaiyuan didn’t know what to say and was quiet for some time.","Just as Qiao Nian was about to explain that she had something on Wei Qi, her phone rang.","Taking it out in annoyance, she saw that it was an unfamiliar number.","Not in a good mood, she didn’t want to answer a random call. Thus, she quickly rejected it and put her phone aside.","She didn’t rest well and only wanted to sleep today. She would deal with this matter tomorrow.","Suddenly, her phone rang again.","Qiao Nian was irritated.","Su Huaiyuan noticed that her phone was ringing non-stop and asked curiously, “Who is it? The person has been calling you non-stop.”","Qiao Nian glanced at it. It was another unfamiliar number.","She picked up her phone in annoyance and said casually, “I don’t know. It’s an unfamiliar number.”","Su Huaiyuan knew that there were many spam calls these days. His phone number had restrictions, but he occasionally received harassing calls, not to mention ordinary phone numbers."]},{"number":514,"title":"Chapter 514 - Maybe the Pressure to Perform Is Too High","paragraphs":["Hearing that, he couldn’t help but laugh. “The advertisers are so dedicated this year. They’re still trying to perform well at night.”","Qiao Nian saw that the number’s area code wasn’t a local Rao City number. Her eyes were dark and her lips were pursed. In annoyance, she casually said, “Maybe you’re right. The pressure to perform is too high.”","...","“Master Wang, Miss Qiao isn’t answering your call?” In a red Buick, Gu San turned around to look at the man sitting in the back seat.","Ye Wangchuan didn’t know that he was reduced to an advertiser who was pressured to perform by two people. At this moment, he pursed his lips, slowly put down the phone, and said nothing as he glanced at the call which was hung up ruthlessly.","However, Gu San gloated. “It’s too bad that your mobile phone is dead and you have to lose mine. Miss Qiao doesn’t have my Beijing phone number. Maybe she thinks that it’s a harassing call.”","However, it felt good to see Master Wang’s call being rejected!","He only dared to think about it. Once Ye Wangchuan looked over, he immediately hid his gloating expression and said sincerely, “Master Wang, how about you try calling Miss Qiao a few more times? Perhaps she might pick it up.”","Of course, there was a possibility that Qiao Nian wouldn’t answer the call and even blacklist the number in annoyance.","Ye Wangchuan obviously thought of that possibility. He squinted his eyes and returned the phone to him. “Forget it. It’s so late. Maybe she wants to rest. I’ll call her tomorrow.”","Gu San quietly took the phone back and wanted to say that it wouldn’t hurt to give Miss Qiao another call if he cared so much about her.","However, he swallowed his words and said instead, “Besides, Cai Gang just said that Miss Qiao left with Old Master Su. With him around, you don’t have to worry about Miss Qiao’s safety. However, what are you planning to do about this matter involving the Wei Family?”","They had already arrived outside the Wei Residence and just had to go in.","Before Master Wang received the documents from Miss Qiao, he felt that this matter was not easy to handle. If Miss Qiao wasn’t there, the Wei Family might not be willing to settle the issue.","However, with Master Wang present, the Wei Family would at least give him face. But this method would lead to some grievances.","He had followed Ye Wangchuan for so many years and had never seen him lower himself before. Although he was doing it for Miss Qiao as there was no way out, he was still a little unwilling.","Now, he had completely changed his mindset.","Miss Qiao had something that could implicate Wei Qi, and using it would put the Wei Family in an uncomfortable situation.","The situation had completely reversed. At this moment, it wasn’t the Wei Family that could decide what to do with Miss Qiao, but what they could do to avoid the negative situation.","If Master Wang wanted Wei Qi to die today, the Wei Family could only gnash their teeth and hold in their anger.","Gu San was quite excited at the moment. He wished that they could go in quickly and look at the expression of that Eldest Daughter of the Wei Family who was so difficult to deal with.","Ye Wangchuan wanted to ask Qiao Nian for her opinion, but the call couldn’t get through. His eyes were deep as he curled his fingers around his knees. He seemed to be thinking about this matter as he squinted his eyes.","“Let’s show it to them first. As for where it will end up, it depends on their attitudes.”","He remembered that Wei Dongshan also used his power to expel Qiao Nian. He heard that Wei Ying didn’t even turn up to meet Old Master Jiang, who had come to plead on Qiao Nian’s behalf, for two hours and was extremely arrogant.","The Wei Family was always ruthless in their ways. Thus, he wanted to see their faces when they admitted defeat."]},{"number":515,"title":"Chapter 515 - The Situation Has Reversed and They’re Making the Demands Now","paragraphs":["At the Shen Residence.","Qiao Chen had just finished practicing the piano upstairs and was enjoying coffee in the living room. Ever since she heard that Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi up, her mood had changed from cloudy to sunny. She even had a better time practicing the piano and did not feel the irritability and anxiety of the previous few days.","As she was about to taste the new flavor of her brewed coffee, she heard the sound of a car parking outside.","“Uncle is back?” Qiao Chen excitedly put the cup down, reacting faster than the servants. She immediately got up from the sofa, walked to the door, and greeted the person entering.","A servant also took out a pair of clean slippers from the shoe cabinet.","Shen Jingyan had hurried back from the Wei Family’s house. There was an ominous air around him, and he didn’t look good.","As soon as he entered the house, he handed his bag to a servant, put on his slippers, and didn’t even glance at Qiao Chen as he hurriedly instructed the servants. “Help me pack two changes of clothes. I’m going to Rao City!”","“Yes, sir.”","The servants hurriedly took his bag and carried out his instructions.","Guessing what was going on, Qiao Chen asked carefully, “Uncle, why are you going back to Rao City all of a sudden? Did something happen?”","She knew that the main issue in Rao City now was that Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi up!","She was in a good mood all night because of this. She was waiting to see the drama and couldn’t wait for Shen Jingyan to come home.","“Yes.”","She shouldn’t have mentioned this, because once she did, Shen Jingyan’s temples were about to explode. He tore off his necktie and threw it on the sofa. Resisting the anger building in his chest, he said in annoyance, “I have to deal with something there.”","Qiao Chen understood that he was referring to Qiao Nian’s incident. Suddenly, the corners of her mouth rose subconsciously. Her eyes flashed, and she immediately asked, “Uncle, can I accompany you?”","“I have to deal with an urgent matter. Why do you want to follow me back to Rao City?” Shen Jingyan was extremely annoyed at the moment. He glanced at her impatiently, obviously in a bad mood.","Well, it would be strange if he were in a good mood!","Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi up. This was a rather serious matter. He had heard about it from his mother-in-law in the afternoon and didn’t think much of it initially.","After all, he had already chosen Qiao Chen. Qiao Nian’s mess was probably not related to him.","However, in a short span of one hour, the situation changed!","Young Master Ye actually visited the Wei Residence in person and showed his mother-in-law something. After she saw it, she was terrified and even seemed to have aged a few years.","After she sent Young Master Ye away, she immediately wanted him to mediate the situation by visiting Rao City and think of ways to placate Qiao Nian. Otherwise, Wei Qi might not make it past this difficult situation!","Wei Qi was spoiled by the Wei Family since he was a child. As long as it wasn’t a heaven-shattering event, his mother-in-law would never say something like that because she doted on him so much.","However...","Even though Qiao Nian was the one who hit Wei Qi and he was still lying in the hospital, his mother-in-law suddenly changed her tune.","Shen Jingyan didn’t understand why, and he was restless as he tried to figure out the reason.","However, Qiao Chen misinterpreted his anxious expression. She thought that he was annoyed because Qiao Nian had caused trouble. The corners of her lips rose subconsciously, and she seemed exhilarated.","She knew how to conceal herself. Thus, even though Shen Jingyan was upset and spoke to her aggressively, she could still act sensibly.","“My mom wants me to go back for a while. She said she wants to host a banquet for me to celebrate my entrance to Qing University...”"]},{"number":516,"title":"Chapter 516 - In Sister Nian’s Eyes, His Phone Call Would Only Be Regarded as Unimportant","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","She subtly brought up that she was admitted to Qing University.","Sure enough, Shen Jingyan’s troubled expression eased, and his sharp and thin eyes were much gentler than before. Pursing his lips and suppressing the anxiety in his heart, he managed to say, “Look at me, I almost forgot about this.”","Qiao Chen immediately went with the flow and said softly, “It’s OK, I know that Uncle is busy. Besides, you already called to congratulate me.”","Shen Jingyan’s expression had eased a lot, and he seemed to be satisfied with her sensible behavior. Thinking about it, he said, “Alright, you should celebrate after getting into university. You’ve not been there for more than a month, it’s reasonable that your mother misses you.","“Ok, you can come with me. Pack your luggage. We’ll leave in half an hour.”","“Is it that urgent?”","“If you think it’s too rushed, you can leave tomorrow. But we won’t be going together. You can decide.”","At this time, no flights from Beijing to Rao City were available. Since Shen Jingyan was in a hurry, he had to think of other ways to get there.","He would fly to the next city first and get on another plane to Rao City. This was the fastest way to get to Rao City, but a lot of time would be wasted during the transfer, and he would feel fatigued as a flight passenger.","However, he couldn’t care much about this and only wanted to go back to the city and clean up this mess.","After talking to Qiao Chen, he was no longer thinking about her and didn’t praise her as he did in the call.","He was obviously in low spirits. After their conversation ended, he went to a corner and took out his cell phone to call someone.","...","After Shen Jingyan made seven or eight phone calls in a row, he turned off his phone.","On the other side, in a villa in Rao City.","Qiao Nian didn’t return until midnight. She immediately went upstairs and fell asleep without saying anything to Jiang Li and the others.","She was so tired that she turned off her phone to avoid being awoken.","She slept soundly. Everyone knew that this week was rough on her and tried their best not to disturb her. When Qiao Nian woke up, the sun had already risen to the middle of the sky.","It rained for several days in a row in Rao City, and it was finally sunny today. The skies were clear, and the temperature was warm, making people sleepy.","Qiao Nian sat up on the bed and realized that the consequence of sleeping for too long after insufficient sleep was a greater headache.","However, she had already woken up and couldn’t possibly go back to sleep. She combed her hair irritably, forced herself to get up from the bed, and took a cold shower before she finally felt awake. The annoyance in her eyes grew stronger.","In the room.","Su Huaiyuan retrieved her black shoulder bag for her; she was too sleepy last night and left it on her desk.","At this moment, Qiao Nian took out a black T-shirt from the closet and put it on. Then, she walked to the desk and turned on her phone.","The phone hadn’t been charged for a day and did not have any battery left.","She plugged the phone into the charging cable and glanced at it casually.","Generally, phones tended to freeze when they were turned on. Phones with less RAM power would take more than a minute to turn on. Qiao Nian’s phone looked old and plain, but it only needed two to three seconds to turn on.","Immediately afterward, countless notifications were received.","There were also many missed calls.","Qiao Nian had a headache after waking up. She lowered her head in annoyance and filtered through the messages on her phone.","After ignoring the unimportant notifications, such as a missed call from Uncle Shen, she noticed an important update.","Chen Yuan had called her, and there was an unread message!"]},{"number":517,"title":"Chapter 517 - Ye Wangchuan Again","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Qiao Nian looked down and opened the message.","It was sent at 3:00 AM.","There was only one sentence.","[Sister Nian, I’m home.]","Surprised, Qiao Nian raised her eyebrows.","She hadn’t given the Wei Family an ultimatum, so there was no way Chen Yuan would be released from the police station for the time being.","She only asked Cai Gang to take care of him and look for a doctor to treat his injuries.","As for Chen Yuan’s bail...","She had planned to talk to somebody today and didn’t expect Chen Yuan to be released on bail last night.","Qiao Nian squinted her eyes and tried to figure out who had released him from the police station.","She could think of no other person with this ability except Ye Wangchuan.","In addition, she had only told him about the incident with Wei Qi last night. Besides him, Qiao Nian couldn’t think of anyone else.","Of course, she hoped that Chen Yuan could be bailed as soon as possible. After all, the sooner his injuries could be treated, the lower the chances that they would cause problems for him in the future.","It was similar to infection and inflammation.","There were still three months before the college entrance examination. Every day was extremely important for senior high school students. She believed that Chen Yuan didn’t want to delay his studying schedule.","Qiao Nian held her phone with her slender fair hand, leaned against the table, and curled her long legs. Pursing her lips, she did not reply to him. Instead, she unplugged the phone from the charger and gave him a call.","Chen Yuan answered within seconds.","“Hey, Sister Nian.”","After hearing his energetic voice, she knew that he was fine and was a little relieved. She asked, “I was asleep yesterday and didn’t see your message. Where are you now?”","“The hospital.” Chen Yuan didn’t wait for her to finish by saying, “I guessed that you were asleep. I called you later, but seeing that your phone was off, I didn’t disturb you further. I initially wanted to tell you that I’m out and you don’t have to worry about me.”","He paused before continuing, “The person you asked to pick me up took me to the hospital to bandage my wounds. The doctor has taken care of all my injuries. There are no major issues, and I’ll be better in two days.”","He was ready to enter the detention center and thought that he might not be able to take the college entrance examination. When he was at his lowest point, someone suddenly came in and told him that someone had come to bail him out.","He didn’t know who that person was, but he mentioned Qiao Nian’s name and comforted him along the way to the hospital. He even revealed that there was a large chance that the confession he was forced to sign would become invalid and that he shouldn’t worry...","He didn’t really care about the confession, but he was worried about his parents’ condition after he was locked up. Now that he was able to leave smoothly, he was very grateful to Qiao Nian.","“Thank you, Sister Nian.”","Qiao Nian didn’t even know that he had been taken to the hospital to treat his injuries and found it irritable that she probably owed someone a favor again.","Irritated by the many nuisances, she felt a headache coming. “It wasn’t me who bailed you out...”","The person on the other end understood her and said with a chuckle, “Even if it wasn’t you, others were willing to help me because of you. It’s no different than you bailing me out.”","Knowing what she was going to ask, he said, “Sister, don’t worry about my family. I went to Nanyuan Hospital to look for them after I had my own injuries checked. They know that I’m OK, so don’t worry about it. In fact, my mother scolded me for involving you in this matter. She refused to talk to me last night and was only willing to talk to me just now.. She wants to treat you to a meal.”"]},{"number":518,"title":"Chapter 518 - Wanting to Invite Many People","paragraphs":["“Tell Aunt Chen I said goodbye.” She looked down with a wild expression before changing her mind. “Forget it, I’ll treat you another day to thank the person who helped you.”","Chen Yuan had already guessed who helped him. As a man, he was actually quite uncomfortable and felt a little awkward.","But after this time, he thoroughly saw the gap between him and Qiao Nian. Not only did he lack experience, but he also lacked in many other areas. Perhaps only that Master Wang was suitable to stay by Sister Nian’s side.","After he let out a foul breath, he insisted. “No need, Sister Nian. I’ll treat him. I saved some money and put it in the bank before I dropped out of school before. There’s not much, but a meal should be fine. Besides, he helped me. I can’t possibly ask you to help me treat him to a meal. It’s not good...”","Qiao Nian knew him. He was stubborn like a cow, but he had strong self-esteem. She didn’t force Chen Yuan and only agreed after thinking for a moment. “Sure. But I’ll choose the place, so you don’t have to worry about this.”","She had known Ye Wangchuan for a long time and probably understood his taste. He liked sweet things and preferred Zhejiang cuisine. He also couldn’t eat spicy food.","The food at Waterside Loft was good but expensive.","Considering Aunt Chen and Chen Yuan’s personalities, they wouldn’t let her pay the bill no matter what. It’d also be too obvious if she gave them a discount at the cashier.","Qiao Nian intended to find a place nearby that served good food at a reasonable price. She also wanted to invite Ye Wangchuan, Gu San, and Old Master Su as they helped her. She considered inviting Cai Gang as he put in a lot of effort as well... She counted with her fingers, and it seemed that she wanted to invite many guests.","Since she wanted to invite Ye Wangchuan and Gu San for a meal, she couldn’t leave out the little guy and Jiang Li. Otherwise, considering their tempers, they would become difficult and sulky...","Qiao Nian leaned on the edge of the table in an irritable mood.","Aunt Yuan also helped to check Chen Yuan’s location. If she came back from overseas, she would have to call her, and this would increase her guest list.","“We’ll talk about it next time. I’ll let you know when I’m sure of the date.” Qiao Nian frowned. Her eyes were as dark as ink and her voice was hoarse as if she just woke up. She lowered her eyes, and her long eyelashes slightly curled up. A faint shadow was cast under her eyelids. “Take care of Aunt Chen and make sure they don’t worry. I’ll definitely get an explanation from those who framed you.”","She couldn’t let Wei Qi’s matter affect Chen Yuan’s entrance examination!","He was definitely going to take the college entrance examination!","Chen Yuan didn’t care about that and only said, “Whatever happens to me isn’t important. It’s fine as long as you aren’t dragged down, Sister Nian. Otherwise, my mom will beat me to death.”","He was serious. If he implicated Qiao Nian, his mom might really disown him!","Qiao Nian knew Aunt Chen’s character and said faintly, “I know. I’m hanging up.”","After that, she hung up. She looked at the remaining battery. There was only 50% left. It was barely enough.","Qiao Nian thought about many things. Deciding not to charge her phone anymore, she took it, opened the door, and walked out of her room.","Jiang Li had made a lot of money in the entertainment industry over the years. As one of the popular stars, he had many activities every day and earned endorsement fees from more than a dozen brands. He earned a large sum just from these alone.","Thus, his investment in real estate was substantial. His single-story villa in Rao City was at least 300 square meters, divided into two floors, and had a parking lot underground. It was definitely a luxury home."]},{"number":519,"title":"Chapter 519 - Sister Nian Is Master Wangs Wife","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian’s room was on the second floor.","She only remembered that she forgot something when she went downstairs. Thus, she went back to her room to retrieve her things before going down again.","Downstairs.","Jiang Li had been pacing around for a long time and couldn’t hold it in anymore. Looking at the man who came back in the middle of last night, he asked anxiously, “Master Wang, why isn’t Nian Nian up yet? It’s already noon. Should I go up to check on her?”","Ye Wangchuan looked as if he didn’t sleep all night. His eyes were bloodshot and dark as he leaned on the sofa with his legs propped up while reading a magazine. He looked calm as usual and only squinted lazily when he heard him. Without looking up, he said, “She didn’t rest well this week. Let her sleep longer.”","Gu San made two cups of coffee and put one in front of the lazy man. He took a sip, yawned, and said sleepily to Jiang Li, who was walking back and forth, “Yes, Young Master Jiang. Don’t keep moving around, you’re making me dizzy.”","“Miss Qiao didn’t rest well this week because she was preparing for the exam and other activities. She stayed up late last night as well. It’s normal for her to sleep more in the morning, so don’t worry.”","Jiang Li glanced at him and said angrily, “Nonsense. She’s not your sister, so of course, you’re not worried. Since she’s my biological cousin, of course, I’m worried about her.”","The corner of Gu San’s mouth twitched. He glanced at the man sitting comfortably on the sofa and almost said something back on impulse.","Miss Qiao was Master Wang’s wife, and even he was calm. Why was he worrying as her cousin?","But when the words came to his lips, he was still sensible and knew that Jiang Li was very defensive when it came to Qiao Nian. He swallowed back his words and said, “I’m concerned about Miss Qiao even though she’s not my cousin. However, she only slept in. Young Master Jiang, your reaction might be too exaggerated since you don’t allow her to sleep in...”","Jiang Li wanted to say it was just a mere matter of sleeping in. Last night when Qiao Nian came back, she immediately went to sleep. He didn’t even have the time to ask her how to solve Wei Qi’s matter and the Wei Family’s attitude towards her. He didn’t sleep last night and could only wait for Qiao Nian to wake up to ask her about it. However, Qiao Nian hadn’t gotten up yet, and it was almost noon...","Jiang Li started to wonder if he should go up and knock on her door again. Looking up, he saw a thin figure appearing upstairs from the corner of his eye.","His eyes lit up.","He didn’t manage to call her when someone beat him to the punch and yelled loudly, “Sister, you’re awake!”","Jiang Li was just about to call Nian Nian and almost choked on his saliva.","He cursed silently in his heart. Damn it!","They were all trying to compete with him! It was so unfair!","...","Qiao Nian had just woken up and felt a little drowsy because she slept for too long. The back of her head was still a little sore.","Holding something in her hand, she slowly walked down. Hearing someone call her, she looked down.","When she saw the little guy jumping on the side of the sofa, she narrowed her eyes. The expression on her beautiful and delicate face softened and she walked straight to him. After that, she handed the game software to him.","“A gift.”","Her voice was wild and lazy.","So handsome!","“You bought a gift for me?”","Ye Qichen looked at the seven or eight games in his arms and immediately recognized the shooting game cover.","His snow-white face was flushed with excitement, and he didn’t hide his happiness. He almost jumped in joy. He stared at it before looking at Qiao Nian again in glee and saying excitedly, “Thank you, Sister!”"]},{"number":520,"title":"Chapter 520 - Being Handsome Is About Looks but a Type of Temperament!","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian replied lazily, walked over to pull out a chair, and sat down resolutely. Then, she poured herself a cup of water and slurped it.","After drinking the cold water, she felt her head clear up, but a trace of sleepiness could still be seen in her eyes.","Gu San greeted her warmly. “Miss Qiao, you’re awake?”","“Yeah.” Qiao Nian put down the cup and rubbed her swollen head. The back of her head was still tense, and it slightly hurt.","Jiang Li was thinking about how Ye Qichen got a gift but he didn’t receive anything. He completely forgot to ask her about Wei Qi and how she came back yesterday.","Instead, Ye Wangchuan put his book down, got up, and said to her, “What do you want to eat for lunch?”","“Lunch?”","Qiao Nian blinked. She was still hazy after waking up and didn’t react for a while.","Her legs were dangling, her elbows were on the table, and she rested her chin lazily on the back of the chair. She squinted like a wolf that just woke up and looked lazy.","“I’m fine with anything.”","The most difficult meal to satisfy was “anything.” Ye Wangchuan was also too lazy in the past, and he would always say anything casually when others asked him what he wanted to eat. Now that someone was telling him the same, he finally understood how others felt.","He felt like this was karma and wanted to laugh inexplicably. However, he was in a good mood. He had only slept on the plane for three hours in the last two days. Gu San was so sleepy that his eyelids were fighting to stay up, but he looked spirited and didn’t seem to be affected by anything. He laughed and said, “Anything? That’s too difficult. If I made something like sugar tomatoes, you wouldn’t eat them.”","Qiao Nian thought about it and immediately frowned. It was sweet and greasy.","Fortunately, Ye Wangchuan only said it casually and wasn’t serious about making sugar tomatoes. He put his hands in his pockets. With his collarbone showing, he stared at her with his deep black eyes and asked, “What about spicy chicken? I think you liked this dish at the Imperial Mansion.”","“Okay.”","Hearing that it was a Sichuan dish, Qiao Nian became more interested. Skepticism appeared on her porcelain small face. “You know how to make spicy chicken?”","“You’ll know once you try it!” The suspicious man raised his attractive eyebrows, and his eyes were deep. “I know more than you think.”","Qiao Nian was speechless.","Erm... it was a very normal sentence, but why did she feel that he was teasing her!","...","Ye Wangchuan cooked very quickly, and soon, three dishes and a soup were ready.","He brought the spicy chicken out.","“It’s time to eat.”","His thin sweater gave him a good silhouette. At this moment, he slowly rolled up his sleeves. The jewelry on his wrist was extremely eye-catching. The Buddhist beats fit perfectly with his aura and looked pleasing to the eye.","Qiao Nian inexplicably remembered something Wei Lou used to say, “Being handsome is not about looks but a type of temperament.”","She never thought about it in the past, but she suddenly felt that it was an apt description of the person in front of her.","However, compared to the person who was pleasing to the eye, the spicy chicken on the table was more attractive to her.","Qiao Nian felt hungry when she smelled the chili oil and pepper.","Gu San filled her bowl with rice and gave her a pair of chopsticks, saying, “Miss Qiao, try it.”","Qiao Nian was never a hypocritical person. She took the chopsticks and went straight for her favorite dish. She put a piece of chicken in her mouth. The chicken was fried, crispy, and spicy. The meat was also not dry. It was so delicious that she almost swallowed it without chewing."]},{"number":521,"title":"Chapter 521 - Why Are They So Calm!","paragraphs":["“How is it?” Ye Wangchuan especially learned to cook this dish from a chef at Imperial Mansion. He was a fast learner and had never doubted his ability. However, this time, he had some self-doubt.","Qiao Nian gave him a thumbs-up and praised him. “Delicious!”","“It’s that good?” Jiang Li was tempted. He picked up his chopsticks as well and tried the dish. However, the first mouthful was spicy enough to turn his face red. But that didn’t stop him from giving his compliments. “Master Wang, this is good. When did you have this up your sleeve?”","He took another bite and said with a full mouth, “Master Wang, are you considering switching things up and becoming a chef instead? Given your culinary skills, I think you’ll be able to make a good living.”","Ye Wangchuan couldn’t be bothered to deal with him. He pulled out a chair and sat across Qiao Nian, then scooped some soup for the girl who was happily eating. He placed the bowl of soup next to her.","His eyes were dark and deep as he asked, “What plans do you have for the afternoon?”","Qiao Nian didn’t like to be distracted while eating, but given that she was eating what he had prepared, she felt a need to respond. She looked up and said, “I think I’ll make a trip down to school.”","Chen Yuan had been bailed out, so she could take her time settling the scores with the Wei Family.","She had to return to school after her leave of absence.","By rights, the school only allowed a leave of absence of three days. Shen Hui had gone against the rules and given her a week of leave. Since she was back, she had to cancel her leave. Otherwise, she would affect the class’s attendance.","On that thought, Qiao Nian felt that she had been troubled by a lot of things lately.","In the past, she would never have cared about class pride and the like. She was so used to being alone and hardly interacted much with her classmates.","Of course, nobody really wanted to approach her too.","Most of the class would treat her like a freak. They kept their distance when they saw her, rather than treating her as a friend.","But the people in Class A were not like that...","She recalled how Liang Bowen flew to Beijing just to “comfort” her and how Shen Qingqing, Jiang Tingting, and the rest texted her non-stop to cheer her up. Upon thinking about the jar full of paper cranes that Liang Bowen had brought to her, her heart warmed and her hand froze for a moment. She looked up once again and added, “I haven’t seen them in a while, so I’ll treat them later. I won’t be back for dinner.”","Ye Wangchuan had always encouraged her to interact more with her friends. After hearing her decision, he leaned back in his seat with no objections.","“Get Gu San to drive you after this. You’re too lazy to get a cab.”","Qiao Nian stuck her chopsticks in her rice and thought about whether she should stop by the hospital after this to visit Aunt Chen and the rest. She looked at those squinted eyes and said patronizingly, “Ah, we’ll see.”","She then added, “We’ll see when the time comes. I’ll let you know if I’m not getting a cab.”","“Yes.”","It was a hearty and happy meal.","Qiao Nian had her fill and also some soup, upon someone’s request. Having had enough, she looked at the time.","It was almost 3:30 in the afternoon.","First High School had long started their lessons for the day.","If she went now, she’d only make it for the last lesson.","Qiao Nian didn’t intend to delay any further. She got up and said to the rest of them in the house, “I’ll head to school first.”","With that, she went upstairs to grab her stuff.","Only after she left her seat did Jiang Li realize that he had forgotten something important—he’d forgotten to ask Qiao Nian what exactly she intended to do about Wei Qi!!!","Wei Qi’s matter wasn’t even settled yet.","Why were Master Wang and Nian Nian so calm!","It was as if he was the only person anxious over it!! How sad!!"]},{"number":522,"title":"Chapter 522 - Couldnt Be Bothered With This Small Fry","paragraphs":["On the other side, Qiao Chen was preparing to leave.","She had arrived in Rao City at four in the morning and did not return home as it was too late. Hence, she and Shen Jingyan stayed in a hotel.","At noon, Xu Xu and Cai Yan, who knew she was returning from Beijing, called her to tell her that the class was preparing a party for her.","They wanted her to make a trip down to First High School.","If this had taken place a few days before, she might not have wanted to go.","After all, she had spent a month in Beijing and gained a lot of exposure living with Shen Jingyan and Wei Ling. She personally experienced the life of the upper class and felt some disdain towards these people in Rao City.","But she was in a great mood these few days.","Moreover, she had transferred out of First High School in such a hurry that it was embarrassing. Now that she was a student of Qing University and her ex-classmates wanted to celebrate for her, she agreed, with some intention to show off.","Since she was going to attend the party, she had to make sure that she was well-dressed. She spent so much time preparing that, by the time she left the house, it was already five in the afternoon, five hours after Xu Xu had called her.","Qiao Chen didn’t mind the time. She picked up her belongings and had just stepped out of the door when she heard Shen Jingyan talking to a man.","“Brother Shen, what’s with that Qiao Nian? I’ve asked Wei Ling, but she said you’re closer to her. Do you know what’s her background...”","Wei Dongshan paused midway when he saw Qiao Chen appear in his peripheral vision. He immediately turned to ask her.","“You are?”","Shen Jingyan turned around and saw Qiao Chen standing respectfully by the side. He rubbed his tired eyes and called out to her, “Chen Chen, come over.”","He then introduced her to Wei Dongshan. “This is my sister’s daughter, Qiao Chen. She’d put up at my house during the time she was sitting for the entrance examinations. Now, she’s successfully entered Qing University. Her mother gave her a call and got her to return to have a celebration, so I brought her along. The flight is late at night, and I found it unsafe to have her go home on her own. So, we put up in a hotel.”","Shen Jingyan was rich and generous. He was putting up in a high-class suite in a five-star hotel. The suite had two stories and four bedrooms, and even the kitchen was well-equipped.","Qiao Chen stayed on the upper floor.","She was standing by the two of them now.","Shen Jingyan was rather bothered by some matters and briefly introduced him to Qiao Chen. “This is your aunt’s cousin, you can address him as Uncle Wei.”","Qiao Chen had always been an obedient kid. On cue, she greeted him, “Hello, Uncle Wei.”","“Hello.” Wei Dongshan simply nodded at her and acknowledged her greeting, but he wasn’t concerned about her.","He hadn’t slept last night as Old Master Su’s reception was too late. He decided to wait up till dawn to quickly get some information.","The moment day broke, he started making countless calls to the neighboring cities. He looked for everybody he could think of but still had not managed to find out how Su Huaiyuan was related to Qiao Nian.","At this point, he really felt like his pants were on fire. Given how anxious he was, how could he possibly pay attention to a Shen family relative? If Shen Jingyan did not mention that she got into Qing University, he wouldn’t even be bothered with this small fry.","Qiao Chen could tell that his response was patronizing. She grabbed her bag straps tightly and made an appropriate remark, “Uncle, my classmates are meeting me back at my alma mater. I won’t bother you and Uncle Wei any further. I’ll take my leave first.”"]},{"number":523,"title":"Chapter 523 - Waiting for Sister Nians huge trouble?","paragraphs":["Her obedience softened Shen Jingyan’s expression. He waved her off. “Go ahead. Be careful and don’t stay out too late. Call your mother when it’s about time.”","“Alright.” Qiao Chen agreed quickly.","Before leaving, she took one last glance at the man sitting across Shen Jingyan. She felt that this Wei Dongshan wasn’t an ordinary person. His aura was extraordinary.","She thought about it for a while and recalled what she had heard him say. She smiled upon thinking about it.","It was Qiao Nian again!","It seemed like Qiao Nian was in huge trouble now!","Her footsteps were light and cheery as she left.","She didn’t hear what Wei Dongshan said worriedly after she’d left.","“I didn’t realize this Qiao Nian’s background was so complicated. She actually knows Old Master Su! You weren’t around to see Old Master Su’s attitude when he received her. He was obviously on her side, and they’re definitely close. Also, I heard this morning that someone bailed Chen Yuan out last night. I asked who it was, and not a single one of them dared to reveal the person’s identity... Brother Shen, that Qiao Nian is your niece and you know her well. Just where did she come from? How have I never heard of her when I was in Rao City?”","Shen Jingyan was so silent, it was as if someone had grabbed him by the throat.","He spent most of his time in Beijing and hardly returned to Rao City. When he learned about this ‘daughter’ from his sister’s family, he did not treat her terribly, but neither did he take special note of her. Under such circumstances, how was he to know about Qiao Nian?!","Wei Dongshan looked at how silent he was acting and took a few sips of tea out of frustration. His brows were locked, and he said solemnly, “You’ve got no idea, I feel like something huge is happening this time! I couldn’t sleep at all last night, and now I’m involved in this matter too. If this doesn’t get settled soon enough, the tables are going to turn!”","He went on, “I’ve already told Wei Ling, but she wouldn’t listen. Why don’t you talk to her and let her know not to persist in this matter? It’s about time she let it go! We both know what Wei Qi is like. He wouldn’t have been beaten up for nothing, he must have offended someone or done something terribly wrong. We have already canceled Qiao Nian’s student status. We just need to get her to pay a sum in compensation and leave it be. It’s what’s best for everyone. There’s no good in blowing this up... Old Master Su...”","Besides being afraid of the big boss Su Huaiyuan, he was also intimidated by the person who bailed Chen Yuan out.","Given his identity, half of Rao City was practically his territory. He already said his piece this morning, but nobody dared to reveal who the other party was.","What did that mean?","Their silence said more than words!","That person was surely at the top of the pyramid. He must be somebody who could determine one’s destiny with just a flick of his sleeves. That was why everyone kept mum!","Shen Jingyan listened to him. He saw how he was anxious sitting down and thought of standing a few times.","Exhaustion seeped through his thick brows as he met eyes with Wei Dongshan, whose gaze was more solemn than his. “The tables have already turned!”","Wei Dongshan was speechless.","Shen Jingyan had no idea how to tell him about the situation in Beijing. Even he had no idea what trump card Ye Wangchuan held against Wei Qi. He vaguely expressed, “The Ye family has already come into the picture!”","“You mean Master Wang?!” Wei Dongshan stood up agitatedly. His face went pale, and he fell back in his seat. Regret filled his face. “No wonder... no wonder nobody dared to tell me who bailed Chen Yuan...”"]},{"number":524,"title":"Chapter 524 - So Smart That They Had to Hide Her Results","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","If it really was the crown prince of the Ye family, who in Rao City would dare to reveal it?","Wei Dongshan was extremely regretful for finding his way into Wei Qi’s affairs. He really regretted getting himself involved. Then, he wouldn’t have had to deal with this much trouble now.","So much of his was at stake.","He felt like an innocent passerby who found himself caught in a fight between two forces!","Wei Dongshan looked at Shen Jingyan dead in the eye. His fingers were locked together and he was trying not to shake nervously. He asked with an awful expression, “Tell me the truth. Just who is Qiao Nian and where is she from? She’s beaten someone up, and now all the big bosses have found their way to Rao City all at once!”","This was a bloody mess!","He had seen the case file. She was just an ordinary high school student!","...","Said ordinary high school student had just arrived at First High School and was clearing her leave with Shen Hui.","Shen Hui had no lessons in the afternoon. Upon hearing that she was coming, she waited in the office.","The teachers in the staff room got agitated upon seeing Qiao Nian.","“This is the student who scored full marks in the Qing University examinations?”","“Teacher Shen, you’ve already got Wu Jie, the 500-pointer from your class. And now you’ve got...” The female teacher didn’t reveal her marks. She was envious, evidently wishing that Qiao Nian was her student instead. “Tsk, once the College Entrance Examinations are over and Qing University releases the scores, I bet the other schools in Rao City will go crazy.”","Qing University’s examination results were kept strictly confidential, even more so now than before. Some other schools’ results could be found online, but Qing University had not released them yet.","A lot of people thought that the questions from Qing University’s examinations were too difficult this time and that the students who sat for the papers were not of a high caliber, so the school refused to publish the results. They assumed that Qing University might be embarrassed if their grades were inferior to the other schools’.","Only a very small minority knew what was really going on.","Qing University wasn’t keeping the results from others because the students did terribly. It was because a student had done too well!","They were afraid that other schools would poach this student before everything was set in stone!","Also, Qiao Nian was a student wanted by the only two honorary professors of the school—Master Nie and Mr. Huang.","If Qiao Nian didn’t end up going to Qing University...","The two professors might just fade from the scene again!","They wouldn’t allow this to happen. This was why they kept their results so confidential this time and made sure not a single bit of information could be accessed. Even most of the people in Qing University had no idea about the examination situation.","“It seems like the compilation of model essays I handed to Qiao Nian was useful, after all.” The Form Teacher of Class C was a man with a smiley and plump face. He was holding a thermos flask and patting Qiao Nian on the shoulder. “Nice one, kid! Making Form Teacher proud!”","Shen Hui wasn’t aware of the delay in the processing of Qiao Nian’s student status. She had no idea about what had happened to Chen Yuan over the last few days, either. Seeing that Qiao Nian was back, she couldn’t conceal the smile on her usually stern face. Taking the leave slip from her, she said gently, “Your leave only ends tomorrow, why didn’t you rest more since you’ve just returned? You didn’t have to rush back.”","Qiao Nian put her hands in her pockets and replied casually, “I’m eating with some classmates. Since I was coming back, I might as well clear my leave.”","“That works too,” Shen Hui said, then thought of something. “Oh, right. The principal wants me to talk to you about something.”","“?”","Qiao Nian raised a brow.","Shen Hui smiled and said, “About the College Entrance Examination.”"]},{"number":525,"title":"Chapter 525 - Did Not Agree Immediately","paragraphs":["Shen Hui told her what Principal Yu thought.","He hoped that she could sit for the upcoming College Entrance Examination and bring glory to the school.","Of course, this was entirely up to Qiao Nian. They wouldn’t force her to do it.","In other words, Qiao Nian could choose not to sit for the College Entrance Examination. She could just use her results from the previous examination to enter the Chinese Medicine Faculty of Qing University.","As to that, Qiao Nian did not agree immediately.","This was because Nie Mi had sent her a message earlier, saying he hoped that she wouldn’t sit for the College Entrance Examination. His reason was simple. He was worried that she would do too well and that other schools would eye her. He didn’t want her to change her mind about joining Qing University.","Although she didn’t agree immediately, Shen Hui kept her calm and did not make things difficult for her in any way. Shen Hui simply hoped that she would consider this option, but did not say anything more.","...","Qiao Nian left the office and headed for the school gate directly.","Liang Bowen, Shen Qingqing, and the rest had received her message and were already waiting at the school gate.","They got excited once Qiao Nian appeared.","“Sister Nian, what are we having?”","Qiao Nian was in a white T-shirt and had a black cap on. She looked at them with her bright eyes and said, “Anything’s fine. You guys decide.”","She had some money, anyway.","It was just a meal.","They could eat all they wanted!","Hearing that, Liang Bowen brushed his nose and looked like he was spoiled for choice as he asked the rest, “Sister Nian’s treating, where should we go?”","“Anywhere’s fine...” Shen Qingqing saw that there were many people around and did not want Qiao Nian to spend too much money.","The rest of the Class A students felt the same.","However, there were just too many eating outlets around school. It was hard to make a choice even if they were easygoing.","Fortunately, Jiang Tingting’s group of friends often dined near school and were very familiar with the options around. Seeing that nobody else had an idea, she suggested, “I remember seeing a new Japanese restaurant opposite our school. It opened only last month, and the place seems nice. It’s reasonably priced, too. Shall we go there?”","Shen Qingqing and a few others had seen that restaurant before when walking to school. The place was brightly lit with large windows, and the interior looked pretty cozy. Moreover, it was a new eatery but had promotional posters once in a while.","“Let’s go there, then.”","Shen Qingqing turned to look at the rest. “Is everyone else alright with that? Voice your objections now, or we’ll settle on that.”","Everyone in Class A just wanted to have a meal with Sister Nian. It didn’t really matter what they were eating.","They were agreeable and instantly decided to dine at the restaurant Jiang Tingting mentioned.","“Sister Nian, let’s have Japanese food then. What about you? Do you have any preferences, we can go with what you like.” After asking for everyone’s take, she made sure to ask for Qiao Nian’s too.","“I’m fine.”","Qiao Nian didn’t seem to have any objection, either.","She stood there carefreely, pulling her cap downwards slightly. “Since we’ve decided, let’s go. I don’t know the way, so I’ll just follow you guys.”","“I know where it is! I’ll lead.”","Jiang Tingting raised her hand and led the group towards the food street.","...","At this moment, the Japanese restaurant they picked was rather crowded.","The Class B teacher had released the class earlier. Xu Xu, Cai Yan, and a few others in their clique took up the largest table in the restaurant and had ordered quite a bit.","They sat around the table, with Qiao Chen being the focus of attention."]},{"number":526,"title":"Chapter 526 - New Belle in Qing University","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","It was time-consuming to prepare Japanese dishes. Seeing that they were a large group, the boss served them some tea first.","Qiao Chen picked up her cup and took a sip elegantly.","It tasted alright. Just one sip was enough for her to tell that the tea leaves were of inferior quality.","She had tasted high-quality tea in the Shen Family home. Having tasted tea that cost thousands of yuan for a few hundred grams of leaves, she became pickier. She put her cup down after just a sip and never touched it again. In fact, she despised the Class B students for picking such a low-class place.","But she had always been adept at keeping her thoughts to herself. While unhappy that her classmates picked such a place to celebrate her achievements, she did not show it.","Meanwhile, Xu Xu, who saw that she was just smiling quietly and no longer sipping her tea, asked, “Chen Chen, have you confirmed your place in Qing University’s Music Faculty? Ah, I envy you. I saw that all the other schools have posted their scores, but not Qing University. I was going to show it off to my mom and dad that you made it into Qing University, but I couldn’t find any news of it.”","The moment she mentioned Qiao Chen’s admission into Qing University, the rest diverted their gazes to Qiao Chen.","That was nothing unusual.","Somebody in class had made it to the top institution. Anyone would be envious!","It was just that some of them showed it while others did not.","Qiao Chen felt everyone’s attention on her. Even the store manager was looking her way now. She smiled reservedly and feigned humility. “Mm, it’s confirmed. Professor Cheng Wu told me about it. He said I’ve been selected by the Music Faculty. I just have to wait till the College Entrance Examinations are over to transfer my file.”","“Wow!” Xu Xu was so envious. She rested her chin on her palms and asked excitedly, “Is this Professor Cheng Wu the Finance Department’s Professor Cheng Wu?”","Qiao Chen found her question a mockery. How could there possibly be two Professor Cheng Wus in Qing University? But she kept her composure and feigned patience, replying tenderly, “Mm, it’s that Professor Cheng Wu indeed. He’s Brother Fu’s mentor, and we have met once before. I was lucky to have had a chance to have a meal with him, so I added him on WeChat. When the results were out, he messaged me on WeChat to tell me about it.”","She made it sound like it was not a big deal, while still emphasizing the important parts.","As she expected, the Class B students looked even more envious now.","Cai Yan was a rich second-generation heiress just like her, but her results weren’t as good. Upon hearing this, she was envious and jealous at the same time. She said a little bitterly, “So in the future, Senior Fu Ge and you could be such an honorable couple in school. You guys will be a focal point of your own. Tsk, how nice.”","Nobody in Class B said anything in response, but they were undoubtedly feeling the same.","It was no surprise. She was pretty and had good results, and her boyfriend was an outstanding lad no less. They compared her to themselves, who still had to work hard for the next few months before the College Entrance Examination. The difference was stark...","The atmosphere got a little heavy.","Qiao Chen tried to ease the tension and picked the cup up to conceal her smile. She appeared embarrassed as she said, “You guys have to stop making fun of me.”","Ever since Zhao Jingwei had been sentenced, Xu Xu had become her top lackey. She supported whatever Qiao Chen said. She added, “Even without Senior Fu Ge, Chen Chen would still be a beautiful focal point on her own in Qing University. I bet there will be a new belle in Qing University once the next semester starts.”","It was obvious which belle she was referring to.","Upon mention of the school belle, someone in Class B recalled. “Oh, right. I heard Qiao Nian from Class A sat for the examinations as well.. We haven’t heard anything from Class A’s side.”"]},{"number":527,"title":"Chapter 527 - Happened to Hear Her Name","paragraphs":["The atmosphere became a little strange the moment he mentioned Qiao Nian’s name.","Qiao Chen despised the tea here and was unwilling to drink it.","But now that she had raised her cup again, she had to take a sip. She brushed her hair aside and tucked it behind her ear, looking calm and composed. It was as if that name meant nothing to her.","Xu Xu’s reaction was the quickest. She snapped out of it quickly and frowned at the person who brought it up. “Wang Heng, why did you have to mention her? Such a downer. Everyone’s happily celebrating Chen Chen’s admission today, but you have to bring up this name that upsets her. Look, now everyone’s unhappy.”","Wang Heng was also a student of Class B. He was a cheeky, playful student whose results were average. He had wooed Qiao Chen earlier on and had always bootlicked her. Even now, he still liked her.","He leaned back in his seat nonchalantly and propped an arm up. “I’m not trying to do anything. It just came to mind.”","He scanned the table and eventually landed his gaze on a girl with thick glasses. He asked mockingly, “Wu Jie, aren’t you from Class A? Tell us about it, how did Qiao Nian do? She especially took leave just to go to Qing University for the examinations, did she make it?”","It was a Class B gathering today, but Qiao Chen invited Wu Jie over.","She said it was just for a meal.","Wu Jie came without knowing that the other Class B students would be around. She thought that Qiao Chen had asked her out individually. By the time she realized and wanted to leave, Qiao Chen had already seen her and called out to her.","Now that everyone was looking at her and waiting for her response, she furrowed her brows and pushed her glasses upwards slightly. She answered hurriedly, “Uh... I heard she didn’t make it.”","Her voice was as soft as a mosquito’s buzzing. One had to pay attention to hear her.","Her quiet voice went, “We didn’t see her when Chen Chen and I were in the classroom waiting for the interview. Most people who didn’t make it past the written segment would not be around for the second round, so...”","Just as Qiao Nian set foot into the restaurant with Jiang Tingting, she heard someone saying her name.","“Ah, you don’t have to be so tactful and long-winded about it. Essentially, Qiao Nian didn’t make it!”","Her jawline was cold as usual as she pulled her cap downwards slightly and looked up.","Eh?","Didn’t make it to what?","Wu Jie didn’t say it explicitly. She tried to be indirect about it, but her point was obvious enough. “I think so. If she made it, our class wouldn’t be so quiet about it. I think it’s likely that she did not make it.","“It’s tough to get into Qing University, everyone there is the cream of the crop. I think Chen Chen is the only one in Rao City who made it this year. I was eliminated in the second round, too.”","Her results for the examinations were just all right at 500 marks. She managed to get through the first round and was offered an interview for her choice department, the Physics Department. However, she was unable to answer quite a number of questions asked by the Physics professor. So, it was clear why she did not make it.","She wasn’t surprised by this outcome. She didn’t think she would make it either, but she wanted to give it a shot.","Though she hadn’t passed the interview round, she hadn’t rushed off immediately. She stayed in the classroom for a while more and heard later on that Qiao Chen had made it. She even heard a candidate mention that Professor Cheng Wu of the Finance Department had a good impression of her and personally invited her to consider the Finance Department as her minor.","Wu Jie couldn’t express her emotions. She was simply in envy. Of course, there was some admiration and respect too; Qiao Chen was, after all, the person that every girl wished to be.","She was pretty, had a good family background, scored good grades, and was such a kind and gentle person..."]},{"number":528,"title":"Chapter 528 - Who Are You Saying That Didn’t Make It?","paragraphs":["As she thought about that, she pouted, not noticing the person who had just arrived at the door. She sounded indignant for Qiao Chen. “Chen Chen’s results are so good, she shouldn’t have transferred out of First High School back then. If she hadn’t left, the glory would surely be First High School’s. Now Fifth High School has it too easy. She was jealous of Chen Chen and wanted to chase her away, but now she didn’t even make it to Qing University herself. I really wonder what she’s thinking sometimes...”","She didn’t speak loudly, but the restaurant was only that large.","Liang Bowen and the rest happened to hear this part and immediately got angry. “Wu Jie, who are you talking about! Who didn’t make it, who’s jealous of Qiao Chen? Make yourself clear!”","Damn, who the hell said that Sister Nian didn’t make it? He would teach them a lesson!","Wu Jie and the Class B students didn’t notice the group who had just entered. Who was the person leading Class A if not Qiao Nian?","They were caught in the act of gossiping behind someone’s back. Everyone’s expressions immediately turned awkward.","Wu Jie shrank back as her face went pale. She looked in shock at the people who had just entered, realizing that besides her, practically the whole of Class A was here.","Including Qiao Nian!","The girl standing in front of the rest had a cap on and revealed only half her face. Just her beautiful jawline and her posture were enough to scream her presence.","Such a wild and charismatic figure!","Recalling what she had just said about Qiao Nian, her hands clenched into fists in a moment of nervousness as dozens of pairs of eyes were fixated on her. She opened her mouth and thought to stand up, but she felt as if her feet were nailed to the ground. Unable to move, her face went pale right away. She stammered, “I- I didn’t mean it that way.”","“Then, what did you mean? Make yourself clear. Let us all hear you out.” Liang Bowen’s handsome face went slightly cold as he folded his arms across his chest, not saving her any face.","He was actually a rather gentlemanly guy and hardly raised his voice at girls, but Wu Jie had really said such terrible things. He couldn’t listen on!","“Who were you referring to when you said she didn’t make it and was jealous of Qiao Chen? Who was it? Don’t tell me you weren’t talking about anyone. You said so much about it, it can’t be nobody!”","Qiao Nian wasn’t petty, especially not with a girl like this who wasn’t worth her time. It wasn’t as if she did something overboard, so Qiao Nian couldn’t be bothered by her. She pulled the furious guy back and said, “Liang Bowen, forget it.”","“Sister Nian!” Liang Bowen couldn’t take this lying down.","Many other Class A students were angry as well. They were mad at the girl from their class who had gone to join Class B for a meal. How could Wu Jie join outsiders to talk bad about their own classmate?","Wu Jie felt as if every gaze directed at her was a needle in her skin. She bit her lip and said out of the blue, “I’m talking about her. Am I not speaking facts? She didn’t make it into Qing University, and Chen Chen did transfer schools because of her. If it wasn’t for her, there would be one more student from First High School making it into Qing University. Because of her, our school lost this glorious opportunity. Can’t I say a word or two?”","What was she saying?","The Class A students were fuming.","Especially Shen Qingqing. Previously, she was stopping Liang Bowen from going on as well. But now, she couldn’t hold back any longer.","“What do you mean?","“Tell me, what have you said that’s right? Did Sister Nian offend you in any way? Or dig up your ancestor’s grave? Did you have to be so mean!”","Wu Jie actually straightened up and retorted, “I was just speaking some facts, what does it have to do with whether someone offended me? Moreover, what have I done? Did I tell her off? How am I mean?”"]},{"number":529,"title":"Chapter 529 - Her Face Would Be Beaten Up Badly","paragraphs":["None of the Class B students expected her to be so defensive.","She even argued with her own classmates.","When they regained their senses, they also started to mock Qiao Nian.","“That’s right. Wu Jie didn’t say anything wrong. It’s too overbearing to prevent others from speaking the truth.”","“What do you even know about this? Class A is the best class in the school. It’s only natural that they don’t allow others to speak badly of them. She’s the star student. She must be extraordinary!”","“Wow, the star student didn’t make it into Qing University? She went to Beijing only to fail the examination?”","“It must be painful to hear the truth, so watch what you are saying. Everyone from Class A is there. What if they hear us and get angry? I’m so afraid of them.”","...","Qiao Chen heard her classmates mocking Class A, and the corners of her mouth raised mockingly.","She didn’t understand why Qiao Nian wasn’t arrested for beating Wei Qi. However, she felt so good at the moment that she didn’t bother to find out the reason.","This matter could have been resolved quickly if she bothered to speak up. She could persuade both sides to stop quarreling, but she didn’t say anything. She sat in her seat leisurely. Her expression was calm, and she held on to the cup proudly as though she was appreciating the tea.","Shen Qingqing felt disgusted upon seeing her relaxed look.","Just as she was about to reply.","Qiao Nian held her back.","“Sister Nian?” She turned her head and looked at Qiao Nian. She was puzzled and didn’t understand what Qiao Nian wanted to do.","Qiao Nian took her hand out of her pocket and walked leisurely over to the table where the students of Class B were sitting.","Although she was slim, she had a strong aura. Not everyone could imitate her strong spirit.","It was too arrogant!","Many students from Class B were gathered there, but no one dared to speak. Although it seemed like there were many of them, when faced with Qiao Nian alone, they no longer dared to show off.","“What... what do you want?” Xu Xu was a timid person. She was seated beside Qiao Chen, but she felt uneasy. She looked at Qiao Nian with worry and vigilance and then said, “Qiao Nian, are you thinking of beating someone? You better not mess around. We’re very close to the school, we can sue you anytime.”","Qiao Nian tutted. Her reply was a casual mockery of what Xu Xu said.","Qiao Nian had a cool expression on her face as she glanced at her and said, “Have I ever said that I wanted to beat you?”","Xu Xu was speechless.","You never said that, but your posture suggested otherwise.","Xu Xu didn’t dare to say anything.","Qiao Nian raised her head slightly and revealed a stunning face. She narrowed her eyes slightly, looked at Wu Jie at the side, and asked her a question.","“How many marks did Qiao Chen score?”","Her voice was slightly hoarse.","It sounded like she had just woken up.","However, it still sounded very good.","It was very provocative.","Wu Jie was stunned by her question and subconsciously looked at Qiao Chen sitting beside her.","Qiao Chen’s heart was pounding. She turned her gaze away from her teacup towards Qiao Nian. Her eyes moved restlessly and her face was pale. Her fingers pinched the teacup as she pursed her lips and said, “They were just joking, they didn’t mean what they said. You can’t be so petty as to hold it against them, right?”","Now, it seemed as though Qiao Nian and her classmates were the ones talking behind someone else’s backs.","Liang Bowen’s face sank, and he couldn’t help but resent her. He said, “You act so magnanimous now, asking us to forgive you guys for making a joke. But what were you doing earlier? When your classmates were bad-mouthing Sister Nian just now, why did you not stop them? Now, if we want to argue with you, we’re the ones being petty? Qiao Chen, I would advise you to not treat people with double standards!”","His words were cruel and direct, causing Qiao Chen’s face to turn dull and pale.","Qiao Nian didn’t bother paying attention to her. She narrowed her eyes slightly, looked at Wu Jie, and asked again, “You spoke so much just now, but you still haven’t told me how much Qiao Chen scored in the examination.”"]},{"number":530,"title":"Chapter 530 - What Did Qiao Nian Mean by That? Was She Deliberately Humiliating Her?","paragraphs":["Qiao Chen did not speak. She clenched her hands tightly, and her heartbeat accelerated.","Some people from Class B had yet to figure out the situation and continued to make rude remarks.","As Qiao Chen’s lackey, Xu Xu spoke the most viciously.","“Does it matter to you how much Chen Chen scored? What can you do about it? It’s not like you can score as high as her!”","Also having a good relationship with Qiao Chen, Cai Yan raised her chin slightly. Her smile was sarcastic, and she spoke with a tone of disdain. “Before you ask how much Chen Chen scored, what about you? Did you even score 500 points?”","Hehe!","Can you believe Sister Nian scored more than 600 points?","Liang Bowen was surprisingly not angry when he heard this. He crossed his arms across his chest and looked at the Class B students coldly. They looked like clowns that were too proud of themselves. He asked Wu Jie coldly, “Why are you not speaking? How many points did Qiao Chen get in the examination? Did she score so well that it gave you the courage to gather here and slander other people behind their backs?”","His words represented the feelings of everyone in Class A.","They were united. Although Wu Jie was usually introverted and did not like to speak up in class, she was never excluded by them.","She was always included in her class activities.","Sister Nian had also invited her to dinner a few times before.","But this time, she was sitting on Qiao Chen’s side and slandering Qiao Nian behind her back. This kind of backstabbing behaviour was disgusting. Everyone here was a hot-blooded teenager. A two-faced person was looked down on by everyone.","Wu Jie could sense the disdain from her classmates. She grew pale and fidgeted uneasily.","However, things had already turned out this way. She was caught between a rock and a hard place and could no longer turn back.","No matter how much Liang Bowen and the rest praised Qiao Nian, she didn’t get into Qing University!","She calmed down when she thought of this. She grabbed her skirt under the table, pursed her lips, and raised her head. A pair of jealous eyes were hidden behind her glasses. She then provocatively asked Qiao Nian a question, “Do you really want to know?”","“Hmm,” Qiao Nian replied casually and tilted her head back slightly. Her face was exquisite and beautiful. It was also relaxed and had a wild aura. It wasn’t as gentle as Qiao Chen’s aura.","“I don’t particularly want to know her score.”","Her answer surprised the people around her.","Wu Jie was holding her breath and preparing to shock Qiao Nian with the news. However, her reply was anticlimactic.","In the next second, the girl standing in front of her put her hand into her pocket and lowered her head. Her eyelashes drooped and she looked at Wu Jie again. She then casually said, “But looking at your reaction, my interest is piqued.”","She was aware that Qiao Chen had participated in the independent enrollment examination for Qing University. However, she never had the intention of comparing their results, let alone compete with her to see who was better.","Since Qiao Chen was no match for her, she didn’t bother to pay any attention to Qiao Chen’s achievements.","She only looked for her own score when she was checking the examination results. She didn’t check the scores of other people. However, seeing Wu Jie and the students from Class B discuss her score so excitedly and seeing Qiao Chen sitting so arrogantly, she was curious as to how much she had scored in the examination. Looking at Qiao Chen, she estimated that she had scored at least 600 points.","“620?” She squinted and glanced at the girl sitting in the middle of the crowd. She spoke very casually and was very calm.","Qiao Chen felt as though she was slapped in the face. She pinched her palm, and tears gathered in her eyes. Her eyes were filled with anger and shame."]},{"number":531,"title":"Chapter 531 - Sister Nian Was a Black Hole","paragraphs":["What did Qiao Nian mean by this? Was she trying to humiliate her deliberately by stating an impossible score?","Qiao Nian saw her expression and understood that she had overstated her score.","She thought for a moment and lowered her expectations by 10 points.","“610?”","She didn’t mean to embarrass Qiao Chen and simply guessed her scores casually.","After all, she was the genius who had scored full marks on the test. It was reasonable if she guessed the scores based on her abilities.","Liang Bowen and Shen Qingqing knew Qiao Nian’s character and were aware that she didn’t mean to humiliate Qiao Chen. However, when they saw Qiao Chen’s embarrassed and angry expression, they couldn’t help but laugh and mock her a little.","“Sister Nian, please lower your standards a little more.” Liang Bowen smiled so widely that it was disgusting.","Qiao Nian was surprised and said, “I didn’t guess low enough?”","“I think you can guess even lower than that.”","He was dying of laughter inside!","Qiao Nian pressed the brim of her cap down impatiently. Her eyes were lazy and were narrowed as if she had just woken up. Her thin lips gently let out a question. “600?”","Based on her memory, the results of the entrance examination wouldn’t be very low. After all, the top students from all over the country were sitting for this examination. Even if the questions were slightly harder than the questions from the College Entrance Examination, the final results from the entrance examination usually ranged between 500 to 630 points.","Based on the statistics, it would seem like Qiao Chen was admitted into Qing University.","Since the Class B students were all here for a special celebration, Qiao Chen’s score might have been higher than usual.","She didn’t expect her score to be lower than 600 points.","She did notice that after she asked this question, Qiao Chen’s face was filled with rage and her eyes were filled with uncontrollable anger.","Although she was very angry, she still had to maintain her image in front of her classmates. Her face was heavy as she reluctantly raised the corners of her mouth and wanted to laugh. She put on a fake smile and said softly, “My grades are not so good. I only scored 588 points in the examination.”","When she said that she scored 588 points, she spoke slowly and clearly. She made sure her words were clear enough for everyone present to hear her.","Her chin was also raised proudly, which was completely different from her modest tone.","Wu Jie was initially confused by Qiao Nian’s guesses. She quickly reacted and tried to explain. “The questions in the independent enrollment examination for Qing University were harder this year. Many people did not score well. When I tried the questions for the previous examination, I only scored 580 points. I only got 500 points for this year’s examination and barely made it to the second round. Chen Chen took the examination for the arts major and scored 588 points. This is already a very high score. She’s among the top few students this year. If she sat for the College Entrance Examination with a score like this, I’m sure she would score at least 600 points! She would be admitted into Qing University either way.”","It was as though she was deliberately trying to make Qiao Nian disgusted as she flattered Qiao Chen so openly. “I didn’t expect Chen Chen to do so well in the examination. She made great improvements. If only she did not transfer schools, she would have been ranked in the top three in the monthly test at our school.”","The top three students at the First High School were usually treated well as they were most likely to make it into a good university.","They usually aimed for the best universities like Qing University and Nanjing University.","Wu Jie used to be ranked among the top three in their grade.","However, when Qiao Nian transferred into the school, she took first place. She was followed by Liang Bowen, who ranked second. Under normal circumstances, Wu Jie would have been ranked third. However, Chen Yuan returned to school. He had dropped out of school for half a year but was ranked third when he came back. He only scored five points less than Liang Bowen. The worst thing was that they scored twenty points more than her, who was ranked fourth. Wu Jie had always felt uneasy over this.","The class had started to unite since Qiao Nian’s arrival, especially Shen Qingqing, Liang Bowen, and Chen Yuan, who always hung around her.","This included Jiang Tingting, who was able to fit in well with them. Even though she hated studying, she seemed to have begun studying hard.","She appeared to be withdrawn and introverted in the class."]},{"number":532,"title":"Chapter 532 - She Was Very Persistent in Asking Qiao Nian for Her Score","paragraphs":["She didn’t particularly dislike her behavior, she simply hated Qiao Nian! She couldn’t understand why people liked her so much. She couldn’t understand why she was naturally so popular that people would gather around her.","“No. With a score of 588, I believe you’ll be ranked first in the monthly test at our school.”","Qiao Nian was currently ranked first in the monthly test.","It was obvious that Wu Jie was targeting Qiao Nian.","Being praised so openly, Qiao Chen tucked the loose strands of her hair behind her ear. She felt better now. She pursed the corners of her mouth slightly, smiled, and said, “It’s not so exaggerated. I’m just lucky and managed to score better. It’s all thanks to my uncle who found a tutor for me. The tutor specialized in tutoring for the entrance examination for Qing University. It’s said that he was a top student who graduated from Fudan University. The questions the tutor emphasized during my tuition actually came out during the examination.”","She was actually lying.","The real reason she scored so well this time was not because of the tutor Shen Jingyan hired.","It was actually because she recognized that some questions were similar to the questions from the exercise book Qiao Nian had given her.","However, she couldn’t admit this openly.","If she said the real reason, she would be blindly giving credit to Qiao Nian.","When Xu Xu heard that, her face filled with envy. She said, “Did the tuition cost a lot?”","Qiao Chen looked down on her bumpkin dress style and smiled modestly, saying, “I’m not sure. It’s probably not very cheap, but it’s probably not the most expensive too.”","“It must be expensive. Is it not obvious? Specialized tutors like that have always been the most expensive tutors to hire. Just compare the difference between hiring a piano tutor and a tutor that specializes in preparing for the entrance examination. I estimate that one lesson would cost about 3,000 yuan. Furthermore, the prices in Rao City are probably cheaper than the prices in Beijing. In Beijing, one lesson might cost up to 10,000 yuan.” Cai Yan’s family was rich and had businesses related to the timber industry. Her family even drove branded cars like the Land Rover and lived in a villa.","When she said this, everyone started to look at Qiao Chen differently.","Cai Yan wasn’t done speaking. She deliberately said, “By the way, Chen Chen, are you wearing the limited edition skirt from Seven?”","Ever since Qiao Chen stumbled upon a bracelet from this brand previously, she had been a fan of their products.","She smiled and raised her eyebrows slightly, saying, “My uncle bought it for me. I didn’t pay attention to the brand.”","It was from her uncle again.","Everyone was jealous.","Qiao Nian glanced at her dress, which was said to be a limited edition product from Seven. The workmanship was of a better quality as compared to the dress she wore to school previously. However, it was only slightly better.","The most expensive products from Seven weren’t their limited edition products. Their most expensive products actually came from their series.","Even if some of their styles were considered limited edition, they were still considered low-end products. There were only one or two items that could be considered really high class.","For example, the dress Ye Lan bought for her. It was a limited edition dress from Seven’s high-end series.","Wu Jie was also envious that Qiao Chen had an uncle in Beijing. It was said that her uncle was very influential. She was at a level where they would never reach easily.","After she admired Qiao Chen’s dress, she didn’t forget to turn her head back to face Qiao Nian. “Before I forget, you haven’t told us your score yet.”","Liang Bowen was still wondering how the conversation’s topic switched to clothes. At that moment, Wu Jie persistently asked Qiao Nian about her score again. It was very disdainful.","Afraid that Qiao Nian would keep her score a secret, Wu Jie spoke sarcastically. “You were talking about scoring 600 points so casually just now. Chen Chen has already told you her score. How about you? How much did you score?","“It can’t be that you’re afraid! Did you even score 500 points?”"]},{"number":533,"title":"Chapter 533 - Higher Than Qiao Chen by 62 points","paragraphs":["She barely made it into the second round of the examination.","She hadn’t seen Qiao Nian in the examination hall, which also meant that Qiao Nian must have scored worse than her!","Qiao Nian definitely scored less than 500 points!","Qiao Nian had already looked away from Qiao Chen’s clothes. She glanced at her and said faintly, “I didn’t score too badly, just 62 points more than her.”","“How much did you say?” Wu Jie unconsciously raised her voice. Her expression looked funny and weird. She couldn’t help but laugh. “You said that you scored 62 points higher than Chen Chen?”","The people from Class B were stunned.","Someone started to calculate her score. “Chen Chen said that she scored 588 points. If Qiao Nian scored 62 points more than her, that means she scored 650 points?”","Another person had also calculated her score and spoke out loud. “650?”","Everyone was speechless.","Qiao Nian scored 650 points?","What a joke!","The maximum score was 650. If Qiao Nian scored 650 points, that would also mean that she had scored full marks in the examination!","Wu Jie also quickly calculated Qiao Nian’s score. She was extremely cynical. She held on to her glasses and said, “Qiao Nian, even if you wanted to boast, could you choose a more believable lie? why don’t you say that you got 700 points instead? You would sound even greater.”","Qiao Nian took her mockery literally and gave it serious consideration. Her eyes were dark and glinted as she put her hands into her pockets casually and spoke seriously. “The maximum score is only so high. I cannot score higher than that.”","Wu Jie laughed out loud.","Many students in Class B also started to laugh.","They were laughing at her for taking the mockery so seriously. They also knew that the maximum score was 650. There was no way she could say that she scored 700 points.","Qiao Chen was the only one who did not laugh. She sat there quietly and uneasily.","She remembered Wen Ziyu saying that Qiao Nian had scored full marks in the examination.","At this moment, Qiao Nian herself also said that she had scored 650 points. The uneasiness that had once shrouded her heart grew stronger. She never expected anyone to get the full score.","At the same time, she also understood Qiao Nian’s character. She would never bother to lie.","However, if Qiao Nian wasn’t lying, could it be possible that she was really the first person in the history of Qing University to get the full score? As soon as Qiao Chen thought of this, she felt so uncomfortable. It was as though a needle was poking her from behind. Her heart started to beat very quickly and the blood drained from her face.","Still acting like a fool, Wu Jie laughed and said, “You said you scored 650 points? Why did I not see you in the hall for the second round of the examination?”","Qiao Nian raised her eyelids and spoke lazily. “Is that so? I saw you talking to Qiao Chen by the podium.”","“How do you know that?” All of a sudden, Wu Jie could no longer laugh. Her expression had changed. It was as though someone was strangling her. Her face reddened and her eyes trembled violently. It was as though she had seen a ghost.","She had never told anyone that she had spoken to Qiao Chen in the examination hall, let alone when and where.","How would Qiao Nian know about this?","Qiao Nian raised her face slightly when she heard Wu Jie’s question. She raised her eyebrows casually and said, “I saw you because I was also in the examination hall. But I didn’t enter through the front door and sat in the back row. You may not have seen me...”","Wu Jie was already starting to believe her.","However, it felt as though someone had slapped her in the face. She felt embarrassed, stunned, and surprised all at the same time. Her face turned pale and her fingers started to tremble as she said, “Did you really score 650 points?”","“Does Sister Nian need to lie?” Liang Bowen sneered and glanced around at the people at the table.","He looked refreshing and handsome. Considered very handsome within First High School, he was also rich. Many girls liked him.","He dressed well and had his own style. Today, he was wearing a suit from a well-known sports brand. His hair was held back, revealing his smooth forehead. He looked fresh and handsome."]},{"number":534,"title":"Chapter 534 - Not Worthy at All!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","At this point, his hands were in his pockets, and the 1.80-meter tall guy was looking down at everyone at the table.","His gaze was rather intimidating.","“Sister Nian scored full marks, 650 points. She’s the top scorer of Qing University’s examinations this year.”","“... Qiao Nian topped the examinations?”","How could that be?","How could there be a 650-pointer for the Qing University examinations? She had done the questions, they were much harder than the practice questions outside. She did her best and only scored 500 points. As such, when she learned that Qiao Chen scored 588, she was full of admiration.","But now she learned that Qiao Nian had scored full marks!","Wu Jie felt as if she had been slapped twice. It grew quiet around her, and she saw the girl standing in front of her almost expressionlessly. Around that girl was the group of Class A students.","Liang Bowen, Shen Qingqing, Jiang Tingting, and the rest looked at her as if she was a traitor. Their gazes were so cold and distant.","Some of them didn’t even bother to conceal their disgust.","Their adverse reactions felt like a stab to her heart. She couldn’t say a word as everything now felt unreal.","Qiao Nian was first?","She was so sure that Qiao Nian didn’t make it, that was why she bootlicked Qiao Chen. Now, she had offended her entire class and had to tell Qiao Chen that she had gotten it wrong. Qiao Chen, whom she had praised sky-high over her score of 588, was actually such a joke to them.","She wasn’t even worthy of such praise.","The other party had scored full marks, and here they were talking about how she couldn’t qualify for Qing University.","Wu Jie refused to believe it. She denied it as she grabbed her cup so tightly that the cup shook. “Impossible. How could she possibly be first, what would that make Chen Chen?”","She just remarked without thinking too much, but these words offended Qiao Chen. Her face went red.","What was wrong with Wu Jie, why was she dragging her into the picture?","Liang Bowen glanced at the person who went red and burst into laughter. “How do I know what that would make her? She wasn’t anything much to begin with, it’s you who thinks she’s impressive. None of us ever thought anything of her.”","He couldn’t be bothered to go on with Wu Jie, and he knew that Qiao Nian only spoke up because she couldn’t tolerate the awful things that Wu Jie and the group continued to spew. Now that Qiao Nian had made things clear, he didn’t see a need to look at Wu Jie and the rest anymore. He said to the girl beside him, “Sister Nian, let’s go. We’ll find another place to dine at.","“After all, people don’t eat with dogs!”","The Class B students were surely upset at him calling them dogs, but none of them spoke up.","What could they do, they brought it upon themselves.","They simply had to accept it.","Moreover, Qiao Nian scored 650 marks, this was... way too high for any student. Nobody had ever thought about achieving such a score. Hence, at this point, they were truly speechless.","Since their opponent was so weak, Liang Bowen saw no fun in saying anything more to them. He turned to say to Qiao Nian, “There’s a grill restaurant nearby, we can have some grilled meat for lunch.”","Qiao Nian was very easygoing. She simply nodded and agreed to the suggestion.","“Let’s go, let’s go.” He hurriedly waved the Class A students out of the restaurant.","Everyone couldn’t be bothered by a person like Wu Jie. They were already mentally excluding her from the class as they walked out.","The next moment, the huge group was out the door, leaving Qiao Chen and the rest at their table.","The atmosphere was very much different from before.","Qiao Chen had almost scratched the skin off her palms. She tried to act as if nothing had happened as she said, “Didn’t Qiao Nian beat someone up? How is she alright?”"]},{"number":535,"title":"Chapter 535 - The School Would Expel Her If They Knew","paragraphs":["Nobody said a thing, mainly because they had no idea it even happened.","Meanwhile, Qiao Chen picked up her teacup, took a small sip, and began slowly, “I heard that the matter blew up. The person who was beaten up landed in hospital with three broken ribs...”","Upon hearing that “Qiao Nian beat someone up and he landed in hospital with three broken ribs”, Xu Xu widened her eyes and exclaimed, “That’s too much! Isn’t that breaking the rules? Wouldn’t the school expel her?”","It was bad enough if it was just a scuffle. But she beat this guy up so badly and ended up in the police station, how could the school not care?","Qiao Chen used the cup to cover her smile and turned to Wu Jie, saying as naturally as possible, “I think the school doesn’t know about it. Otherwise, they wouldn’t just leave it.”","Xu Xu nodded, seeming to have just been enlightened. “True. So what if her results are good, she’s acting like a gangster and causing so much trouble. This affects the school’s reputation. The school surely doesn’t know. Otherwise, they would have expelled her.","“If the school expels her, wouldn’t she be unable to enroll into Qing University...” She looked like she couldn’t wait to let the school know about it.","On the other hand, Qiao Chen looked gentle as she said calmly, “I’m not sure. But if she isn’t a student of any school, I doubt she would be able to enter university.”","As they say, the speaker might not have any intentions, but the listener could have their own interpretations.","Wu Jie’s initially pale face went a little red. She bit her lower lip, and the eyes behind her glasses went cold...","...","On the other side, Qiao Nian was just done having her meal with the Class A students when she received a call from Shen Jingyan.","She flagged down a cab by the road and then arrived at a cafe in the city center to meet him.","She had had a drink with Shen Jingyan before. It was a rather high-end cafe with a nice ambiance.","Qiao Nian lowered her cap before she casually pushed open the door and entered.","The moment she got in, someone waved at her.","“Nian Nian, over here!”","She looked up and caught sight of him. Of course, it was none other than the smiling Shen Jingyan.","She put her hands in her pockets and approached him, greeting him politely, “Uncle Shen.”","Shen Jingyan quickly pulled a chair for her and got the waiter to come over.","Soon, the waiter arrived and asked respectfully, “May I know what you’d like to order?”","“A Blue Mountain. No sugar, please.”","After ordering his coffee, he asked Qiao Nian, “What about you, Nian Nian? What would you like?”","Qiao Nian took a seat and leaned back. She sat very casually as she thought about it. Then, she said, “Lemon water, please.”","“A cup of Blue Mountain and a glass of lemon water?” The waiter confirmed their orders.","Qiao Nian simply nodded. “Mm.”","The waiter smiled and said, “Alright, I’ll bring it to you right away.”","Shen Jingyan hadn’t expected her to just order a glass of water. He was about to ask if she wanted anything else to drink when Qiao Nian spoke.","“Uncle Shen, is anything the matter?”","“Uh...”","The waiter happened to serve the coffee and lemon water at this point, easing his awkwardness.","Shen Jingyan picked up his cup and took a sip before starting. “It’s about Wei Qi. I heard about it. This... is his fault, and I apologize on his behalf.”","Qiao Nian wasn’t surprised at all.","After all, she had just learned from Chen Yuan that Ye Wangchuan involved himself in this matter. With that, she was even less surprised that Shen Jingyan had come looking for her."]},{"number":536,"title":"Chapter 536 - A Million Yuan in Compensation, How’s That?","paragraphs":["She was willing to meet him for a simple reason. Shen Jingyan used to treat her pretty well and was reasonable about things. She considered him to be an elder.","That was why she showed him some respect by meeting him.","But about Wei Qi’s matter...","Qiao Nian raised a brow and said succinctly, “Uncle Shen, you’ve got it wrong. He doesn’t have to apologize to me since he doesn’t owe me anything. He owes someone else an apology.”","“...”","Shen Jingyan had called Wei Ying previously to ask what exactly Master Wang of the Ye family had shown her.","Upon hearing what Qiao Nian said now, he felt his head throb.","Of course, he knew who Qiao Nian was referring to.","Chen Yuan!","A poor guy with nothing to his family’s name. His parents had moved from the country to develop their child. A guy like him had a negligible existence, and he wouldn’t even have given him a second look in the past. But now, he had no idea how to face this Chen Yuan.","Shen Jingyan’s expression tensed slightly, and he thought for a while before saying, “Nian Nian, I know what you mean. You’d like for Wei Qi to apologize to Chen Yuan. I’ve asked him about it. He did get someone to threaten Chen Yuan and make him sign it, but he had no idea that those people would get physical. He didn’t expect things to turn out like that...”","Qiao Nian didn’t make a sound, and her expression was calm as usual. She was leaning back leisurely in her seat, awaiting his continuation. He couldn’t tell if she was smiling.","Given Shen Jingyan’s current status, it had been a while since he had to speak to someone in such a demeanor. Yet, he lowered his position once again as he said softly, “Nian Nian, you have also gotten physical and stood up for Chen Yuan. He’s also lying in hospital now and has realized his mistake. Do you think it’s possible to minimize the problem...”","Qiao Nian waited for him to be done before resting her hand on the edge of the glass table. She looked extremely casual and at ease as she asked him, “Uncle Shen, if, I’m saying if, Chen Yuan was your son, would you be saying this to me now and telling me to forget it?”","This silenced Shen Jingyan.","Because he knew his answer!","He would never allow it to slide just like that!","Seeing his reaction, Qiao Nian went on, “Wei Qi is lying in the hospital now, but Chen Yuan was also beaten up and might not be able to make it into a university because of this. You should know about his family’s situation by now. They’re not doing well; his father is in the hospital all year round and his mother makes a living at a stall. The family depended on him to qualify for a university to change their lives...”","Shen Jingyan didn’t bother about these. He was getting frustrated. Like Wei Ling, he didn’t care about Chen Yuan at all. He immediately said, “I really... had not considered this well enough. How about this, Nian Nian. We’ll compensate his family. A million yuan, how’s that?”","A million yuan?","For most ordinary people, this was indeed a large sum of money. In Chen Yuan’s case, for instance, his family would probably not be able to make that sum even in 10 years.","But she had money herself. If Aunt Chen was willing to accept this sort of money, she would have been able to provide for her without her having to run her stall. But the point was that Aunt Chen never accepted her money. That was why she could only help her out in other ways, like getting Uncle Chen into a single-bed ward, or altering the medical bills for their family such that they only had to pay a third of it or less. Of course, she did this behind the Chen family’s back, without anyone knowing...","Hence, when she heard that Shen Jingyan wanted to use money to settle the matter, she felt like laughing deep down in her heart. But in her eyes, there was only coldness."]},{"number":537,"title":"Chapter 537 - I Could Even Get Professor Liang Lu to Treat His Father","paragraphs":["“Uncle Shen, I think you’ve got me wrong,” she said slowly.","Shen Jingyan misunderstood her and thought that she found the compensation amount insufficient. Hence, he said, “In that case, since you said that Chen Yuan’s father is in the hospital all year round, and the hospitals in Rao City don’t have the best resources, I can transfer him to a hospital in Beijing and find the best specialist for him.”","On that note, something came to mind. “Have you heard of Professor Liang Lu from Qing University?”","His expression softened and he smiled slightly. “She’s a top-tier neurologist in the country. If Chen Yuan’s father has a related condition, I can step forward and get Professor Liang Lu to have a look at him. Professor Liang Lu hardly ever does consultation for anyone. She takes on no more than two or three surgeries per year. But she owes me a favor and should accede to my request if I come forward. She’s likely to agree to it if I ask her... This is already an unimaginable concession, I believe it should be enough to make up for Wei Qi’s folly.”","Liang Lu.","Qiao Nian went through this name for a bit and recalled this person. She was the one who specially made the trip down to Rao City to benevolently offer Qiao Nian a secured place in Qing University. It was she who flared up in embarrassment after Qiao Nian rejected her, and in turn, found trouble with Qiao Nian thereafter.","She squinted her eyes as she leaned back. Her expression was one of disdain—this person did not mean much to her.","Compared to Liang Lu...","She was more certain of Mr. Huang’s ability in treating Uncle Chen.","As for Liang Lu, she didn’t even have the basic character for being a doctor. She didn’t think much about a person like Liang Lu in the medical field.","How good could a doctor be if she couldn’t even tolerate and embrace differences?","Chinese Medicine, Western Medicine... were they not serving the same purpose of treating patients?","If she really wanted to get someone to treat Uncle Chen, she could get Mr. Huang. There was no need for her to go through him to ask for Liang Lu’s help.","In terms of both reputation and skills, Liang Lu and Mr. Huang were not in the same league; not locally, not internationally either!","But this simply wasn’t the time. Uncle Chen’s constitution was too weak at the moment, and it wasn’t suitable to get him to travel. She had to take the next few months to strengthen his constitution before she could consider the next step.","Shen Jingyan was still going on about how good Liang Lu was and how difficult it was to get her help.","Qiao Nian interrupted him and said curtly, “Uncle Shen, I can let Wei Qi’s matter slide, but my two requests remain. Firstly, Wei Qi has to apologize to Chen Yuan. Secondly, Chen Yuan’s education cannot be compromised. This is my bottom line. If these requests aren’t met, there’s nothing left to talk about.”","Shen Jingyan didn’t expect her stance to be so firm. He had already lowered himself this much, and she was still unwilling to step back.","His expression was slightly awful and his smile had faded. He looked Qiao Nian in the eye and said seriously, “Nian Nian, I can accede to the second request. But the first, could you let it go?”","Chen Yuan’s statement in which he pleaded guilty could be retracted by pulling strings, but getting Wei Qi to apologize was simply too difficult.","Firstly, Wei Qi was a second-generation heir who had been spoiled by his parents throughout his growing years. This tyrant would never admit his wrongs to anybody, not to mention to someone like Chen Yuan whom he despised.","Moreover, if Wei Qi admitted his fault, he would also be admitting to the fact that the item found on Chen Yuan actually belonged to him. He would have to be detained and face the consequences.","If Wei Qi was detained, where would the Wei Family put their pride?!","Her request sounded simple, but it was too difficult to fulfill.","At the very least, he was trying to ease the situation now.","“I know that Chen Yuan is your friend and you want to stand up for him. I’m also aware that Wei Qi wasn’t being moral, but he really knows his mistakes now. Nian Nian, can you forgive him just this once on my account? Take it that Uncle is pleading with you, alright?”"]},{"number":538,"title":"Chapter 538 - Sister Nian: I’m Poor, but I Can Afford a Lawyer","paragraphs":["At this juncture, Shen Jingyan couldn’t be bothered to protect his ego any further and played the ‘Uncle’ card.","He quietly said, “How about this, I’ll take another step back. I’ll find a way to get Chen Yuan to continue his studies, it will surely not affect his attending university. Additionally, the compensation sum I mentioned earlier will be in effect as well. I’ll also find a way to get his father to be transferred to a hospital in Beijing. If Professor Liang Lu can help out, I will get her help in treating his father. If she can’t, I will get another skilled specialist. In any case, I’ll do all I can to get his father treated... is this alright?”","He really thought that his conditions were extremely appealing.","A million yuan, the best hospital in Beijing, a skilled specialist—all things that Chen Yuan would never have been able to achieve in this lifetime.","As for Qiao Nian...","Shen Jingyan looked at the girl opposite him with a sophisticated expression. This girl was sitting in a casual position, as leisurely as anyone could get. Besides the exceptionally pretty face beneath her cap, she looked no different from an ordinary girl.","But this matter really changed his view and understanding of Qiao Nian...","He subconsciously tightened his grip on his cup as his eyes glinted. He thought about the call Wei Dongshan received before he left earlier today and felt his heart tighten.","Wei Dongshan canceled her student status the previous night.","Today, he received a call saying that the higher-ups were going to investigate this matter. They even said that Wei Dongshan was abusing his power and would undergo investigation as well.","Usually, if someone underwent investigation, the outcome wouldn’t just be a simple punishment.","Wei Dongshan evidently offended someone extraordinary!","He couldn’t tell how much backing Qiao Nian had at this point. Both superpowers, Old Master Su and the Ye family lad had gotten themselves involved in Wei Qi’s affairs.","He couldn’t tell whether these two people were contacted by the powerful Old Master in the Jiang Family, or if it was the case speculated by Wei Dongshan, that Old Master Su knew Qiao Nian personally!","He was able to swallow the first possibility, but the second was simply incredulous. He was extremely doubtful about it.","If Su Huaiyuan and Ye Wangchuan were both really standing up for Qiao Nian, wouldn’t it make him an idiot for choosing Qiao Chen over her previously!","Shen Jingyan didn’t wish to think about it. He tried to play the kinship card to get Qiao Nian on his side. He said gently, “Nian Nian, I have been thinking about his interests time and again because he’s your friend. If this goes on, everyone will get hurt.”","“Are you done talking?”","Qiao Nian picked up her glass and took a sip of her lemon water, then put it down. She grabbed her belongings, stood up, and then said to him, “Uncle Shen, since you’ve come to see me, it means that you’ve already seen Wei Qi’s documents. I’m already taking a step back and compromising on your account. If you think that Wei Qi is suffering a loss by doing this, then Chen Yuan and I can go by legal procedures. As for the money you mentioned... Chen Yuan doesn’t have it, but I do have some. It should be enough to fight a lawsuit!”","If Gu San was around, he would surely not be able to resist interjecting—”Big boss, your tiny pill can fetch an eight-figure sum, you call that ‘some’ money! That ‘some’ money of yours might just be able to knock the Wei Family, or at least Wei Ling and Wei Ying, down for a lifetime! Moreover, you have Master Wang as your backing. Causing them to go bankrupt would just be the beginning. Wei Qi would have to go to hell and back, and nobody can guarantee if he would survive!”","But Gu San wasn’t around and nobody was saying this.","Qiao Nian wouldn’t say this to Shen Jingyan, either."]},{"number":539,"title":"Chapter 539 - Scaring Sister Nian Just Because Shes Young","paragraphs":["When she was done talking, her cell phone went off. She glanced at the screen and saw that it was a message from Gu San asking if she was done eating and where she was.","He then sent her his location to tell her that he was nearby.","Qiao Nian could guess that Ye Wangchuan was probably with him. She pursed her lips for a moment and then sent a quick message.","[QN: I’ve something on, give me five minutes.]","Done replying, she placed her cell phone in her bag and looked up at Shen Jingyan.","“Uncle Shen, take some time to consider.”","Shen Jingyan looked fatigued by now. He had busied himself the whole night, and his dark eye circles were obvious.","Seeing that she was about to leave, he straightened his back and put his arm by his side. His dark eyes seemed a little threatening.","“Nian Nian, you might not understand the situation in Beijing very well.","“Beijing is dominated by three parties, the Wen Family, Ye Family, and Wei Family. Even the Shen Family has to bow down to these three families. Among them, the Ye Family is the strongest, followed by the Wei Family. The Wen Family is slightly weaker than the Wei Family. Ever since Old Master Wei started making a name for himself, the family has been developing and expanding. They have contacts in every possible industry, and they’re involved in matters far more complicated than you can imagine. There are only two heirs in the Wei Family in Wei Qi’s generation. In other words, Wei Qi is likely to be taking over the Wei Family in future.”","Qiao Nian wasn’t the least bit interested in what he was saying. She was much more involved in the illegal businesses and forces and was not as aware of the scene in Beijing.","She narrowed her eyes and stood in a casual posture, with an air of rebellion around her. She looked at the man who was talking and stretched her patience. “So?”","Shen Jingyan couldn’t be saying all of this for nothing. He must have something to add, some subtext he was getting at.","Shen Jingyan didn’t expect her to be so calm. He pursed his lips for a while, not knowing how to go about talking to this version of Qiao Nian he knew.","“Nian Nian, what I’m trying to say is that some matters aren’t as simple as you make them out to be. You think that you’re fighting for justice for your friend, but you might just have rustled a beehive. You have the Jiang Family’s protection and will be safe. But do you think the Wei Family will let Chen Yuan off?”","His tone was still controlled and warm, but his words were much more cutting.","“His father is still in the hospital and his mother has to work at the stall every day. The circumstances of his family are prone to accidents, to begin with. If a flustered nurse accidentally gives his father the wrong type of medicine... all of these are possible occurrences.”","He didn’t want to come to such a juncture with Qiao Nian, and he wasn’t about to resort to these underhand means either. He was simply saying this because Qiao Nian was young and he wanted to scare her. It was easier to target her and to get Wei Qi’s documents from her rather than others.","His voice was casual and light, like an elder talking sense into a rebellious junior. He continued feigning kindness. “I know you have something about Wei Qi on hand, but you’ve heard what I said about the Wei Family’s power. Do you think that with their background, you’re really able to do anything by going through a legal proceeding?","“Would anyone in Rao City dare to take up your case?”","He felt increasingly relaxed as he spoke. He now leaned back in his seat and looked at the girl who had narrowed her eyes, evidently angered by him."]},{"number":540,"title":"Chapter 540 - You’re Not That Important Even to Me","paragraphs":["“Nian Nian, I’m not threatening you, I’m just sharing some important lessons with you. This world isn’t black-and-white, and not everything can be settled with the law. Even the sun doesn’t shine on every corner of the earth.”","He took a check out of his wallet and placed it on the table, then shifted it to Qiao Nian. He said calmly, “A million yuan is quite a sum. If we let things slide here, Chen Yuan doesn’t just receive a million yuan in compensation, his father will also get to have the best treatment in a hospital in Beijing. This transaction is a win for him. As for him... when he graduates, I will personally find him a company and ensure he lands a job. How’s that?”","This was not a negotiation, this was an option after a threat!","Qiao Nian’s dark eyes went cold. She initially already had her bag on her shoulder. At this point, she tossed her bag back onto the seat and chuckled, looking at him with her exquisite look.","Then, she said unkindly, “You guys can try us...”","After laughing, her cell phone buzzed again. Qiao Nian looked down and saw that Gu San had replied.","[Gu San: Miss Qiao, we’re already near where you are. I’ve parked the car by the roadside, and we’re waiting for you. Master Wang wants me to let you know you can take your time, there’s no rush (*?▽?*)]","After seeing the emoticon in the last line, some of the coldness faded from her eyes.","In the past, only Jiang Li and her dad would use this emoticon.","Now, even Gu San had learned to do the same.","Recently, the people around her loved to add these cute emoticons when messaging her. Even Shen Qingqing and the rest would do that in their texts.","Qiao Nian didn’t reply to the message. After glancing at her cell phone, she looked up at Shen Jingyan once again. Much of her ferocity had dispersed after the interrupting message came in, but her eyes were still cold and unfriendly. She didn’t want to say much more and simply left Shen Jingyan with a statement.","“You’re right that the world isn’t all black-and-white. But I believe that there is justice and fairness. However dark it may be, there will be light!”","That was why she liked this word.","Sun.","Light.","Sunlight.","Zhui Guang!","“I advise you not to think of targeting Aunt Chen and her family. I’m willing to let Wei Qi off on your account, but you aren’t that important even to me. At least, you’re not so important that the relationship we share can guarantee me letting Wei Qi off...”","Qiao Nian’s cap was pulled extremely low, and she appeared not to have much of an expression. Yet, Shen Jingyan felt a strange sense of oppression. It was almost suffocating.","He never realized how strong her presence was in the past.","This sort of aura.","He had never before experienced it in all his years in Beijing.","At this point, he felt that Qiao Chen couldn’t compare to Qiao Nian at all. She was negligible when placed next to her!","If not for the fact that he knew Qiao Nian didn’t make it to Qing University, he would really be doubting his choices now.","Qiao Nian had no idea what he was thinking. After suppressing her anger, she bent over and picked up her bag once again, slinging it on her shoulder. She had one hand in her pocket, looking casual but curt at the same time. “... If anything untoward happens to Aunt Chen or her family, Wei Qi will be suffering the same right after. Uncle Shen, I mean what I say!”","She was succinct and ruthless.","Shen Jingyan had lived the high life all these years and was respected, even revered, wherever he went. When had he ever had to deal with such directness?","—I’m willing to let Wei Qi off on your account, but you aren’t that important even to me!","—If anything untoward happens to Aunt Chen or her family, Wei Qi will be suffering the same right after.","At that moment, Shen Jingyan actually had no idea how to respond.","He was the one threatening Qiao Nian, why had the tables turned? Qiao Nian was now the one warning him!"]},{"number":541,"title":"Chapter 541 - Slapped in the Face","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","His eyes widened as he took the blow of Qiao Nian’s words. Qiao Nian was now saying in a distant manner, “Uncle Shen, if there’s nothing more, I’ll take my leave first. My friend’s waiting outside.”","Shen Jingyan’s muscles were all tense by now as he tried to force a smile. “Mm, alright.”","After all, he had experienced all sorts of situations. He managed to recover quickly and picked up the car keys on the table. He got up as well and asked, “Do you need me to send you there?”","Qiao Nian lowered her cap once again and declined his offer. “No need, they’re just nearby, I’ll go over on my own.”","He looked out and saw many cars on the wide road. He wasn’t sure which car Qiao Nian was referring to. Qiao Nian had gone to the bar counter to settle the tab and had left the cafeteria.","Only then did he fall back into his seat and sip on his coffee.","When he took a sip of this Blue Mountain previously, he did not find it bitter. But now, there was a taste that made it hard to swallow.","Shen Jingyan only took a small sip before putting it back down. He looked for his cell phone and scrolled through to find Wei Dongshan’s contact. There was a moment’s hesitation as he considered whether to call him to ask if he had figured out Qiao Nian’s relationship with Su Huaiyuan.","He had been in the business circle for so long, but this was the first time he had felt this lost and troubled. It was as if a huge hand was wrapped around his neck, suppressing him, leaving him with no good way of dealing with Wei Qi’s matters.","He was still hesitating.","Out of the blue, his cell phone rang.","Shen Jingyan saw the caller ID and frowned. He received the call and held the phone up. “Hello?”","He had just said a word and then listened to what the other party had to say. His expression changed, and he accidentally knocked over the cup of coffee on the table. Paleness took over his usually elegant look, and his expression practically crumbled. He clenched his teeth and squeezed out the words, “What did you say? Wei Qi has been taken away?”","He had just asked Qiao Nian out for a chat and threatened to hurt Chen Yuan’s family. The next moment, Wei Qi was taken away from the hospital.","Shen Jingyan had lived all these years, and this was the first time he was slapped in the face this way.","Hearing Wei Ling’s anxious voice, he took a deep breath to calm himself. Then, he quickly picked up his bag and said, “Wait for me, I’m coming right over.”","...","A black Phaeton was parked right outside First High School.","The school day had ended early for some of them, and a few students were walking out the gate. A couple of them would look over curiously every now and then.","Ye Wangchuan was seated leisurely in the backseat. He had one arm rested on the window as his deep eyes looked out.","Gu San had drawn the window down as well. He stuck his head out to scan the surroundings, then said to the man in the back, “Master Wang, didn’t Miss Qiao say she’d take five minutes? It’s been almost 10 minutes, where is she?”","He was a bit worried about Qiao Nian. “Should I call her to ask where she is?”","“No need, wait a bit more.” Ye Wangchuan retracted his gaze. He took a packet of cigarettes from the drawer, took one out, and lit it.","A spark emerged, then he drew a slow and deep breath. The cigarette rested between his slender fingers. His eyes were dark and deep, like the unchartered waters, hiding currents beneath.","“Has Cai Gang replied to your message?”"]},{"number":542,"title":"Chapter 542 - Rising Through the Ranks","paragraphs":["He tapped the cigarette lightly as if asking a casual question.","Gu San immediately smiled. “He replied. He personally brought his men along to the hospital to get Wei Qi. That Wei Ling even tried to counter him. She called someone from Beijing and even Wei Dongshan in front of his face. Tsk, it was useless! Given what Miss Qiao has handed us, it would be too kind even if we were to ask for Wei Qi’s life in exchange. She has no idea what the situation really is now and thinks that she has the means to protect that heir. She shows off her prowess to Cai Gang, not knowing that you’re his backing...”","Wei Qi’s matter was neither big nor small. If Chen Yuan hadn’t known Miss Qiao, the Wei Family would probably have the final say in this. Chen Yuan would have no choice but to blame it on his luck.","But Wei Qi happened to be this unlucky. Chen Yuan knew Miss Qiao and was on good terms with her. In that case, how could Master Wang sit back and just watch it unfold?","Besides the fact that Wei Dongshan and Wei Ling were too arrogant for their liking, they had even gone as far as to cancel Miss Qiao’s student status. This spurred Master Wang’s desire to defend the vulnerable. Now, there was no way he could let Wei Qi off.","Gu San was definitely on Qiao Nian’s side and felt bad for her. He said gloatingly, “I heard that Miss Qiao broke three of Wei Qi’s ribs. Now that he’s landed in Cai Gang’s hands, I doubt he’ll recover any time soon.”","Upon mentioning Cai Gang, he said, “Actually, Cai Gang is a pretty smart guy. He doesn’t hold a high post, but he was able to do what he needed to. I heard that before we managed to get to Beijing, he was the one defending Miss Qiao and making sure that Wei Dongshan and Wei Ling wouldn’t have their way.”","Wei Ling was a ruthless lady. She wanted to get a statement out of Wei Qi’s hospitalization to land Miss Qiao in jail.","It would have been fine if she didn’t try to cause all this trouble behind their backs. Wei Qi might not have been in such a bad state. It was precisely because she made things difficult for Qiao Nian that Master Wang wouldn’t even consider letting Wei Qi recuperate in the hospital.","If Master Wang wouldn’t let it happen, what could Wei Qi do about it?","He had three broken ribs, and Cai Gang still got someone to get him out on a stretcher.","There really was no need for this!","“Liang Heng’s investigation outcomes are almost out. I think he’s being taken off his post...” Ye Wangchuan raised a brow and tapped the cigarette again, causing some ash to fall off the cigarette butt.","He spoke slowly, as if he was uninterested in the topic. He was too lazy to even straighten up from his seat. “Cai Gang did pretty well this time. It’d be just right for him to take over Liang Heng’s post.”","Gu San took a while to recall who Liang Heng was.","He grinned. “Alright, I’ll let him know later. He’ll surely be overjoyed to hear about it.”","He wasn’t exaggerating it at all. Although it looked like a tiny step up the ladder, the fact was that most people in Cai Gang’s position would never be able to take that step in their lifetime.","This time, Cai Gang went up a rung just like that.","What truly mattered was not the rise in ranks, but that he was now favored by Master Wang.","Most people would beg for this opportunity to be in Master Wang’s good books, but Cai Gang managed to do it this easily."]},{"number":543,"title":"Chapter 543 - Master Wang Took Advantage of the Situation","paragraphs":["While they were chatting, Qiao Nian walked over and opened the door. Happening to hear the last line, she raised her brow and asked casually, “Who’s going to be overjoyed?”","“Miss Qiao, you’re back?” Gu San had only just noticed her and explained awkwardly, “Master Wang and I were talking, I didn’t see you.”","Ye Wangchuan effortlessly and discreetly put the cigarette out. He tossed the pack back into the compartment and wound the window down for some ventilation.","Qiao Nian didn’t notice that he was smoking.","Upon hearing what Gu San said, she responded, “Mm, I’d told you that I’d take five minutes, but I got caught up. Did you wait long?”","“Nope.” Gu San looked at the time. It was just 10 minutes past the set time.","Qiao Nian was already in the car. She still remembered her question. “Who did you say was going to be overjoyed?”","“It’s just that...” The words Cai Gang were almost mentioned.","Just before the name came out of his mouth, Gu San suddenly recalled that Master Wang did not seem to want Miss Qiao to know about what he was doing for her.","“That what?” Qiao Nian was getting impatient.","“That...” Gu San almost bit his tongue. He really wanted to slap himself. Why did he have to talk so much? How was he going to salvage the situation now?","He had waited for Qiao Nian in the car for almost half an hour and should be feeling warm by now. But at this point, Gu San felt that he was perspiring cold sweat. His clothes were already damp with it.","“It’s just...”","Gu San stammered but couldn’t go on. He was on the verge of tears, but he knew that Master Wang wouldn’t allow him to speak the truth. He dared not mention Cai Gang’s name.","Qiao Nian was just asking casually and wasn’t paying much attention. But seeing how nervous he looked now, she turned to look at the man beside her.","“Do you know who Gu San is talking about?”","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were deep. His usual cold jawline had softened from the moment Qiao Nian hopped on. Hearing her question, he looked up at the man in the front seat evidently begging for help. Then, he said calmly, “No idea, I wasn’t listening.”","Gu San was speechless.","Master Wang, I don’t know if I’m human, but I’m sure you’re a dog!!!","“Oh.” Qiao Nian knew that he was usually laid-back and hardly recalled the trivial matters. It was completely sensible that he was not listening carefully to what Gu San had said. She didn’t think too much about it.","After a burst of cold sweat, Gu San racked his brain and found an answer. “I remember now. Miss Qiao, it’s me. I’m overjoyed.”","“?”","He calmed himself down and quickly summoned his excuse. “Remember that night when you gave to Master Wang a document? I thought about how it contained details about all the things Wei Qi had done, and I couldn’t help but feel happy about it. That’s why I told Master Wang I’m overjoyed...”","This reason was obviously too far-fetched. It didn’t make much sense.","Gu San himself knew that this lie was not well-thought-out. He held his breath for fear that Qiao Nian would probe further, then quickly changed the topic. “Oh, right. Miss Qiao, where did you get that stuff? It should have been difficult to have found out all of that.”","In the documents that Qiao Nian sent was an overseas transaction record. It wasn’t just anyone’s transaction record, but Wei Qi’s.","But the person who had transferred the money to him was an interesting figure.","It was an overseas fugitive drug lord.","This evidence was enough to send Wei Qi to hell. This was also why the infamous Wei Ying was doing all she could to get it back.","But what could she do? Wei Qi’s life was in Master Wang’s hands. Could she not surrender?"]},{"number":544,"title":"Chapter 544 - Why Not Rob a Bank","paragraphs":["He just couldn’t figure out where Qiao Nian got these confidential records from.","This wasn’t easy to get on hand.","If it really was easy, the Wei Family could have found out much earlier and eradicated all evidence.","Ye Wangchuan squinted and turned towards her slightly. He was still calm, apparently not at all surprised that Qiao Nian managed to get this stuff.","He remembered that Qiao Nian seemed to have some contact with the Red Alliance. But he hadn’t figured out the depth of the relationship.","He knew that, but Gu San did not. Gu San only knew that Qiao Nian was medically skilled and had sold a coveted drug on the black market.","Gu San scratched his head and verbalized the question that had been on his mind. “Miss Qiao, do you know a very skilled hacker or something?”","This was definitely obtained by a hacker, not an ordinary person.","He asked her so intently, there was no way Qiao Nian could evade his question.","She wasn’t flustered or anxious in any way. In fact, she looked confident as she said, “Oh, that. I bought it.”","“Bought it?” Gu San was confused.","Ye Wangchuan also raised his brow, completely speechless.","Gu San then asked, “Where from?”","“No, wait, you can buy this stuff? Who sells them?”","With two pairs of eyes on her all of a sudden, Qiao Nian still managed to keep her composure. Her dark eyes were still. She took a chewing gum bottle out of her bag and, in front of Gu San, took a white pill out and ate it.","She then responded indifferently, “The Red Alliance.”","Gu San watched how she just casually swallowed a pill that was now impossible to get hold of even on the black market. He could barely react.","He then heard her mention the Red Alliance, and his mind went blank. It stopped processing for a moment.","“Miss Qiao, you bought Wei Qi’s transaction records from the Red Alliance?”","Qiao Nian chewed on the pill, but her face was still slightly pale. Her fair skin appeared almost translucent at this point, and her lips were also rather colorless. She leaned back in her seat with her hand on her stomach. Given how casual her postures usually were, it wasn’t anything out of the ordinary that she was just resting her hand there.","“Yes.”","“... So it really is the Red Alliance.”","Gu San drew a sharp breath when he heard her confirmation. He intuitively turned to look at the man sitting behind him and asked a little dejectedly, “Master Wang, why did the Red Alliance ignore us? Did we not give them enough money?”","Ye Wangchuan had also gotten the Red Alliance to investigate some illegal goods, but they hadn’t taken up the job.","They had thought that the Red Alliance had certain regulations and did not want to take up anything that involved illegal business. But now it seemed like... they probably just had not offered them enough?","Gu San wasn’t surprised that Qiao Nian knew of the Red Alliance’s existence. After all, the Red Alliance had a strong presence in both the legal and illegal businesses. Since Qiao Nian was able to sell her pills in the black market, she surely knew some friends who belonged in the “grey area” and had channels to request for a mission to the Red Alliance. But he hadn’t expected the Red Alliance to take up a job like hers, which was so “trivial”.","After all, getting the Red Alliance to investigate someone like Wei Qi was a bit of an overkill.","He was thinking about this while driving, and he couldn’t stop going on about their request. “We did give them a good offer just to check something out. It’s an eight-figure sum, is that not enough? Why don’t they rob a bank instead?”","Qiao Nian leaned back and thought about how she had gotten them to buy Uncle Chen some rare goods in the past. They had topped up the amount about seven to eight times, and the eventual amount was a nine-figure sum. Slim Waist Control had scolded them the same way.","Why don’t they rob a bank instead?","Gee.","She almost retorted in the same way Daji did back then: [It’s much faster robbing a big boss than robbing a bank, and you don’t have to serve time for that.]","This was such an appropriate time to make this statement!"]},{"number":545,"title":"Chapter 545 - Master Wang Is Spoiling Her","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","He was looking for the Red Alliance to help him check on something?","What did he want to check?","Qiao Nian bent her legs and leaned obliquely, glancing at the people around her. Ye Wangchuan had been busy the past couple of days and did not get any sleep last night, so he had eye bags under his eyes. It seemed like his bloodthirsty aura was heavier than usual.","Qiao Nian turned away after a quick glance. Then, she slowly took out her cell phone and unconsciously opened up the chat with the Red Alliance.","The red letter ‘S’ was particularly conspicuous on her cell phone screen.","However, Ye Wangchuan did not look her way. Rubbing his eyebrows and eyes with one hand, he touched his thin lips with the other hand and said, “Stop by the supermarket along the way. I want to buy something.”","Gu San hesitated, looked aside, and asked him strangely, “Master Wang, what are you planning to buy so late in the evening? Let me go buy it for you.”","Just as he said this, he passed by a supermarket.","He parked his car along the side of the road and turned his head around. He stretched out his hand to unbuckle his seatbelt and said, “Master Wang, please remain in the car. Let me go buy it.”","Ye Wangchuan’s slender hand opened the door and stopped him, saying, “I’ll go by myself. Please wait a while.”","Qiao Nian muttered an agreement softly. She felt unwell and was curled up lazily in the corner. She didn’t stop him.","Although Gu San wanted to go with him, he was worried about leaving Qiao Nian alone in the car. Thus, he gave up on the idea of following him.","He asked briefly, “What are you planning to buy, Master Wang? Are you going to get some gum?”","He wasn’t guessing blindly.","Master Wang was smoking just now. When Miss Qiao got in the car, he put out the cigarette butt and threw it away. However, it would still be possible for Miss Qiao to smell the smoke on him. Therefore, it was possible that Master Wang was going to get some gum to hide the smoke smell on him.","Qiao Nian didn’t think too deeply about this as she picked at the tip of her eyebrows. She just wondered why Ye Wangchuan wanted chewing gum.","The tall figure quickly returned to the car.","Tall and long-legged, he stood out from the crowd when he walked along the street. Qiao Nian noticed several girls looking at him.","He returned very quickly.","Holding on to a plastic bag, he handed its content to her after he got into the car—some medicine he had bought for her.","“Eat the medicine. The drugstore clerk said that after eating this medicine, your stomach will no longer hurt after half an hour.”","He then handed her a drink. His eyebrows and eyes were looking down, looking very handsome.","“Eat the medicine together with this drink.”","Qiao Nian took the medicine with complex eyes. She looked down and saw that he had bought a medicine called Fenbid.","Furthermore, she could feel the warmth of the drink through the paper cup. It was very warm, even warmer than the actual temperature of the drink itself.","She held onto her cup and was not able to voice out her inner feelings. In a deep voice, she said, “You went just to buy these for me?”","“Yes. You’re suffering from an upset stomach, right?”","Ye Wangchuan looked at the pale and distressed face in front of him and stuffed the black plastic bag into her arms. He spoke slowly, and his voice was very provocative. A smile seemed to tug at the corners of his eyes. “I bought some other stuff too. I didn’t know which brands you prefer, so I asked the clerk and bought you these two bags. The clerk recommended these brands.”","Gu San was lost in his thoughts while listening to their conversation and almost blurted out a question.","Out of the corner of his eye, he saw the black plastic bag that Ye Wangchuan had passed to Qiao Nian. He recognized the brand of the product inside the bag. He had seen the packaging on television commercials every day.","His face suddenly turned red.","Oh my goodness, it was a product from the Sophie brand?","Master Wang went down to buy sanitary pads for Miss Qiao?","He took another look at Qiao Nian’s pale face and lips, and it became obvious what kind of medicine Qiao Nian was holding.","It was definitely medicine used by girls on their period!"]},{"number":546,"title":"Chapter 546 - It Would Only Be About Three to Five Years if You Are Sentenced Now","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Qiao Nian felt a little drowsy after taking the medicine and drinking half a cup of warm milk. In addition, Gu San was driving the car very smoothly. She closed her eyes slightly and soon fell asleep in the back of the car.","She didn’t see her phone screen light up.","Ye Wangchuan saw it. It seemed like Uncle Shen was trying to contact her.","There were usually not many people around her. Besides her classmates, Yuan Yongqin, and Su Huaiyuan, there was only one other person with the surname Shen.","Shen Jingyan.","Ye Wangchuan picked up her cell phone, lowered his eyes, and pressed on the shutdown button. After pressing the button for a while, the screen stopped flashing and went completely black.","He put the cell phone back to where it was, took off his coat, and gently put it on Qiao Nian. He then said to Gu San in the front seat, “Drive slower. Make a detour before going back.”","Gu San looked in the rearview mirror and saw that Qiao Nian was sleeping. She rarely fell asleep in the car. Without further explanation, he nodded, lowered his voice, and said, “Okay. I’ll drive around this road twice. This will give Miss Qiao a little more time to sleep.”","Ye Wangchuan looked at Qiao Nian’s sleeping face and thought of something. Suddenly, he said with a lazy tone, “Tell Cai Gang to convey this message to everyone. If Wei Qi is sentenced now, he will face a maximum of about three to five years in prison. However, if he decides to drag this out and waste more time, he may be looking at a lifetime behind bars.”","Gu San guessed that he was probably feeling unhappy. He nodded. Without hesitation, he called Cai Gang and conveyed Ye Wangchuan’s message through a Bluetooth headset.","...","Outside the provincial hospital.","Shen Jingyan and Wei Ling were at the hospital. Even Wei Dongshan and Qiao Weimin had hurried over.","Wei Ling had a sullen face and sat there looking very unpleasant. Needless to say, it was because Cai Gang had released the person right in front of her, not giving her any face. He had trampled over her and the Wei Family’s pride.","Shen Jingyan was outside making a call and had not come in for the time being.","Wei Dongshan had just arrived. When he heard that Wei Qi had been taken away, his heart jumped and he frowned. He said, “We may have messed with the wrong person this time.","“Why don’t we just let this matter go? If you keep hounding after Qiao Nian, you don’t know what will happen. We also don’t know who is backing her. She’s so evil...”","“How can we just let this go? Wei Qi would have broken three ribs for nothing!” Wei Ling asked angrily. She couldn’t accept his solution and wouldn’t listen to his persuasion.","She clenched her fist and teeth hard and said, “I still hold some leeway over her and Chen Yuan with the punishment. Even if she has enough influence to make Cai Gang bring them away, I don’t believe she has the ability to resolve everything by herself! Unless she’s willing to forego the College Entrance Examination, we shall see who wins in the end!”","She was blinded by anger and speaking recklessly.","In her heart, there was no comparison. Between Qiao Nian being unable to go to college and her spoiled brother being locked up in the police station, there was no question as to which was more important.","She was so angry she felt like she could kill Qiao Nian right now. But even if she did, it wouldn’t appease a tenth of her anger.","Qiao Chen had also followed Qiao Weimin here. She didn’t know what had happened. However, seeing Wei Ling so angry while mentioning Qiao Nian’s name, she had a feeling it was related to Qiao Nian beating up Wei Qi.","She was in a bad mood after being embarrassed in front of her classmates in the gathering. However, she suddenly felt better. She obediently went forward and tried to persuade Wei Ling. “Aunt, please don’t be angry anymore. What good will come out of it?”","She paused for a moment, looked out, took Wei Ling’s arm, and said softly, “Uncle is here.. He’ll definitely have a solution for this problem.”"]},{"number":547,"title":"Chapter 547 - They Could Only Apologize","paragraphs":["Wei Ling was upset and did not pay any attention to her.","At that moment, Shen Jingyan, who had been making a call outside, came back into the room.","Looking dignified, he looked over at Wei Ling and Qiao Chen. His gaze finally landed on Wei Dongshan and he said, “Wei Dongshan, can you find a way to take back the punishment meted out to Qiao Nian and Chen Yuan?”","“What are you saying? Why do we have to take back the punishment?” Wei Ling instinctively stood up in disagreement before she fully understood the situation.","Shen Jingyan felt annoyed when he thought about the call he had just received. In addition, he saw Wei Ling’s stubborn face, which seemed adamant on punishing Qiao Nian.","He spoke to her very directly. “Wei Qi is at the police station, right? I’ll drive us there later to pick him up. We will bring him over to apologize to Chen Yuan.”","Wei Ling was speechless. She felt wronged and looked stunned.","Shen Jingyan ignored her and spoke quickly and steadily. “Before we go to see Chen Yuan, let’s go to the mall to buy some nutritional supplements for him. Be sure to be considerate towards him. With regards to Wei Qi, I will tell him that we have made a sincere apology. I have also prepared a check of three million yuan for them. Let’s hope they will accept it.”","When he told Qiao Nian that he would give Chen Yuan one million yuan, he was condescending about it.","But this time, he was worried that Chen Yuan wouldn’t accept the three million yuan.","This was a huge change in attitude.","Shen Jingyan was still worried after he finished speaking. He raised his eyes and looked at Qiao Weimin. He was also confused and had not fully understood the situation. His dark eyes flashed. His tone was unusually gentle as he said, “Brother-in-law, you’re familiar with the Chen Family. Please come with us later and help us persuade Chen Yuan to stop arguing with Wei Qi. Regarding Chen Yuan’s loss, we will definitely find a way to make it up to him. Let’s try to put this whole matter behind us!”","“Hmm.” Qiao Weimin didn’t sleep well last night. He was still thinking about the matter between Chen Yuan and Wei Qi. Furthermore, Wei Qi had been beaten up and even sent to the hospital. He was afraid that this matter wouldn’t end well. He never expected Shen Jingyan to say this. He was stunned for a long time before speaking mechanically. “Okay.”","After speaking so much, he looked over at Wei Ling again. She looked like she was about to burst out in anger again. He rubbed his forehead and looked helpless, then spoke in an aggravated tone. “This is also what Mother-in-law wants!”","“This is what my Mom wants?” Wei Ling couldn’t believe what she was hearing. “How could that be possible?”","“Take a look at this first.” He handed the thing he got from Beijing that afternoon over to Wei Ling.","When Wei Ling finished reading it, her face turned pale. She couldn’t believe her eyes.","Wei Qi actually did something so terrible.","He even let someone get a hold of evidence regarding this matter!","Shen Jingyan saw that her expression had changed and continued in a deep voice, “Cai Gang called me a few minutes ago and told me that Wei Qi will be in prison for at least three years because of what he did this time. If we keep pestering them, he may face up to a lifetime in prison. Now, there’s only one option left for us—apologize!”","He had never thought of threatening Qiao Nian before. He wanted to let this matter slowly resolve itself after some time.","Who could have expected Ye Wangchuan to interfere?","His words had influence.","If they were still unwilling to admit their mistakes, Wei Qi would be left completely to the law, and no mercy would have been given. They wouldn’t be able to expect any kindness from him!","What else could they do?","They could only follow Qiao Nian’s demands. She wanted them to make Wei Qi apologize to Chen Yuan and erase the punishment meted out to him.","Shen Jingyan had a splitting headache, and his heart felt like it was falling into a bottomless pit. He didn’t know how much he could help even after doing so much."]},{"number":548,"title":"Chapter 548 - This Was a Habit of Someone at the Top","paragraphs":["“In short, we can only take this matter one step at a time. We’ll go to apologize to the Chen family first and see if they’re willing to forgive us. If they’re unwilling, then we have no choice but to find another way.”","Wei Ling was still stunned and couldn’t speak. Her face was as white as a piece of paper, still holding the document Shen Jingyan had given her earlier. Her throat felt like it was blocked, and she couldn’t say a word.","Before seeing this document, she was still arrogant and confident. She wasn’t afraid to stand up against Qiao Nian. Even if she got in trouble, she still wanted to teach Qiao Nian a lesson.","However, she now understood the situation clearly. Qiao Nian had something against Wei Qi. This evidence was enough to ruin Wei Qi’s life. Moreover, they made it very clear. If they apologized sincerely now, Wei Qi would only face up to five years in prison. However, if they decided to continue fighting against them and pestering them about Qiao Nian beating him up, Wei Qi would spend the rest of his life in prison.","Wei Ling clenched her jaw tightly. She hated that she didn’t have a choice in this matter. She felt powerless.","She could continue to fight against this decision. However, even if the court ruled that Qiao Nian beat Wei Qi up for no reason, the punishment wouldn’t be severe as the medical records showed that Wei Qi was only slightly injured.","Furthermore, Qiao Nian had only just turned 18. She was still considered a student.","Under such circumstances, the court wouldn’t punish her too severely.","At the most, she would only face a fine. Qiao Nian would also have to be locked up in the detention center for about three to five days and receive counseling.","On the other hand, her brother would have to pay a heavy price.","She couldn’t afford to risk it. She hated Qiao Nian so much that she couldn’t help clenching her jaw. Even so, she didn’t dare to gamble with her brother’s life!","Shen Jingyan was aware of her temperament. He knew she was from a very influential family. She had spent most of her life looking down on people and acting arrogantly. She had also never suffered a loss before. It was because he understood his wife’s character so well that he set his eyes on her again and said with a serious expression, “Wei Ling, this is Wei Qi’s last chance. When we see Chen Yuan later, you must look out for your attitude. Don’t blow this matter up even more. Wei Qi will be the one on the losing end. He’s still young. Do you want him to spend the rest of his life in prison?”","Wei Ling’s face was pale. She was speechless.","“Hey, actually, Nian Nian is also not a stranger to us. Didn’t you like her very much before? Although it’s wrong that she beat Wei Qi, you were also a little too impulsive. You immediately went to look for Dongshan to cancel her student status. You should have tried to understand why she beat him up first. She’s not the kind of child who would beat someone up for no reason.”","Although he spoke casually, after the incident, he didn’t bother to find out the reason why Qiao Nian beat Wei Qi up.","He thought the same way as Wei Ling. There was no reason or excuse that could pardon you if you beat someone up.","Qiao Nian had beat Wei Qi up. She must pay the price for this.","She had to pay the price, regardless of what Wei Qi did.","Some people were just born different. Even if they did something wrong, it could be due to their young age and naivety. They were merely ignorant. Anyone who came across them would just consider themselves unlucky. Even if they came after them, it would just seem as though they were trying to hit a stone with an egg. The only person who would be losing out would be themselves!","In the past, when Wei Qi used to be a bully in Beijing, they would always help to clean up his messes. This was also why Wei Qi had this mentality.","In addition, they handled this matter just like how they used to do it.","Who would expect that they would face a loss this time!","They hurt themselves badly!","Shen Jingyan’s expression was cold and hard, and his eyes were clear. He had the mentality of a businessman. There were no feelings, only thoughts of gains and losses in his eyes.","“It’s our loss this time. We must be more careful next time.”"]},{"number":549,"title":"Chapter 549 - Trying to Stir Up Trouble for Sister Nian","paragraphs":["“As for Wei Qi, we can just let him be sent to prison for three to five years. He can take it as a lesson. Otherwise, he will never learn how much trouble he’s always causing us! When the Old Master was still in power, people would always give us some face. Now, the Old Master is critically ill and we have yet to find a suitable doctor to operate on him. The Wei Family is in a mess, and Wei Lou is also back. If he causes trouble now, he’ll definitely be caught by your uncle and his family.”","As he was speaking, he put his cell phone at the head of the bed. Then, with a stern face, he said, “If he manages to learn to be a better person in prison, he will still have the chance to lead the Wei Family in the future. Looking at how he does things now, you cannot expect him to lead the family properly.”","His marriage with Wei Ling was originally an alliance between two strong families, whether it was emotionally or intellectually. He certainly hoped that the person to inherit the Wei Family would be his brother-in-law.","That way, the Shen Family could also continue to rise in power alongside them.","He patted Wei Ling’s shoulder and comforted her. “Don’t think too much about this. Maybe this could be a good thing for Wei Qi. He’s not young anymore. He can’t keep relying on us whenever he runs into trouble.”","Although he was saying this on the outside, he felt annoyed on the inside. He couldn’t understand how unlucky his useless brother-in-law was. He actually managed to provoke the Ye family twice in a row.","According to seniority, he was Ye Wangchuan’s elder. Ye Wangchuan should address him as an elder.","However, in reality, everyone in Beijing knew of the Young Master from the Ye family. He had an extraordinary ability from a young age and had a lot of influence and contacts.","Even though Ye Wangchuan was only in his early twenties, no one from the older generation in Beijing dared to refer to their seniority in front of him.","If Ye Wangchuan hadn’t interfered, Wei Qi would also have been left with more options!","Wei Ling covered her face. She still couldn’t accept the possibility of Wei Qi going to prison for three to five years. Her eyes were red and she wanted to cry, but her self-esteem did not allow her to expose her vulnerable side in front of so many people.","Qiao Chen had been standing by the side and listening to their conversation the whole time. The more she listened, the more confused she got. Even if Wei Ling and Shen Jingyan were speaking implicitly, they didn’t divulge the full story. She could only understand about half of the conversation.","Qiao Nian had found a backer, and the matter regarding her beating up Wei Qi will be put to rest!","Qiao Chen bit her lips reluctantly. Her eyes twinkled as she said, “Did Qiao Nian not beat up someone?”","That was right. It was Qiao Nian who beat up her brother. However, it was her brother who would be going to jail now. How could this be reasonable!","Wei Ling felt as though her heart was being stabbed. Feeling uncomfortable, she raised her head and looked at Qiao Chen.","In fact, Qiao Chen was a little afraid of her gaze. However, she didn’t want Qiao Nian to get away so easily. Thus, she stood her ground. She bit her lip and shrunk her neck. Her heart pounding, she said, “Why are we the ones apologizing when she was the one who beat up Wei Qi? Aunt Wei Ling, is there a mistake? I thought the Wei Family was very powerful. How can we just let Qiao Nian go so easily? We must at least punish her for this.”","Wei Ling couldn’t tell her what Wei Qi had done. Instead, she tried to change the subject. She looked at Qiao Chen deeply and asked thoughtlessly, “By the way, Chen Chen, Your mom is planning to invite your friends and relatives over for a feast to celebrate your admission into Qing University, right?”","Qiao Chen didn’t expect the conversation to suddenly switch from Qiao Nian to herself. How did the conversation become about her? Although she didn’t know why Wei Ling changed the subject, she still obediently nodded her head.","“Yes. After all, I made it into Qing University. My mom wants to celebrate this achievement.”"]},{"number":550,"title":"Chapter 550 - This Is Master Nies Last Disciple","paragraphs":["She didn’t know why Wei Ling suddenly brought this up. Her heart was in a mess.","Wei Ling’s indignant expression was gradually replaced by hatred. Her face was cold as she stood up and adjusted her fox fur shawl. She pursed her lips and said, “You should celebrate your success. How about this? I’ll invite Professor Cheng over for a meal. You have to learn finance from him in the future and build a good relationship with him. It’ll help you in the future.”","Qiao Chen looked up and was stunned for half a second. When she realized what she had said, she was immediately overjoyed and said, “Thank you, Aunt!”","“Okay.” Wei Ling used to look down on her flattering and ingratiating face. Ever since she experienced this, she felt that her obedient and delicate appearance was much better than some people’s arrogant and domineering faces. At least, she did not bite.","At this thought, she raised her chin slightly and looked at the surprised girl. “There’s something else I didn’t have time to tell you.”","Qiao Chen stood there obediently and turned her head to ask gently, “What is it, Aunt?”","Wei Ling glanced at her from the corner of her eye and saw that she had specially dressed up today. She was wearing branded clothes and had delicate features. Although she wasn’t as exquisite and brash as Qiao Nian, she at least had the look of a daughter from a prestigious family.","Not keeping her in suspense, she said concisely, “Last time, Beijing Television Station planned a music science program, and the results were very good. I heard that they intend to hold a concert. At that time, Zhui Guang will also go. If you can beat Zhui Guang in piano skills, Master Nie will definitely look at you in a different light.”","She stared at Qiao Chen as if she could see through her soul. Her lips curled into a mocking smile as she adjusted her clothes and said casually, “Don’t you want to acknowledge Master Nie as your master? This is the best opportunity. Practice the piano properly when you get back. I’ll try my best to string you up!”","“...” Qiao Chen clenched her fists. She couldn’t believe that such a good thing would happen to her.","Wei Ling’s expression was cold. “Why? You don’t want to participate?","“The Piano Association has only two slots for this concert. According to the rules, you aren’t qualified to take one. You’ll be going through the back door. If you’re unwilling, then forget it.”","How could Qiao Chen not be willing? When she heard her unhappy tone, she hurriedly expressed her stance. “I’m willing! Aunt, I’m willing!","“I was just too excited and didn’t react in time, so I didn’t answer you immediately.” Qiao Chen restrained the ambition and excitement in her eyes, bit her lip, and said softly, “Aunt, I want to participate...”","Seeing that she was in a hurry to explain herself, Wei Ling pursed her lips and looked down at her. Her tone was cold. “It’s good that you want to participate. When the time comes, I’ll leave a spot in the association for you. Prepare yourself. Don’t disappoint me!”","She didn’t think much of Qiao Chen, nor did she think that her talent would bring her much fortune.","But she hated Qiao Nian.","There was an old saying: the enemy of your enemy is your friend.","Qiao Nian didn’t like Qiao Chen and loved to compare herself with her, right?","If that was the case, she would insist on praising Qiao Chen to the heavens, to a height that Qiao Nian couldn’t reach even if she jumped!","Master Nie’s last disciple was at this height!","...","On the other side.","On the second floor of the villa.","Qiao Nian returned to her room the moment she arrived. She had just taken a shower and changed into a clean set of clothes. When she walked out of the bathroom, she saw the screen of her cell phone on the bed flash."]},{"number":551,"title":"Chapter 551 - Sister Nian Is Not Going Where They Wish to Go","paragraphs":["She secured her hair with the towel in frustration and walked over. Then, she bent down, picked up her phone, and unlocked it.","She received a message.","She held her phone in one hand and leaned on one side to click on the message.","It was from Nie Mi.","It was a long message. He roughly told her that not long after, a very high-level concert would be held in Rao City. He would be attending it as a guest. He had a spot in his hands. The organizer wanted him to give her the spot because the VCR she had helped to film last time was very effective. They wanted her to participate. After Nie Mi thought about it, he also wanted her to go...","Qiao Nian read the message patiently and opened the invitation attached to the message.","On the gold-plated invitation, the other party had written it sincerely, hoping to invite [Zhui Guang] to the scene.","Qiao Nian was no longer interested after just one glance. She clicked away immediately, her slender and fair hand holding her phone. She didn’t even see what she was typing before she replied in a few seconds.","...","Beijing.","Wen Ruxia was drinking tea with an old man in a traditional Chinese suit. After her assistant gently brought hot water, she quietly went out. Throughout the entire process, she held her breath and did not dare to look around.","Halfway through, the elder’s phone suddenly rang.","Seeming relaxed and not seeming to care about anything, the old man suddenly seemed to have become a different person. He stopped drinking his tea and immediately picked up his phone by the table.","Nie Mi was really nervous, and his heart was in his mouth. He couldn’t wait to open Qiao Nian’s message.","[QN: No.]","It was obvious at a glance.","Compared to the 180-word message he had sent, she was too heartless!","Wen Ruxia didn’t know what was written on the message, but she could guess from his grave expression. She picked up her teacup and took a sip of tea. Smiling unhurriedly, she said, “Master Nie, what did Zhui Guang say? She’s not coming?”","Although in the eyes of outsiders, with Master Nie’s status in the music industry, there shouldn’t be anyone who wouldn’t give him face if he invited a newcomer to the concert, she was lucky to have seen that Zhui Guang through a video.","She was young, looking to be only 18 years old. She might still be studying, but her aura was definitely not that of an ordinary person.","How should she describe that big boss?","The thing that left the deepest impression was her overly beautiful face.","Then, there was the calmness and banditry in her eyes.","She remembered that the other party had introduced traditional music and kowtowing. Her tone was neither slow nor slow, but it was like a cool breeze blowing past, making one feel comfortable.","Few young people were this calm nowadays.","Although she had yet to see Zhui Guang in person, Wen Ruxia felt that she wasn’t the kind of person who pursued fame and fortune.","After all, with the name “Zhui Guang,” and the current traffic and popularity...","Putting everything else aside, being in the entertainment industry was just a casual matter.","Plus that face...","The girl’s overly beautiful face appeared in Wen Ruxia’s mind again. She couldn’t help but think of her silly nephew.","The two of them seemed to be about the same age.","She stopped at the thought.","She felt quite regretful.","If it was an ordinary family, that beautiful and talented young lady would be more than enough to be Wen Ziyu’s girlfriend.","Unfortunately, the Wen Family wasn’t ordinary. No matter how carefree they were, they still had certain requirements for a daughter-in-law.","That girl was not bad, but she wasn’t worthy of Wen Ziyu."]},{"number":552,"title":"Chapter 552 - Veteran Zhui Guangs Name Is QN","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Nie Mi didn’t know what she was thinking. If he knew, he might not even drink his tea and just leave.","At this moment, his mind was filled with Qiao Nian’s reply. He said without looking up, “She definitely doesn’t want to come with her dog-like temper. It’s fine. I’ll ask her again.”","Wen Ruxia picked up her teacup and looked at the tea leaves floating in the cup. Dressed in a shirt and a professional suit, she looked smart and experienced. She smiled and said, “Only Zhui Guang can make you ask a second time. If it were anyone else, they would have agreed long ago, afraid that you’d change your mind!”","“Sigh!” Unwilling to give up, Nie Mi sent a few more messages to bomb Qian Nian. Then, he looked up and said seriously, “She’s different.”","Stunned, Wen Ruxia was about to ask him what was wrong.","At this moment, Nie Mi’s phone flashed again. Wen Ruxia saw a new reply from the corner of her eye.","[QN: I’m not interested.]","QN?","Wen Ruxia was in a daze. She lowered her eyelashes and took a sip of tea.","The big boss’ name was QN?","Why did this abbreviation sound so familiar? Recently, the girl that Wen Ziyu often mentioned seemed to have the same initials.","What was that girl’s name again?","She took a sip of tea and thought for a moment before remembering.","Qiao Nian!","Yes, Wen Ziyu had been telling her recently that there was a genius in this year’s joint examination at Qing University. She had scored full marks in the joint examination, 650 points. She was beautiful and had a good personality. Her name was Qiao Nian, and she was also studying in Rao City in her third year of high school this year.","Master Nie had sent a message to Zhui Guang. The legendary mysterious and hidden Zhui Guang’s nickname was also QN.","At first glance, there seemed to be an astonishing coincidence between the two.","However, after swallowing the tea in her mouth, she put down the cup unhurriedly. Her charming and capable face wasn’t moved at all. In the blink of an eye, she threw this coincidence to the back of her mind.","She had seen Zhui Guang’s face through the VCR. She was young and brash, and she didn’t seem like a disciplined student. She was quite a gangster.","Such people usually didn’t study well.","Moreover, she played underground music and rock. She didn’t think that she could take into account her good grades at the same time.","Wen Ruxia retracted the light in her eyes and smiled slightly. She said to the elder sitting opposite her regretfully and helplessly, “Sigh, I originally wanted to invite Zhui Guang to participate. If she could participate, traditional music would shine again this time. Unfortunately, she’s unwilling...”","It was within her expectations that Zhui Guang would decline.","After all, the most mysterious existence among the young musicians had always done as she pleased. Even if the standard of the normal concert organized by her this time was very high, other than experts like Master Nie in the country, pianists like Stephen would also come from overseas. It could be said that this was a good opportunity for a youngster to stand out and earn a reputation. This kind of opportunity was different from ordinary television opportunities. The levels were different, and the circle was also different!","It was a pity that Zhui Guang refused to come.","Nie Mi couldn’t do anything about Qiao Nian’s temper. When he saw her reply, he frowned and didn’t even want to drink tea anymore. He stood up and said, “Wait for me. I’ll make a call.”","Wen Ruxia leaned back in her chair and smiled very politely. “As you wish, Master Nie.”","“Okay.” Nie Mi was still thinking about something, so he didn’t stand on ceremony with her.","He took his phone and left in a hurry."]},{"number":553,"title":"Chapter 553 - She Knew He Was Acting Pitiful","paragraphs":["On the other hand, Qiao Nian had just put down her phone and pulled out a chair, preparing to turn on her computer, when Nie Mi called her.","Her eyebrows were restrained as she picked up the call irritably. She had just finished her shower and her voice was low. “Hello.”","“Nian Nian, are you busy?”","Nie Mi’s voice came through the phone.","Qiao Nian glanced at her computer, which had just been switched on. She placed her hand on her forehead and walked to the side to answer his call. “No. What’s the matter?”","Nie Mi didn’t like to beat around the bush. He said bluntly, “I want to tell you about the concert.”","Qiao Nian wasn’t interested. However, out of courtesy, she controlled her temper and said, “Oh, tell me.”","Nie Mi immediately started promoting the grand event that was going to be held in Rao City.","“The level of this concert is very high. Apart from me, the Wen Family has also invited many masters from the music industry domestically and overseas. You can get to know a lot of people. Also, this is a very good opportunity to promote traditional music. With your standards, you will definitely amaze the entire audience. When the time comes...”","Qiao Nian had been listening to him patiently. But when she heard this, she interrupted him in frustration. “I’m not interested.”","She had never liked crowded places, not to mention such places as Nie Mi had mentioned. Therefore, she was even less interested.","She wasn’t Qiao Chen, who liked to show off in crowded places.","If she could choose, she would rather sleep in her room and play games to relax if she had time, rather than attend the concert.","She didn’t want to show off in that kind of setting, either.","Nie Mi knew she would say that. Before making the call, he had already thought of a countermeasure. His voice immediately softened. “You really don’t want to go?","“This is a rare opportunity. Not many people in the country have a spot. I originally thought that if you wanted to go, I would go with you.”","Qiao Nian lowered her eyes, not interested. “I don’t want to go.”","A direct refusal.","He didn’t even have a chance to persuade her.","Nie Mi felt stifled. The level of this concert was clearly very good, and many people were not qualified to go even if they wanted to. Why was it the other way around when it was his turn? It was him begging her to go, but she had refused.","He said gloomily in a low voice, “...Why don’t you reconsider? This is really a good opportunity. It’s fine even if you go. I’ve asked the person who led the exchange, and she promised me that not many people will attend. It’ll be considered a private gathering. She’ll lead the way and let the Midwestern Music Competition be held. You know, it’s easy to find students from Western Music. There are many of them. They’re all good seedlings who study the piano and the violin. But it’s difficult for us with traditional instruments!”","“Didn’t others learn traditional music?” She had seen many people playing traditional music on the video website.","“There definitely are, but too few people can spar with others at this level. No one will be able to show off when the time comes. I can represent my generation, but I don’t want others to think that I’m the only one who can do it. In a hundred years, the skills behind this instrument will be lost and it will be my fault...”","Hearing his depressed words, Qiao Nian knew that he was pretending to be pitiful, but she still couldn’t help but rub her forehead and say, “I might not have the time.”","Nie Mi heard her tone soften, and she didn’t reject him as firmly as before."]},{"number":554,"title":"Chapter 554 - Sister Nian Will Definitely Get First","paragraphs":["He immediately continued, “It’s okay. I’ll leave this spot here first. If you go, I’ll go with you. If you don’t, I won’t go either.”","He wasn’t saying this out of anger or threatening Qiao Nian.","He spoke the truth.","The level of this concert was extremely high. When the time came, even foreign pianists like Stephen would come.","They were all outstanding young musicians.","However, he didn’t have a successor whom he could bring out. Not to mention anything else, he wasn’t afraid of losing face for himself. However, he didn’t want people both domestically and internationally to think that only the older generation was playing traditional instruments like konghou in the country. He didn’t want others to think he was the only one who was still struggling to support the industry as an elder. After a hundred years, those national essences whose ancestors had been passed down for a thousand years would be buried with them!","The only person in the younger generation who could represent them to participate in such a high-class concert and make traditional instruments shine was only one person—Qiao Nian!","If she was unwilling to go, there was no need for him to participate.","“...” Qiao Nian didn’t expect him to say this. She felt an inexplicable headache. She pursed her lips, restrained the banditry in her eyes, and whispered, “Okay, we’ll see.”","“Okay.”","On the other end of the line, Nie Mi’s voice sounded energetic and loud.","However, Qiao Nian’s heart stirred. When she thought of what he had just said, a hint of helplessness flashed across her eyes. She added, “I’ll try my best to take some time.”","In the next three months, she would put most of her energy into helping Uncle Chen recuperate. After Chen Yuan’s college entrance examination was over, she would bring Uncle Chen to Beijing. First, she would transfer him to a hospital there. Then, she would let Elder Huang take a look at Uncle Chen’s condition when she had the chance.","Ye Wangchuan had the rare materials that Uncle Chen needed for his surgery. She didn’t lack materials now. She only lacked some technical problems during the surgery.","She had simulated this surgery in her mind many times. There were only a few details that she had yet to figure out. When she did, she could operate on Uncle Chen. At that time, Uncle Chen would be able to get rid of the hospital bed and the heavy machines. After he recovered, he would slowly have the ability to take care of himself and become an ordinary person...","This was what she had always wanted to do.","She had promised Aunt Chen this a long time ago.","“I just might not have the time.” Qiao Nian’s eyes flashed. She felt that she had more to do in the next three months.","The school had also gotten Shen Hui to talk to her about the college entrance examination, hoping that she would take it.","If she agreed to this, she still needed to find time to study.","It was impossible for her to take a look at the teaching materials now and go straight to the examination hall with a pen.","Of course, it was not impossible.","Qiao Nian knew very well that even if she didn’t read much, just what listened to in many classes in the past half a year was probably enough.","But no matter what, the school definitely wanted her to get good results. If she didn’t get first or second place, it would be meaningless to go.","Of course, the word “second” did not exist in her dictionary.","If she went, she would definitely get first place.","Nie Mi agreed readily. “It’s fine. We’ll see when the time comes. Anyway, everything depends on your time!”","Qiao Nian restrained the emotions in her eyes and nodded. She walked back to the desk and opened her laptop. “That’s all. I still have something on. Bye.”","“Okay, bye.”","Qiao Nian placed her phone on the table and pulled out a chair. She sat down and"]},{"number":555,"title":"Chapter 555 - Could It Be a Text from His Girlfriend?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","[Sun: You guys here?]","The chat group flashed, and someone came out immediately.","[Daji Plays With You: If Boss asked, I have to be there~ Boss, why are you free to come online today?]","[Guan Yan: I’m here.]","The light from the computer shone slowly on her face. Qiao Nian had finished her shower and taken some medicine. She felt much better now. She rested her elbows on the desk and looked at the group messages, realizing that Slim Waist Control was not online today.","She didn’t care. Her slender fingers flew across the keyboard as she sent a message.","[Sun: Did the Ye family look for us for a job recently?]","Guan Yan was usually the least chatty and most serious. This time, she replied the fastest.","[Guan Yan: Ye family? There seems to be a job with the surname Ye, but we didn’t take it. He wants to investigate a batch of goods in the illegal district.]","[Daji Plays With You: Doesn’t the Red Alliance never take on such jobs? We’re not second-hand dealers who sell information.]","Qiao Nian placed her phone on the table and happened to see this message on the chat.","The Red Alliance was in the hacker business. Usually, they would sell software and information technology. They wouldn’t even touch low-level hackers like selling information. It would lower their prices!","But this time...","The ends of her eyes curled up as she looked at the black plastic bag on the bed. Her black eyes were restrained and a little annoyed. Although she wasn’t afraid of being bitten when there were too many lice, she felt a little strange when she owed someone a favor. Every time that person was mentioned, she would be flustered.","Qiao Nian suppressed the strange feeling in her heart and returned her attention to replying.","[Sun: Send me that job, I’ll take it.]","[Guan Yan: ???]","[Daji Plays With You: ???]","[Daji Plays With You: Boss, are you drunk?]","Sun hadn’t taken on orders for many years. This time, she actually personally took on a list to check the goods. This was too...!!","Unbelievable!","Qiao Nian didn’t look at the messages in the group chat. From the corner of her eye, she saw the phone on the table light up. It was the number for the batch of goods that Guan Yan had sent her.","[Sun: That’s it. Bye.]","After sending the message, she didn’t even look at the reaction in the group. She exited the app and leaned back, casually picking up her phone to click on it.","Her fingers flew across the keyboard. No one knew what software she had opened, but the words on it kept jumping. She keyed in the cargo code that she had found. After a while, she narrowed her eyes and pressed the enter button.","The characters on the phone screen jumped rapidly. After about a minute, they stopped and a map with a red dot appeared.","Qiao Nian took a screenshot of the map and threw it back into the email. She sent it according to the address on the number.","The entire process took about half an hour.","After doing all of this, she wiped the traces on her phone and got up to go to the bathroom to dry her hair.","...","“Damn!”","At the same time, at a certain club in Beijing, the man who had received the email cursed. He held his phone and stood up to look at it for a long time. He couldn’t believe his eyes.","Zhang Yang and the others were shocked by his sudden action and looked at him.","“Young Master Qin, what’s wrong?”","“Who sent Young Master Qin a message and made you so excited? Is she your girlfriend?”","Jiang Xianrou was also present today. She was the only girl present. Today, she was wearing a Bvlgari dress, looking beautiful and poised. She sat there like a moon surrounded by stars, reserved and elegant.","When she heard Zhang Yang teasing Qin Si about receiving a message from his girlfriend, she also looked up in curiosity and smiled. “Young Master Qin, you have a girlfriend?”"]},{"number":556,"title":"Chapter 556 - The Super Wild and Powerful Kind","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Unexpectedly, Qin Si stood up and walked back and forth for a bit. He then spoke angrily. “What girlfriend? I’m still single!”","It was more likely that Master Wang had a girlfriend.","Master Wang had picked up a call previously. After the call, he even ignored the people from the CIA and left, leaving him alone with the blonde-haired and blue-eyed foreigners. It was so annoying!","However, he didn’t voice his displeasure. He glanced in Jiang Xianrou’s direction.","Everyone in their private circle knew that Jiang Xianrou was interested in Master Wang. However, reality was cruel. It didn’t seem like Ye Wangchuan liked Jiang Xianrou. If he was interested in her, they would have started dating long ago. It wouldn’t have remained as such an ordinary relationship.","“If it wasn’t your girlfriend, then who was it? Who sent you the message?”","Zhang Yang and the other people were still curious.","Qin Si didn’t hide it from them. He kept a straight face, and it was rare that he did not speak with his usual cynicism. There was no expression on his face, and he looked as though he had seen a ghost. He said, “It was from the Red Alliance.”","Most of the people present came from influential families. They were all aware of the legal and illegal areas in society.","The Red Alliance?","The powerful hacker organization?","Qin Si didn’t bother to provide further explanation. He couldn’t stop smiling. He was afraid that if he hesitated, the mail would disappear from his cell phone. He paced back and forth excitedly, and at the same time, opened the mail. When he saw that there was an attached picture in the mail, he quickly downloaded it and clicked on it. The picture was a map.","The map was clear, and there was a red dot on it.","There was a circle above the red dot. The words in the circle indicated that the goods were located at the position marked by the red dot.","The handwriting was flamboyant and looked wild!","Judging by the handwriting, it seemed like the person who wrote this was a wild and wilful person.","Qin Si looked at the message for several seconds. He then looked up at the sender. His mouth opened and his eyes widened in surprise. He looked as though he couldn’t control his expression and was barely able to speak.","“Sun?”","The Red Alliance had always been famous. Countless people were trying to seek help from them. These people came from all walks of life. They posted their requests online, tagging the Red Alliance in their requests. They wanted the Red Alliance to help them with those requests.","However, everyone knew that the members of the Red Alliance were arrogant and did things according to their own wishes. No one could control them.","They would sometimes take on three or four requests a month, and sometimes, they wouldn’t even complete one request in half a year.","Whether the Red Alliance took on the request depended on luck!","Furthermore, each member operated differently.","For example, Slim Waist Control usually took on more requests as compared to the other members. The other member that took on requests more frequently would be Guan Yan.","Among the members of the Red Alliance, the person who accepted requests the least would be the boss, the legendary Sun. Sun was the most powerful member of the Red Alliance.","Sun rarely accepted any requests.","Although Sun rarely accepted any requests, Sun was the most powerful person in the Red Alliance. It was said that the anti-theft software used by major banks was developed by Sun. In other words, Sun was so powerful that it would be a waste of time to pick up requests from the black market.","This time, they were trying to track down a batch of goods that came from the illegal zone. Their request had already been on the internet for three months. They had even enlisted the CIA’s help. They tried to extract information from the other party, but it did not work.","Unexpectedly, the Red Alliance had accepted their request. The tables had turned!","Furthermore, the request was accepted by Sun, the Red Alliance’s boss. Sun not only found the goods but also marked them on a map.","Qin Si took a while to recover from his joy. He was stunned.","When Jiang Xianrou saw him acting so happily, she couldn’t help but ask, “Young Master Qin, who is Sun?”","Qin Si was too busy forwarding the mail to Ye Wangchuanthat he replied absentmindedly, “A hacker.”","The super wild and powerful kind."]},{"number":557,"title":"Chapter 557 - If You’re Looking for Hackers, I Know Someone Who Could Help","paragraphs":["He gave one more line of explanation. “Master Wang wanted to check on something, but no one accepted his request until now.”","“Ohh.” Jiang Xianrou wasn’t interested in the organization of hackers. However, when she knew that Ye Wangchuan was looking for a hacker, she casually answered, “If you’re looking for a hacker, I know someone who could help.”","She saw Qin Si looking over at her.","Her smile was reserved. She knew that Zhou Hengfeng had a decent position in the domestic hacker community, so she spoke softly but confidently. “His name is Zhou Hengfeng. He was a student of my grandfather. Now, he’s a slightly well-known hacker in China.”","Before Qin Si could speak, Zhang Yang’s expression turned to surprise and he interrupted their conversation. “Miss Jiang, are you referring to big boss Zhou Hengfeng?”","Zhou Hengfeng was one of the best in the hacker community in China. Everyone was envious of him.","“Zhou Hengfeng is a proud man. He’s not the kind of person who would just accept any request. The likelihood of him accepting a request is less than the chance of someone going to heaven. Some time ago, my family’s company faced some problems. My parents wanted to enlist Zhou Hengfeng’s help, but he refused, even after we pulled in a lot of favors.”","After saying all that, he looked at Jiang Xianrou with admiration in his eyes and said enviously, “As expected of Miss Jiang. You’re so influential, to be even able to call Zhou Hengfeng to take on a request.”","It was difficult for Qin Si and Ye Wangchuan to enter this exclusive circle. So far, only Jiang Xianrou managed to do so.","Ye Wangchuan wasn’t here tonight. Not everyone here was a part of their small circle. Some people that Qin Si had called over tonight were also trying to get into their small circle.","For example, this person with a head of hair looking like a bird’s nest. His family was a little rich and had some connections. He was roaming around various circles and finally got the opportunity to join this evening’s party. Naturally, he was trying hard to please Qin Si.","However, he didn’t dare to suck up to him directly. After much consideration, he decided to start a connection with Jiang Xianrou first!","He had been singing Jiang Xianrou’s praises all night. He agreed with and praised whatever she said. He also praised her high status.","This method of flattery was common to the people in the circle. However, when they saw how much Zhang Yang was sucking up to her, they couldn’t help but frown contemptuously.","The only person who seemed to be enjoying the attention was Jiang Xianrou. She smiled and said, “Uncle Zhou is my elder. I can ask him, but I cannot guarantee that he will help you. However...”","She changed the tone of her voice, looked at Qin Si earnestly, and said, “However, if I mention that the request is from you, it’s likely that he will accept it.”","Zhou Hengfeng had a strong character and a reputation.","He also changed his attitude based on who he was facing.","Ye Wangchuan was also a person who stood at the top of the hierarchy in Beijing. Qin Si was at a slightly lower position. No matter how lofty Zhou Hengfeng was, he still lived in Beijing and had to earn a living.","He knew who he could afford to offend and who he should never offend.","With regards to showing off, when done in front of the appropriate people, it would seem like he was confident, unconventional, and lofty.","However, in front of the wrong people, he would just be tempting fate!","Jiang Xianrou knew in her heart that Zhou Hengfeng was also not a fool. He wasn’t as influential as Master Nie. If he were, he wouldn’t have to befriend her family. In the past, she had asked Zhou Hengfeng to help track down Zhui Guang’s IP address. Did he not help her out in the end?","If it were a request made by someone else, would he have helped to look up such trivial matters?","She took out her cell phone and was about to call Zhou Hengfeng.","At this moment, Qin Si had already forwarded the email to Ye Wangchuan. Noticing that she was about to make the call, he immediately stopped her and said, “There’s no need to call him.”"]},{"number":558,"title":"Chapter 558 - Zhou Hengfeng Is on the Same Level as Sun?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Surprised, Jiang Xianrou pursed her lips and said modestly, “Why not? Did you not say that Master Wang was trying to check on something? He even went to look for a few people to help, but they didn’t manage to find anything.”","She mistakenly thought that Qin Si refused her offer because he was unfamiliar with Zhou Hengfeng. She then explained softly, “I don’t know who Sun is, but Uncle Zhou is famous in China. He should be about the same level as Sun from the Red Alliance. If Master Wang needs him to help out, I can try to ask Uncle Zhou to help him out.”","“You said that Zhou Hengfeng is of the same level as Sun?”","Jiang Xianrou was still enjoying the praise she received just now and was still in her own world. She nodded calmly. “He should be of the same level as the Sun you were referring to just now. However, Uncle Zhou does not accept online requests. He’s relatively more low-key and might be less well-known because of this.”","Qin Si was speechless.","Was the Red Alliance merely a third-rate hacker organization that would simply accept requests that were posted online in her eyes?","Was Sun merely a lowly hacker that operated under a false name online?","Seeing her arrogant and casual expression, Qin Si knew that she might have heard of the Red Alliance before. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have made this remark.","He had also heard of Zhou Hengfeng before. Zhou Hengfeng was indeed famous among Chinese hackers.","However, they had already sought help from people who were a hundred times more powerful than Zhou Hengfeng. Even they were unable to help them!","They finally managed to solve their issue when the Red Alliance accepted their request. In less than half an hour, the Red Alliance managed to complete their request and even attached a map!","Leaving Jiang Xianrou aside, even if Zhou Hengfeng was here, he wouldn’t dare to say that he was at the same level as Sun.","It could only be said that Jiang Xianrou was fearless. She dared to make such an unthinkable remark.","Qin Si’s earrings were shining and his expression was cynical. He had managed to suppress the thoughts in his heart.","Zhou Hengfeng was comparable to Sun?","He was afraid that Zhou Hengfeng wouldn’t even be qualified to carry Sun’s shoes!","However, Jiang Xianrou was still Jiang Li’s sister. Even if he wanted to make a remark, he still had to respect the person backing her. He was too lazy to explain how powerful the Red Alliance was and how admirable Sun really was.","Taking out his cell phone to call Bo Jingxing, he gave Jiang Xianrou a simple reply, “Not this time, thank you. We have already found what we are looking for.","“I’m going to make a call. You guys continue playing first.”","As he said that, he took his cell phone and walked out.","The other people looked at each other. Zhang Yang could tell something was up from his words and glanced at Jiang Xianrou. He could read the atmosphere well and did not allow his inner thoughts to show. However, his attitude towards Jiang Xianrou wasn’t as warm as before.","The other people who followed him here in the hopes of joining the small circle were not as insightful and observant as him.","He noticed Qin Si’s gentle tone when speaking to Jiang Xianrou, so he paid more attention to Jiang Xianrou’s position within the circle. He smiled and gently poured her a cup of agave wine, thinking of another topic to engage with her. “Miss Jiang, I heard that a music convention will be held in Rao City. Master Nie and many professionals will attend. Will you also be attending?”","Jiang Xianrou looked in the direction where Qin Si had left. Her heart felt empty. She had always felt like there was something wrong. However, before she could broach that topic, someone asked about the music convention.","The others beside Zhang Yang continued to ask her questions. “Music convention? What kind of an event is that? If it was so great, why is it being held in Rao City and not in Beijing? Master Wang has also been going to Rao City quite frequently. He’s seldom in Beijing. I don’t know what’s so attractive about Rao City.. Recently, everyone has been going there.”"]},{"number":559,"title":"Chapter 559 - Leave a Ticket for Sister Nian Even If It’s Hard to Get","paragraphs":["“The music event this time is big. It will be organized by the Wen Family. It’s very hard to get invited to this event as it is a small private event. I heard about this event from my auntie. I initially wanted to go, but I wasn’t able to get an invitation.”","Glancing around, his gaze landed on Jiang Xianrou again. He smiled and said, “But you’re Miss Jiang. I feel that you should have been invited to the event.”","Jiang Xianrou had outstanding talent. She was famous in both the entertainment and classical music circles. She was a talented woman who was famous among all the celebrities in Beijing.","At this moment, she picked up her glass of agave wine and swirled it. She was trying to conceal the triumph and pride hidden in her eyes. She tucked the stray strands of hair behind her ears and raised her chin slightly; with her outstanding facial features and exquisite makeup, she looked stunning. She smiled proudly and admitted to the people around her. “Well, I did receive an invitation for this event. I’ll be attending it.","“It will be my honor to attend this music event with Master Nie and the other professionals. I’m looking forward to learning many new things.”","Someone just said that this event was very exclusive and that it was hard to receive an invitation.","Now, Jiang Xianrou admitted that she had received an invitation and was going to attend this event.","Even Zhang Yang had to look at her differently now. His originally cold attitude turned a little warmer.","...","It was evening already, and Qiao Chen was following Qiao Weimin home from the provincial hospital.","She was thinking about the music event the whole way.","Reaching the entrance, she said, “I’m home.”","Shen Qiongzhi quickly stepped out and said, “Chen Chen, are you home?”","She put her hands on Qiao Chen’s shoulders, caressed her face, and looked at her from the left and right. She was so excited that her eyes were reddish. She choked a little and said, “You have grown thin. Look at these eyebags. Have you not been sleeping well recently?”","Qiao Chen said disapprovingly, “I have been busy preparing for the examination and practicing with the piano at night recently. I didn’t have much time to sleep.” She then shrugged off her hands and said impatiently, “Mom, please let me in first. I’m tired.”","“Oh my goodness! Look at me. I was so excited that I forgot that we’re still standing here. Come on in.” Shen Qiongzhi let go of her and followed her into the house. She excitedly said, “I’m stewing some pigeon soup. I’ll prepare a bowl for you once it is done. The helper said that this soup will help replenish your energy. You’re so tired from the examination and your health is declining. You should drink this soup to make up for your lost nutrients.”","Qiao Chen didn’t reply. She walked over to the sofa, bent down to take a glass of water, and took a sip.","She was a little annoyed because it always felt like she was being nagged at.","Shen Qiongzhi was so happy that she didn’t notice that Qiao Chen was annoyed. She spoke excitedly. “I have booked a hotel to celebrate you passing the examination. This time, we won’t be going to the Waterside Pavilion. I have also informed my relatives of the location. We’ll be having a feast in the banquet hall on the third floor of Huanyu Hotel. I have also invited your former Form Teacher, Teacher Chen. In addition, I have also invited some of your father’s business partners.”","When she finished speaking, she asked Qiao Chen a question. “Chen Chen, do you have anyone else you want to invite? Do you want to invite your classmates? You can invite them if you want to.","“Initially, I wanted to organize a huge feast to celebrate your admission into Qing University. However, your father said that it was too high-profile. He suggested only inviting our relatives and some friends for dinner. Although I agreed, a celebration should be more lively with more people. If you have any friends or relatives you wish to invite, you can let me know. We can still afford to accommodate them.” Her face expressed regret as she explained the plans to Qiao Chen in frustration.","Hearing this, Qiao Chen thought of something. She looked at her and said, “My aunt said that I should invite Professor Cheng Wu. In addition, I’d like to invite Brother Fu and Auntie Fu.”","She looked down on her classmates in Rao City, such as Xu Xu and Cai Yan. Naturally, there was no need to invite them."]},{"number":560,"title":"Chapter 560 - It Isn’t Clear Who the Winner Is Yet","paragraphs":["She was only intending to invite Fu Ge and his family.","She was also planning to invite Professor Cheng Wu at that time. Not wanting her celebration feast to seem too low class, she turned to Shen Qiongzhi and said, “Mom, can you also invite Grandma Tang? After all, it’s my celebration banquet. I hope that she’ll be able to attend.”","She knew all the famous people and families in Rao City, but only Tang Wei’s family was worth forging a relationship with.","The Tang Family wasn’t as powerful as the Jiang Family.","However, they were still considered the top one or two most powerful family in Rao City.","Qiao Chen wanted to invite them to her banquet to support herself.","“Regarding this...” Shen Qiongzhi hesitated. It wasn’t that she was unwilling to invite the Tang Family. They were strong and influential. If they were willing to attend Qiao Chen’s celebration banquet, it would definitely be beneficial.","However, they had caused some trouble for the Tang Family when they celebrated Qiao Chen’s birthday previously. At that time, Tang Wei already expressed that they should have as little contact with each other as possible. Although they didn’t explicitly cut off all ties, it would be shameless of them to invite the Tang Family after that incident.","However, her daughter wanted to invite people from the Tang Family. Even if Shen Qiongzhi felt embarrassed, she still agreed. “Okay, I’ll let your grandmother know and try to get Grandma Tang to attend your celebration feast.”","“Yes.”","Qiao Chen didn’t care if they were embarrassed while inviting the Tang Family. She felt satisfied after she achieved her goal. She gave a simple acknowledgment, put down her glass of water, and started walking to her room.","Shen Qiongzhi suddenly said, “By the way, I want to invite someone too.” No one knew if she was already thinking of inviting someone else or she did this on a whim.","“Who is it?” Qiao Chen didn’t care and asked casually. “Mom, you can just invite anyone you want. One or two more people won’t make much of a difference.”","“She’s special!”","Shen Qiongzhi raised her chin, unable to hide her pride and contempt. She whispered, “I’d like to invite Qiao Nian to your celebration banquet.”","The piece of paper in Qiao Chen’s hand was almost destroyed.","“Qiao Nian?”","Shen Qiongzhi still didn’t know that Qiao Nian had been admitted into Qing University. She had a look of disdain on her face as she said, “That’s right. In the past, she went around messing things up for you everywhere. She even caused you to lose your sponsorship. This time, you successfully got into Qing University, but she failed. This is a chance to show her who is truly the phoenix! That will show her whose fault it really was, whether it was because we, the Qiao Family, treated her poorly, or because she’s useless.”","Qiao Chen wasn’t in the mood to listen to her explanation. Qiao Chen saw that she was very excited. The corners of her mouth twitched and she had a complex look in her eyes. However, she wasn’t able to tell her what happened in the afternoon.","Everyone thought that Qiao Nian had failed the examination. No one knew that she actually scored 650 points, the full marks for the examinations!","Not only did she make it into Qing University, but according to Wen Ziyu, the reason Qing University did not publicize the results this time was to prevent other schools from poaching Qiao Nian!","It was so humiliating. How could she allow Qiao Nian to attend her celebration banquet?","If Qiao Nian really came, she was afraid that she would come with an air of arrogance and look at her with condescending eyes.","It would be just like what happened in the Japanese food store during lunch. It would be similar to how Liang Bowen and the rest looked at her!","Qiao Chen was upset.","Fortunately, Qiao Weimin had heard what Shen Qiongzhi said. Dissatisfied, he interrupted her. “All right, it’s a good thing that she was admitted into college. Why do you have to make someone else unhappy?”","“I think you’re still trying to defend Qiao Nian.”","“I’m not defending her. I just feel that since everyone is already on such bad terms with each other, there’s no need to antagonize her anymore. Furthermore, you have also raised her for more than ten years. Why do you have to treat her like she’s your enemy?”","Taking advantage of their quarrel, Qiao Chen said, “Mom, I will go back to my room first.”"]},{"number":561,"title":"Chapter 561 - You Said Qiao Nian Beat Someone...","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","“Chen Chen, pigeon soup...” Shen Qiongzhi saw that she was going upstairs and did not bother arguing with Qiao Weimin. She called out to her from behind.","“No, I don’t want it.”","Qiao Chen’s face and lips were pale as she hurried upstairs.","...","Upstairs, she closed the door as soon as she entered the room. She threw her bag on the bed and pulled a chair to sit down in frustration.","Biting her lips, her heart was in a mess and she couldn’t calm down.","Now, almost everyone thought that Qiao Nian hadn’t been accepted by Qing University.","She couldn’t imagine how everyone would react when they saw Qiao Nian’s results after the results were released!","Her parents were fine. Even if they couldn’t wait for Qiao Nian to fail, they wouldn’t take their anger out on her just because she did well.","However, Qiao Chen knew very well that Wei Ling wasn’t like that.","The reason why she could successfully get a spot in the music exchange this time was partly that Wei Ling wanted to take revenge on Qiao Nian. If Wei Ling knew that Qiao Nian had also entered Qing University and had even done better than her, would she still help her unconditionally? She wasn’t sure herself...","Frustrated, she took out her phone from her bag. She really wanted to call Fu Ge and ask him about the details of Wen Ziyu and Qiao Nian’s joint examination.","For example, if Qiao Nian did so well, why did Wen Ziyu say that Qiao Nian had chosen the Chinese Medicine Faculty?","Another example was which mentor was in charge of Qiao Nian in the Chinese Medicine Faculty and if she had any other facilitation majors. For example, Liang Lu’s Clinical Department.","She wanted to know all these.","Qiao Chen had already finished typing her message, but she still had not sent it.","Lowering her curved eyelashes, she deleted all the words she had typed in frustration and placed her phone back on the table, feeling extremely conflicted.","She really wanted to find out about Qiao Nian’s joint examination, but if she asked Fu Ge, it would be equivalent to telling him that Qiao Nian really got in and had even scored 650 points.","Previously, she had gone to the Imperial Mansion for a meal with Fu Ge to celebrate her admission to Qing University.","She had also unintentionally mentioned to him that Qiao Nian hadn’t managed to get into Qing University. She had said that Qiao Nian would return to Rao City in disappointment if she didn’t get into Qing University. Now, if she sent a message asking him to ask his roommate which department Qiao Nian was in, wasn’t it equivalent to slapping herself in the face?","Qiao Chen’s life had been smooth-sailing, and this was the first time she had suffered such a blow in the past month. Even the matter of the concert wasn’t a problem for her.","She hugged her knees with both arms and buried her head in them. After an unknown period of time, Shen Qiongzhi knocked on the door. She said that the pigeon soup was ready and brought her a bowl. Qiao Chen didn’t even look up and only said quietly that she wanted to sleep and did not want to drink it.","Until her phone rang persistently.","Lost in her thoughts, the girl finally looked up. She reached for her phone on the table and looked at the caller ID.","With this glance, the frustration and anxiety on her face dissipated like the wind. Her eyes flashed as she picked up the call.","“Hello.”","The person on the other end of the line did not speak for a long time.","Qiao Chen controlled her temper and looked at her phone again. When she saw that she was still on the line, she placed it by her ear and said gently, “Student Wu Jie, why are you calling me so late at night?”","Actually, she could roughly guess why Wu Jie was looking for her. However, Wu Jie was like a piece of straw that had delivered itself to her door. She happened to be able to resolve her urgent needs!","Therefore, she had enough patience to wait for her to speak!","As expected.","The person on the other end of the line was silent for a full two minutes before asking her obscurely, “Chen Chen, this afternoon, you said that Qiao Nian hit someone...”"]},{"number":562,"title":"Chapter 562 - Perfect Solution","paragraphs":["“Ah, that matter.” A trace of a smile appeared on Qiao Chen’s lips as her eyes flashed. She immediately cut her off and pretended to be troubled. “I heard that her family had found a connection for her, so I think it’ll be forgotten. Unfortunately, the person she beat up for no reason is still lying in the hospital...”","There was silence on the other end of the line for a few seconds before she asked, “So Qiao Nian was set free after hitting someone?”","Qiao Chen smiled and said indifferently, “She might be fine. Unless...”","“Unless what?”","Qiao Chen held her phone and restrained the ruthlessness in her eyes as she said softly, “Unless someone reports it to the school, this matter will most likely be taken lightly and treated as if it never happened.","“Actually, since she did so well this time, the school will definitely know her results. Even if the teacher finds out about it, it might not be useful. The teacher will definitely protect the students. It wasn’t easy for the school to get her into Qing University, especially your class. Two people went this time, and only she got in. It’s only natural for the teacher to protect her. Don’t think too much about it...”","With that, she didn’t deliberately encourage Wu Jie. She only said what she needed to say and quietly waited for Wu Jie to think about it herself.","Wu Jie didn’t say what she was thinking directly. Qiao Chen only heard the girl’s deep voice on the other end of the line. “I understand. Thank you, Chen Chen.”","When Qiao Chen heard her voice, the corners of her lips curved into a mocking smile. She had already relaxed most of her heart, but she still spoke hypocritically.","“Why are you thanking me? I implicated you this time. You were originally doing well in Class A, but because I invited you to lunch, your classmates were quite angry this afternoon. I was afraid... afraid that they would ostracize you in the future.”","She paused and said thoughtfully, “... Qiao Nian is used to being domineering. Now that you’re openly on my side, I reckon she won’t bother with you anymore! If she ignores you, the people around her... Sigh... Maybe things aren’t as bad as I thought!”","“... I know her personality. She’s just a hooligan. Today, she hit others indiscriminately, and tomorrow, she can hit me indiscriminately. I won’t sit back and do nothing!”","“Aren’t you thinking too much? She wouldn’t hit you...” Qiao Chen smiled completely, her eyes filled with mockery. Unfortunately, Wu Jie was at home and couldn’t see her current expression. She only heard her gentle and kind voice persuading her. “Perhaps things aren’t as bad as you think. If someone else reports this and it gets out of hand, the school won’t ignore it.”","The girl on the other end of the line did not seem to want to continue. She hurriedly said, “Alright, alright. My mom is coming up. I’ll hang up first.”","“Ok.”","Qiao Chen hung up.","She smiled and sent Wu Jie another message, then put down her phone. Her depressed mood was swept away. She returned to her usual arrogant demeanor and smiled before getting up to remove her makeup and take a shower...","...","The next day.","Qiao Nian was woken up by her phone early in the morning.","She hadn’t woken up yet and was usually quite angry when she woke up. Now, she held her head in her hands, her eyes filled with the frustration of being woken up. She took her phone from the bed, suppressed her anger, and picked up the call.","“Hello.”","She had slept late last night and hadn’t slept well. Her voice was extremely hoarse.","Shen Qingqing’s shouting could be heard from the other end of the phone. “Sister Nian, look at the school forum. The forum is about to explode!”"]},{"number":563,"title":"Chapter 563 - Wu Jies Real Name","paragraphs":["“Yes.”","Qiao Nian was still in a daze and her mind was still groggy. She rubbed her temples lazily and replied casually, “So what if it exploded? I’m not a police officer.”","It seemed like a place like First High School’s forum was not under her control. The school forum usually had a moderator. What did it have to do with her?","“No.” Shen Qingqing was quite anxious and couldn’t explain it clearly for a while. She only said, “The school’s forum exploded because of you. Sister Nian, quickly get up and take a look. I think there will be trouble at school today!”","Qiao Nian didn’t want to care about the small conflicts in school. She still planned to visit Uncle Chen at the hospital today.","Anyway, her quota for Qing University had been decided. Shen Hui didn’t care much about her. She could go to school or not, it depended on her.","However, since Shen Qingqing was in such a hurry, Qiao Nian still forced herself to get out of bed after hanging up. As she went to the bathroom to brush her teeth and wash up, she slowly picked up her phone and searched for First High School’s school forum.","There was indeed a popular post on the top.","It was from Wu Jie.","It was sent at midnight last night.","It had risen to first place at 8:00 AM this morning, followed by the word “hot topic.” It was obvious how popular it was.","She glanced at it and saw her name on the thread.","— I’m going to report my senior year classmate in Class A for hitting someone outside of school!","“...” Qiao Nian gritted her teeth. Her temples throbbed, and her eyes were cold and dry. She was very annoyed.","Even Liang Bowen didn’t know that she had hit Wei Qi. How did Wu Jie know about this? A figure appeared in her mind.","She opened the thread expressionlessly.","The thread wrote: Hello, everyone. I’m Wu Jie from First High School’s Year Three Class A. I want to report to the entire school about Qiao Nian’s assault outside the school. Qiao Nian usually likes to form cliques in class and isolate the other students. This time, she beat someone outside the school for no reason and broke three ribs of the victim. Her behavior is bad, and she severely broke the school’s rules! On behalf of all the students, I severely condemn this kind of despicable behavior and request the school to punish such students who break the school rules severely!","Qiao Nian’s casual gaze landed on the words “forming cliques” and “isolating other students”. She looked away coldly.","She casually scrolled through the comments below.","Not long after Wu Jie’s post was posted, someone replied.","It was obvious that there were many sleepless night owls among the students.","[Peach’s Sweetness: Wow! There’s such an explosive post in the middle of the night. Senior Sister Qiao Nian from Class A? I’ve heard of her. She’s very pretty. Many boys in our class gossiped about her in private, saying that she’s the campus belle of First High School. It turns out that the campus belle also fights. ━((*′д`)爻(′д`*))━!!!!]","[Flying Cat: I didn’t see how Qiao Nian bullied her classmates. Instead, I saw the OP’s jealous face.]","[Hehe, my son is the one on the first floor: Report her by name?? That awesome??]","[You don’t understand Daddy’s posture: Wow, this is the first time I’ve seen such an exciting post. OP is awesome! I support you.]","[Question is nonsense: There’s nothing to say. Wait for the school to settle the results.]","When she flipped through two pages, they were filled with nonsense. Qiao Nian couldn’t be bothered to read them and left.","At this moment, Liang Bowen, Jiang Tingting, Chen Yuan, and the others had all sent her messages. Qiao Nian didn’t read any of them. She calmly brushed her teeth and washed up, changed her clothes, and went downstairs with her phone.","Gu San, Jiang Li, and the others had not woken up yet."]},{"number":564,"title":"Chapter 564 - What Did You Call Me?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","She saw someone walking from the living room to the sofa with a cup of coffee.","Ye Wangchuan was stirring the coffee cup in his hand with his well-defined and fair fingers. His hand was clean and good-looking. He was definitely qualified to be a hand model.","He was wearing a long black coat with a shirt that he had bought himself. It made him look lean, and his legs long and straight.","He was quite eye-catching!","Who didn’t want to see a beautiful human early in the morning?","Qiao Nian felt like it was quite refreshing. At least, her eyes, which had been stung by the post on the school’s forum, felt much better now.","She went down the stairs.","Halfway through, the man lazily stirring his coffee looked up and saw her. His deep eyes narrowed slightly, and his pupils reflected her shadow.","“You’re up?”","“Yes.”","Qiao Nian walked over and opened the fridge. She had wanted to take out a bottle of water, but who knew that as soon as her hand touched the bottle, someone’s hands moved faster than her. He took the bottle away and held the fridge door as he said domineeringly, “You can’t drink ice water.”","“??”","Qiao Nian was confused.","In the past, she used to do whatever she wanted. Why was there so much that she couldn’t do now?","Ye Wangchuan’s deep eyes seemed to see through her thoughts. He narrowed his eyes dangerously and touched his scarlet lips. “Have you forgotten about your stomachache last night?”","It would have been better if he hadn’t mentioned it. Now that he did, she recalled the uncomfortable feeling in her stomach last night. Her lower abdomen felt like it was being pulled apart again.","She frowned.","He had already pulled her hand away.","Ye Wangchuan closed the fridge and said calmly, “Sit on the sofa for a while. Wait for me. I’ll make you a cup of warm water.”","“Okay.” Qiao Nian shrugged. Actually, she wanted to say that she didn’t want to drink ice water. She could even get a cup of lukewarm water.","However, the man was very fast. He let go of her hand and entered the kitchen.","She had no choice but to obediently sit on the sofa and play with her phone while listening to him.","In a few minutes, the man walked over with a cup.","The mug was the one she often used. Jiang Li and the little bun had bought it for her together. There was a cat print on it, and the mug was from a very expensive brand. One mug was about five digits, and it was convenient to use.","She usually used that cup to drink water.","At this moment, hot smoke was coming from the mug. She could tell that the water he had made for her was very hot.","“Drink slowly. It’s hot.”","“...” Qiao Nian took the cup. She had thought that it would be the same hot coffee as his. Who knew that there would be two red dates floating in a cup of brown sugar water?","She suddenly remembered what Wei Lou had said about “grapes, wine, and wolfberry cups. Young people must take care of themselves.” The corners of her mouth twitched. She looked up at the man beside her, who had bent down to pick up his coffee cup. She couldn’t help but say, “Master Wang, does Gu San know that you know these things?”","He usually looked inconspicuous, but he actually knew what girls should drink during their period.","She was just teasing him casually, but the man holding the coffee looked at her with his deep eyes. He raised his eyebrows and said with a domineering gaze, “Huh? What did you call me?”","Qiao Nian was speechless.","What did she just call him?","Master Wang?","It didn’t seem wrong.","Gu San and Jiang Li usually called him that.","At this thought, Qiao Nian’s body relaxed. She took a sip of the brown sugar water. It was so sweet that she felt flustered and annoyed. She raised her head and looked into his eyes with her distinctive black and white eyes.. She answered casually, “I called you Master Wang. Is there anything wrong with that?”"]},{"number":565,"title":"Chapter 565 - Havent You Always Called Me Brother Ye?","paragraphs":["Ye Wangchuan looked at her slouching on the sofa and raised his overly beautiful face. She even asked himself lazily what was wrong. He lowered his eyes and chuckled very attractively. “Nothing’s wrong. But haven’t you always called me Brother Ye?”","His voice was low and deep. He was already very charming without deliberately lowering his voice. Now, Qiao Nian seriously suspected that he was doing this on purpose!","She pursed her lips. The brown sugar water suddenly stopped being sweet. To hide her frustration, she lowered her head and took two sips. Then, she raised her head and composed herself before replying, “I also called you Uncle like Chen Chen does.”","In other words, if he felt that something was wrong, she could call him Uncle.","Ye Wangchuan had only wanted to tease her, but who knew that she would make him speechless? He put down his coffee cup and rubbed his forehead. His handsome face revealed his helplessness as he said, “Forget about Uncle. I’m not that old. You can call me whatever you want.”","“Then, I’ll call you Master Wang.” It was rare for Qiao Nian to win against him. In a good mood, she said straightforwardly, “They all call you Master Wang. It’s more natural when I call you that.”","In the past, she didn’t feel that there was anything wrong with calling him Brother Ye. Later on... when her alias fell, she couldn’t be bothered to pretend in front of him.","It felt strange to call him Brother Ye again.","Ye Wangchuan had no objections. When he saw that she was obediently drinking the brown sugar water he had made for her, his eyes became more relaxed. He looked at her disheveled appearance and asked, “What are your plans later? Are you going to school?”","Last night, Qin Si had sent him an email saying that the Red Alliance had accepted their order and had even taken a screenshot of the goods. He seriously suspected that it had something to do with the girl in front of him.","However...","Ye Wangchuan pursed his lips and controlled his temper. He was in no hurry to ask a certain someone, in case he aroused her rebellious thoughts.","Master Wang was always better than Uncle, and better than... good friends!","Their relationship had progressed at least a step, hadn’t it?","Qiao Nian didn’t know what he was thinking. She lowered her head and took another big sip of brown sugar water. It was still so sweet that it made her nervous. However, at least the faint pain in her stomach was much better. She put down the cup and raised her eyes, then said lazily, “I’m probably going to the hospital.”","“To the hospital?”","“Yeah.” Qiao Nian nodded blatantly. “I want to go to the hospital to see Uncle Chen and tell Chen Yuan to attend school.”","Chen Yuan still didn’t know that his punishment had been withdrawn. As the college entrance examination was approaching, every day was very important. He couldn’t possibly continue to skip classes like this.","Chen Yuan... Ye Wangchuan narrowed his eyes. His black eyelashes drooped as he retracted the light in his eyes. It took him a long time to remember who Chen Yuan was. He seemed to be a boy who often followed Qiao Nian. He was average-looking and had an introverted personality. He wasn’t as eye-catching as Liang Bowen, but he was more focused on Qiao Nian than the latter.","He didn’t take the young boy, who hadn’t even grown all his hair, seriously. He took his car keys magnanimously and said to her, “Let’s go. I have nothing on today. I’ll send you there.”","“Er, I can take a taxi.” Qiao Nian was unwilling to let him send her off, so she got up slowly.","“This is the villa district. Even if you call a taxi, they won’t be able to enter. Anyway, I’m free. Aunt Chen treated me to hot and sour noodles before. Since her husband isn’t in good health, I should visit the hospital as a polite gesture.”","Qiao Nian was speechless. After treating him to a bowl of 7 yuan hot and sour noodles, he would make a special trip to the hospital?"]},{"number":566,"title":"Chapter 566 - Deliberately Come to Class Early","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Although she didn’t understand what Ye Wangchuan was doing, when did the Ye family in Beijing become so free?","He was bought over with a bowl of hot and sour noodles?","Ye Wangchuan raised his eyes. The ends of his eyes were dark red from waking up early. However, he was still very firm in certain matters. He took her phone away and walked in front. “Let’s go.”","...","It was early in the morning at Rao City’s First High School.","The students who came to class all said the same thing when they met in the morning: Hey, have you seen the school forum?","The English representative of Class A, which was supposed to be having morning reading, did not go up to lead. No one spoke in class. Everyone took out a book and spread it on the table, but not many people read it. Their gazes were basically on the second seat on the third row.","Wu Jie arrived early. She had been sitting in her seat all morning. Her back was straight and her face was tense. There was no expression on her face as she kept her head buried as if she was reading seriously.","Shen Qingqing gritted her teeth. As she looked at her back, which was filled with righteousness, she couldn’t help but feel disgusted. “She sure can hold it in. She even dared to come to class.”","It was English morning self-study this morning, but a Chinese book was spread out on Liang Bowen’s desk. He was half leaning against the wall, and it could be seen that he wasn’t reading seriously at a glance. His handsome face revealed a cold smile as he replied cynically, “Of course she dares to come to school. She can’t wait for us to ‘bully’ her. It’ll be a good opportunity to let the forum gossip and let everyone in the school know that our class bully bullied her. She can also conveniently pin this on Sister Nian and say that she instructed us to do it... Otherwise, why do you think she came to class so early? Is she looking for a beating?”","“Pfft! She’s dreaming. She went to kneel down and curry favor with Qiao Chen. She curried favor with the wrong person, so she posted on the Internet to slander Sister Nian. When did Sister Nian isolate her? When did she form cliques?” Shen Qingqing was disgusted by Wu Jie’s behavior. She said coldly, “Sister Nian has a good personality, so we’re willing to play with her. Is that called forming cliques? Besides, have we isolated her before? Her seat should have been in the third last row, but because she isn’t tall, the teacher mentioned that she couldn’t see the blackboard because of her short-sightedness. Jiang Tingting took the initiative to give her the front row seat and let her sit in the front. Is this called isolation? When has everyone not called her out for any group activities? If she doesn’t want to participate, why is she saying people isolated her?","“Alright, even if this is called isolation, we’re the ones who isolated her. What has it got to do with Sister Nian? How long has Sister Nian been transferred to our class? Half a year? It’s Sister Nian’s fault that she was ‘isolated’ for three years?”","Liang Bowen saw that her face was so red from anger that she looked like a ripe apple. He really wanted to take a bite, but since the time and setting were not right, he could only endure it. He silently touched his high nose bridge and advised her, “Don’t be too angry. Some people are like this. They’re just jealous. Even if Sister Nian hasn’t done anything, she can still pick out bones from eggs. It’s enough if everyone can tell what kind of person she is.”","Shen Qingqing put down the book and said in frustration, “Are we just going to let her slander Sister Nian for no reason?”","“Wait until Sister Nian comes...” Liang Bowen didn’t think much of Wu Jie. He was more concerned that Qiao Nian hadn’t replied to his message.","However, since she didn’t reply to his messages, he felt more at ease. At least it meant that Qiao Nian didn’t take Wu Jie’s matter to heart and the matter was not that serious.","At least, it was not as serious as Wu Jie had said in the post. She said that Sister Nian might be sentenced for beating someone up until he was disabled.","If it was really that serious, Sister Nian would have replied long ago."]},{"number":567,"title":"Chapter 567 - Whos Wu Jie? The Principal Is Looking for You","paragraphs":["They didn’t deliberately lower their voices when they spoke, nor were they afraid that anyone would hear them.","Therefore, Wu Jie heard it clearly.","When she heard Liang Bowen say that she was jealous of Qiao Nian, she bit her lower lip and deliberately straightened her back. She held the pen firmly in her hand and drew a line on the paper with the tip of the pen.","She wasn’t wrong to say that Qiao Nian had hit someone outside school. Why should they say that she was jealous?","Was it wrong for her to report Qiao Nian for breaking the rules?","She couldn’t report Qiao Nian for doing something wrong just because they were classmates?","What was the difference between this and protecting her!","Wu Jie clenched the pen tightly and told herself that she didn’t do anything wrong. The ones wrong were Shen Qingqing, Liang Bowen, and the others. They were the ones who had ignored the school rules.","However, the gazes of everyone in class fell on her. She originally thought that if she came to class early, people like Jiang Tingting, who did not do well in class A and always surrounded Qiao Nian, would definitely find trouble with her. In the end, Jiang Tingting and the others did not make things difficult for her. They only snorted at her twice and left as if she was air...","Wu Jie felt very uncomfortable at being ignored.","At this moment, Class C’s form teacher happened to pass by. She stuck her head into the classroom and shouted, “Who’s Wu Jie?”","Wu Jie stood up, took a deep breath, and puffed out her chest. “Teacher, I’m Wu Jie.”","Holding the thermos, the class teacher who looked quite friendly glanced at her with a serious expression. It was rare that she did not smile as she said, “Oh, it’s you. Come with me to the principal’s office. The principal is looking for you.”","“Alright, Teacher.” Wu Jie clenched her fists by her sides and put down her pen. Without hesitation, she pulled out a chair and followed her.","The moment she left.","In the back row, Jiang Tingting kicked the table away and said in frustration, “Damn! Why did the principal ask for her? She won’t talk nonsense, right? If it wasn’t for Sister Nian, I would have f*cking attacked her this morning. She’s too cheap! It’s like she learned from someone. Look at her. She’s exactly like someone from Class B.”","Who else could it be? She was definitely talking about Qiao Chen.","Liang Bowen also looked worried. Looking at Wu Jie’s back, he took out his phone and sent a message to Qiao Nian.","...","In the principal’s office.","Shen Hui and a few Year Three class teachers were there. The principal was also there.","The atmosphere was very serious. No one spoke.","The moment Wu Jie entered, she saw a row of teachers standing or sitting in the bright and spacious office. The other person was the principal, who was sitting in the swivel chair.","She had rarely seen such a scene. She was so nervous that she didn’t know how to walk.","The moment she entered, she greeted them obediently.","“Hello, principal. Hello, Teacher Shen. Hello, teachers.”","Shen Hui was wearing a professional white shirt and a black cardigan. Her hair was combed neatly behind her, and she was expressionless. She looked very serious. Seeing her enter, she gave a faint nod of acknowledgment.","Wu Jie felt that her attitude toward her was much more stern and cold than before.","She bit her lip and recalled what Qiao Chen had said on the phone last night.","She said that she and Qiao Nian were the only ones in their class who had participated in Qing University’s joint examination. If she didn’t get in but Qiao Nian did, Shen Hui would definitely be biased toward the student who got in. After all, Qiao Nian represented the honor of their class...","She didn’t believe it at first. After all, Shen Hui had always been very fair. She had never seen her favor anyone.","At this moment, her heart turned cold. She believed Qiao Chen’s words now."]},{"number":568,"title":"Chapter 568 - Did You Post on the School Forum?","paragraphs":["Wu Jie’s heart raced as she thought about it.","When Principal Yu, who was sitting behind his desk, saw her enter, he covered his mouth with his hand and coughed softly. Then, he said gently, “Ahem, Student Wu Jie is here.”","Wu Jie didn’t dare to look him in the eye. She lowered her head and greeted politely, “Hello, Principal.”","“Hello.” Principal Yu was in his forties. His voice was gentle, and he did not blame her. Instead, he advised her not to be nervous. “Student Wu Jie, don’t be nervous. I got Teacher Liu to call you to my office because I have something to ask you.”","Wu Jie let out a sigh of relief. Her rapidly beating heart was slightly less nervous. She looked up with a tense expression and looked at the man sitting in the swivel chair. Her voice was very soft and small. “Principal, you’re asking...”","She knew what Principal Yu wanted to ask. It was definitely related to the post she made last night. She had long been mentally prepared.","Principal Yu took in her expression of “facing death with equanimity” and restrained his gentleness. Then, his expression gradually became serious. He crossed his hands and placed them on the table, then looked at the girl standing in the middle of the office and asked, “Did you post the thread on the school’s forum?”","Unexpectedly, Wu Jie did not have any intention of backing down. She raised her head, straightened her back, and nodded. “Yes, I posted it. I reported Classmate Qiao Nian for breaking the rules...”","The teachers in the principal’s office were all stunned.","Ever since she entered the school, she had always been a weak and timid person. No one could tell that she was the kind of person who would report her classmates on the school’s forum in the middle of the night. Now that she admitted her actions without hesitation, the head teachers were all shocked.","Shen Hui frowned and looked at her. She said anxiously, “Why did you do it? You could have told me first if there was anything...”","Before she could finish, Wu Jie clenched her fists tightly and turned to look at her. Biting her lips stubbornly, she asked, “If I had told you, Teacher Shen, would you have punished Qiao Nian?”","“...” Shen Hui frowned even more tightly. She didn’t understand what she meant. Why did her words sound like she was usually very protective of Qiao Nian? However, as a qualified teacher, even if she already had some emotions in her heart, Shen Hui still told her seriously, “I would have investigated clearly first and found Qiao Nian to ask if it was true. Then, I would have reported it to the Academic Affairs Office and waited for the school to make a decision.”","Wu Jie didn’t believe her at all. Her eyes behind her glasses were cold. She clenched her fists tightly and braced herself. “If Qiao Nian refused to admit it, would you still protect her?”","“I don’t know what you mean by this question. Do you mean that regardless of whether Qiao Nian admits it or not, I should be certain that she has violated the school rules and refuse to protect her?”","Shen Hui’s face darkened, her eyes sharp and serious.","“You guys are classmates. I have never done anything to protect anyone in the past. If there are any problems, we should be speaking the truth instead of bringing our personal emotions into it.”","Wu Jie bit her lip and remained silent, looking aggrieved and stubborn.","“I’m not saying that you can’t report people who violate the school rules. I’m just saying that you have a better way to do this. You shouldn’t have used this kind of method to expose your classmate. What if you made a mistake? What if Qiao Nian didn’t beat someone outside the school as you said? How are you going to make up for this?”"]},{"number":569,"title":"Chapter 569 - Calling Qiao Nian to School","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Wu Jie was usually good at her studies and was a good seedling to enter a key university. Shen Hui didn’t want her to get into a dead-end three months before the college entrance examination and ruin herself.","After criticizing her severely, she said gently, “The school will investigate the problem you’ve reported. Delete the post on the forum first and don’t expand the impact of this matter.”","When Wu Jie heard this, she gritted her teeth and suddenly raised her head. She looked at her stubbornly and said, “So Teacher Shen wants to protect Qiao Nian, right?”","Shen Hui didn’t understand why she refused to listen. She pulled a long face and said loudly, “I’m not protecting anyone. It’s just that this matter hasn’t been clarified yet. You can’t unilaterally spread false news on the Internet! This will cause adverse effects to the other students.”","Wu Jie didn’t hear a single word that she said. Her mind was filled with thoughts about the joint examination.","When she heard this, she looked up at the group of form teachers and headmasters in the office. Her hands were clenched into fists as she bit her lips and said firmly, “I know that Qiao Nian did well in Qing University’s joint examination this time. She’s the only one in our school who got into Qing University. The school will definitely not deal with her for the sake of enrollment and glory. That’s why I posted on the forum. I want to blow this matter up!","“So what if she’s good at her studies? For a student who can easily beat someone to a pulp, staying in school is just a black sheep! Today, she can injure others outside the school, and tomorrow, she can bully the other students in school.”","She spoke as if she was righteous and upright. It was as if what she had said was true, and that she had reported Qiao Nian without any selfish motives.","“I want to stand up on behalf of my righteous classmates and report her for this behavior! Before the school deals with her, I will not delete the post on the forum. If you want to delete it, you can get the forum administrator to do it. But if you forcefully delete the post, it will only let the students of the other grades know that Qiao Nian has special privileges in First High School...”","The teachers in the third year of high school looked at each other when they heard this. They had never seen a student who refused to listen and insisted on fooling around.","For a moment, they did not know what to do.","If they just deleted the post on the forum, as she had said, the students of the other grades and their parents who didn’t know the inside story would think that the school was protecting a student who had broken the school rules.","If they didn’t delete it, they would leave the thread alone, and this matter wouldn’t be investigated at all. If they didn’t care about such a post with subjective assumptions, it would be harmful to Class A’s Qiao Nian.","Furthermore, it wasn’t easy for the school to have a good seedling, and she had also been admitted to Qing University. They didn’t understand why Wu Jie had to make things so chaotic. They were all classmates. Why couldn’t she tell the teacher in private like Shen Hui had said and let the school investigate before resolving the matter?","When the form teacher of Class C saw that this matter couldn’t be resolved properly, she glanced at the girl who stood stubbornly on the spot and insisted that they give her an explanation. She looked up at the principal and asked softly, “Principal, how do you think we should handle this now...”","Principal Yu also knew that this matter could not continue like this. Firstly, it would tarnish the school’s reputation. Secondly, Qiao Nian might even take the college entrance examination in the future. How could they continue like this? If this continued, the students’ parents would also cause trouble if they saw this.","He supported his forehead with his hand and said with a headache, “Teacher Shen, please call Qiao Nian and ask her to come to school.”"]},{"number":570,"title":"Chapter 570 - Tsk, One Million to Three Million","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","At the city hospital.","Qiao Nian had just watched Uncle Chen leave the ward.","Chen Yuan followed behind her.","Qiao Nian closed the door and led him to the corner of the corridor. Then, she leaned against the wall and looked at him.","“When are you going back to school?”","“I don’t know yet. I’ll stay in the hospital and take care of my dad for now.”","Chen Yuan still didn’t know that most of Wei Qi’s matters had been resolved. When he saw her asking about his school, his expression was obscure and ugly. From the corner of his eye, he saw the man waiting for Qiao Nian not far away.","He had seen him several times.","It was Ye Wangchuan.","He seemed to be Sister Nian’s good friend from Beijing.","However, he was a man. Even if he hadn’t grown into a real man, he knew that men looked at women differently.","When Chen Yuan thought of this, he felt bitter. Even though he had long planned to give up, he still felt uncomfortable when he looked at the girl in front of him. He lowered his eyes and whispered, “...When he feels better, I’ll think of a way to see if I can further my studies in the future.”","When Qiao Nian heard this, she frowned and looked at him angrily. “You’re not going to take the college entrance examination?”","“I...” Chen Yuan lowered his head, not knowing what to say.","Of course, he wanted to take the college entrance examination. However, he had signed a confession letter previously, and there were punishments on his record. No university would want him even if he took the college entrance examination. Why waste three months?","“Why?” After he didn’t say anything after a long time, Qiao Nian thought of something. Her slightly furrowed eyebrows gradually relaxed as she straightened her back and walked over with long and straight legs. She stood facing him and asked with a slightly hoarse voice, “Is it because of Wei Qi?”","Chen Yuan looked up and pursed his lips without saying anything.","But his eyes betrayed his heart.","Qiao Nian could tell at a glance that he had come to this decision because Wei Qi had forced him to sign the confession letter. He thought that he was being disciplined, so he said he wouldn’t take the college entrance examination and would further his studies in the future.","Speaking of which, Chen Yuan and Aunt Chen had the same personality. They were the kind of people who would rather swallow their teeth than tell her because they were afraid of troubling her.","Actually, many things were nothing to her. It wasn’t troublesome at all.","Furthermore, Aunt Chen and her family had treated her so well back then. Even if it was troublesome, she was willing!","Qiao Nian’s eyebrows were a little cold. She patted his shoulder and said softly, “Your punishment has been resolved. Did someone from the Wei family come to look for you?”","Speaking of this, Chen Yuan thought of the group of people who had come last night. He shook his head and looked at her. “A few people came. They gave me a cheque for three million, but I didn’t take it.”","Qiao Nian retracted her hand and responded with an “oh.” It was not strange at all. It had changed from one million to three million. Someone must have played a part in this. She looked at him and said indifferently, “Next time they give it to you, take it. They should have given it in the first place. It’s not like you’re taking advantage of them!”","Chen Yuan shook his head. His still young face was firm and brave. He only said, “I don’t want their money, and neither do my parents.”","If they took that money, it meant that they had forgiven each other.","When Qiao Nian heard that Aunt Chen did not want the money, she did not say anything else. At this moment, her phone rang.","Qiao Nian took it out and looked at the caller ID. It was Shen Hui. She didn’t pick up. Her eyes narrowed as she hung up.","She looked up and said, “Remember to go to school tomorrow.”","With that, she waved the phone in her hand. “I’m leaving.”","Then, she turned around and walked away..."]},{"number":571,"title":"Chapter 571 - Are You Really Not Jealous at All?","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","“Have you finished chatting with Chen Yuan?”","As soon as Qiao Nian came over, she saw the man leaning against the wall straighten up and walk toward her. His long black trench coat looked tall and impressive on him, making him quite eye-catching.","She retracted her gaze and nodded. For some reason, she paused again and added, “I told him to go to school tomorrow. Aunt Chen has been worried about him these past few days. I just convinced her to go back to sleep. Uncle Chen is bedridden and can’t control him. I’m the only one who’s able to control him.”","Ye Wangchuan’s eyebrows rose as he walked in front. There was a hint of unhappiness in his deep eyes, but it dissipated like clouds. His voice was low and alluring. “I know you’re on good terms with the Chen family. Uncle Chen and Aunt Chen are not in good health. You treat Chen Yuan as your younger brother and your friend. It’s okay to take care of him.”","Fortunately, Gu San did not follow.","If Gu San came along, he would definitely ask him, “Master Wang, do you really think so? You weren’t jealous at all when you saw Miss Qiao putting her hand on Chen Yuan’s shoulder?”","However, Gu San wasn’t around, and Qiao Nian didn’t think about it.","When they got into the car, Qiao Nian had just put on her seatbelt when Shen Hui called again.","She rolled her eyes and took out her phone. Although she was feeling very frustrated, she answered the call politely, “Hello, Teacher Shen.”","Ye Wangchuan turned the car around and placed his hand on the steering wheel. He was in no hurry to drive back. Instead, he waited patiently for her to answer the call.","It was unknown what the other party was talking about. Qiao Nian frowned slightly, her exquisite eyes filled with impatience. She nodded and said, “I’m outside. I’ll go over later.”","Where was she going? Ye Wangchuan raised his eyebrows and looked at her.","Qiao Nian didn’t look in his direction. She rolled down the car window and fresh air flowed in from outside. She looked out of the car window, holding her phone in one hand and resting the other on the window. She exuded a strong sense of laziness.","“Okay, I understand. Bye.”","Two minutes later, she hung up and put down her phone. Then, she said to the man beside her in a deep voice, “I’m going to the school for a while. I have something on.”","“I’ll send you there.” Ye Wangchuan had been waiting for her to call. After she made the call, he said naturally, “Since I have nothing on today, I’ll accompany you.”","In the past, Qiao Nian would have definitely said no. However, she didn’t say anything today.","On the way from the city hospital to the school, she flipped through the posts on the school’s forum. Perhaps because all the students had gone to school, that post became even more popular. The number of views broke 10,000, and more people replied to it.","Qiao Nian lowered her eyes and casually flipped through it. She saw many people from Class A standing up for her.","[Indigo Collar: I’m from Class A, why haven’t I seen Sister Nian bully anyone?]","[I’ll carry a gun and pry open the earth: Those who took the opportunity to scold and spout nonsense in the posts, come to Class A to look for your sister if you have the guts. Your sister will never change her name no matter what. She’s Jiang Tingting from Class A. I’ll be waiting for you!]","[Figure Jumping Water: I’m also from Class A. The post says that Qiao Nian is forming cliques in class and is isolating the other students. It’s too much of an exaggeration. I can only say that she’s very popular and that everyone likes to play with her. Also, Wu Jie said that the matter of Qiao Nian injuring someone has not been investigated clearly. She’s the only one talking about it. I think it’s best to treat it rationally.. There’s no need to stand out and criticize her first, lest you slap yourself in the face.]"]},{"number":572,"title":"Chapter 572 - The First Wave of Humiliation","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian scrolled through the comments and saw that many people were attacking her.","They said that she only got first place through the back door.","Some people also said that she was jealous of Qiao Chen. In order to squeeze out the position of the school belle, she had schemed and forced Qiao Chen to transfer schools. In the end, Qiao Chen turned around and got into Qing University, but their school did not get to bask in her glory...","She took a look. Most of the people were shouting and cursing with other people’s support.","She could guess the identity of the people making a fuss in the thread. Needless to say, they were most likely the people following Qiao Chen.","Qiao Nian couldn’t be bothered to continue reading. She casually opened an app, and Wu Jie’s post on First High School’s forum disappeared.","She had deleted the post.","Qiao Nian took out her phone’s contact list and made a call.","“Uncle Shen, please bring Qiao Chen along to school.”","...","On the other side, Shen Jingyan happened to be at the Qiao Residence.","He hung up and turned around to see Wei Ling and Qiao Chen coming down from the second floor.","Wei Ling hadn’t slept well these past two days. Her exquisite makeup couldn’t hide her fatigue. She didn’t look as poised and elegant as before, but her aura was still there. Although her face did not look good, the pride and arrogance nurtured by life could still be seen in her.","She was talking to Qiao Chen.","“You still have to practice this song a little more. Many masters from the music industry will be attending this exchange. With your current standards, you still won’t be able to amaze Master Nie. Fortunately, there’s still half a month left. During this period of time, you can only practice more, especially when facing someone like Zhui Guang who isn’t on the right track. You can only walk the path of a stupid bird flying first. Hard work can make up for your lack of talent...”","When Qiao Chen heard her use a light tone to say that she couldn’t compare to Zhui Guang and could only rely on hard work to make up for the difference, she felt a little uncomfortable inside. However, she was an extremely sensible person. She was very smart and did not rebut Wei Ling. She hugged the score and nodded obediently. “I understand, Aunt. I will practice more.”","“Okay.” Wei Ling’s expression softened a little. She looked at her again and said half-heartedly, “You don’t have to worry too much. I’ll definitely make Master Nie accept you this time.”","Even if she had to use her family’s name this time, she had to make Master Nie accept Qiao Chen. This way, the gap between her and that wolf cub would widen!","When Wei Ling thought of this, she thought of her younger brother, who was still at the police station. The blood in her chest surged, and she almost couldn’t hold back her anger. Her eyes were gloomy as she looked at the girl beside her and asked, “By the way, has the date of your commemoration banquet been fixed? Which hotel is it?”","“Yes, it’s in the banquet hall on the third floor of Huanyu Hotel.” When Qiao Chen heard her mention the banquet, she nervously held the score in her hands tightly and did not dare to look at her. Her heart was in a mess as she replied very softly, “It’s this weekend.”","When she woke up in the morning, she especially went on First High School’s forums. Indeed, she saw Wu Jie’s post.","She casually shared the post with Xu Xu and Cai Yan and then ignored it.","Qiao Chen pursed her lips and calculated the time in her heart.","With Xu Xu and the others posting comments to set the pace, the matter should have been more or less settled. She just didn’t know how the school would handle Qiao Nian.","Since the matter had blown up so much, the school definitely had to give an explanation to the other students and their parents. It was impossible for them to shield Qiao Nian anymore!","With this thought, Qiao Chen felt slightly relieved and let out a sigh of relief."]},{"number":573,"title":"Chapter 573 - Chen Chen, Dont You Know What Happened at School?","paragraphs":["Wei Ling didn’t notice the change in her expression. She nodded and said calmly, “Your commemoration banquet is in the banquet hall on the third floor of Huanyu Hotel this weekend?”","“Yes, Aunt.”","Wei Ling adjusted her shawl and said coldly, “I understand. I’ll call Professor Cheng Wu later and tell him.”","Qiao Chen couldn’t hide the joy in her eyes. Before she was done being happy, she saw Shen Jingyan walking to the staircase with his phone. He frowned and asked her, “Chen Chen, do you know what happened in First High School?”","Qiao Chen’s smile froze as she subconsciously hugged the score in her arms tightly. Her expression did not look good as she shook her head nervously. “I... I don’t know.”","Wei Ling glanced at her and turned to look at Shen Jingyan. “What happened?”","“I don’t know, either.” Shen Jingyan held his phone and said with a headache, “Nian Nian called me just now and asked me to bring Chen Chen to school. I think something happened there.”","When Wei Ling heard Qiao Nian’s name, her expression darkened. She pulled a long face and said unhappily, “What’s she trying to do again?! Chen Chen is no longer a student of First High School. Why did she ask you to bring her over?”","“I don’t know. That’s why I asked if Chen Chen knew.”","Shen Jingyan also remembered that Qiao Chen had transferred her school register to Rao City’s Fifth High School before she participated in Qing University’s joint examination. Logically speaking, she was not under First High School’s jurisdiction. But...","He raised his head and looked at Qiao Chen. His eyes were a little warm as he said gently, “Chen Chen, go and pack up. Come with me to First High School to see what’s going on.”","A trace of coldness appeared on Wei Ling’s lips as she snorted coldly. Although her expression was ugly, she still raised her chin and did not say anything.","Wei Qi was still in her hands. Even if she hated Qiao Nian to the core, she could only suppress her temper and let it be.","...","At this moment, the black Phaeton had stopped in front of the school building.","Ye Wangchuan opened the door and got out with her. He said naturally, “I’ll go up with you.”","Initially, Qiao Nian didn’t want him to follow her. However, her eyebrows moved slightly and she did not say anything in the end. She just nodded indifferently and walked in front.","This wasn’t her first time going to the principal’s office. She had been there a few times before. Qiao Nian was very familiar with the way and arrived outside very quickly.","She didn’t barge in. Instead, she stood at the door and knocked politely twice. Her eyes were filled with banditry as she said in a deep voice, “Sir, I’m Qiao Nian. Can I come in?”","The principal’s voice immediately came from inside.","“Come in.”","Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and lowered the brim of her hat before walking in.","She walked slowly and even a little casually. Her posture was relaxed, but her aura was so strong that it was difficult to ignore her existence.","“She’s Qiao Nian?”","As soon as Qiao Nian entered, she heard a woman’s sharp voice.","Her voice was frivolous and filled with disdain. “You look like a hooligan. No wonder you fought outside the school!”","Tsk~","Qiao Nian looked up lazily and saw quite a lot of people inside the office. Other than Principal Yu, a few Year Three form teachers were also there. There were also a few middle-aged men and women about the same age as the form teachers. Next was Wu Jie, who was standing in the corner silently.","Perhaps sensing her gaze, the girl standing in the corner quickly looked up and glanced in her direction. She then immediately lowered her head guiltily and avoided her gaze."]},{"number":574,"title":"Chapter 574 - Im Her Guardian. Whats Wrong?","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian didn’t care. She only glanced at her and slowly retracted her gaze. She walked up to Shen Hui and restrained her arrogant expression, then said politely, “Teacher Shen.”","“You’re here?” Shen Hui rubbed her head and said with a headache, “I didn’t want to call you here, but...”","With the situation being like this, Wu Jie had even called her parents over.","Wu Jie’s parents were also members of the Home Committee. When her mother caused a ruckus in the parents’ group chat, many parents of the Home Committee also ran to the school and asked them to give an explanation.","She didn’t expect Wu Jie to have so many thoughts.","She could only get Qiao Nian to come over.","Before she could finish, Qiao Nian already knew what was going on. She held her shoulders and lowered her eyes comfortingly. “I know, Teacher Shen. You don’t have to explain to me.”","“You were the one who fought with someone outside the school and crippled him. You even bullied my daughter in school and formed gangs to isolate the other students?”","When the woman saw that no one was paying attention to her, her face darkened again and she questioned loudly.","“Where are your parents? Are you the only one here? Don’t your parents care about you?”","Ye Wangchuan had his hands in his pockets. His face was rather eye-catching. From the moment he entered, he had deliberately restrained his aura. At this moment, he narrowed his eyes and looked at the troublemaker. He said loudly, “I’m her guardian. What’s wrong?”","When the principal saw him, the back of his head hurt. Why was this master coming to school with her? Were they treating this matter lightly?","Hopefully, this matter could be settled properly today. Otherwise... it was still a question if his position as First High School’s principal could be kept.","“You’re her guardian?”","The woman with curly hair looked at him in disbelief. “So young? Don’t tell me she found someone outside the school to pretend to be her guardian.”","No one had spoken to him in such a tone in a long time. Ye Wangchuan raised his eyebrows in amusement.","The principal was afraid that he would be angry, so he quickly explained, “Wu Jie’s mother, this is Qiao Nian’s guardian. I’ve seen him before.”","“Is he really her guardian?”","Liu Linuo still did not believe him. She looked at Ye Wangchuan suspiciously and slowly retracted her gaze. She reluctantly gave the principal some face and said, “Alright. Since the principal has said so, I’ll treat him as Qiao Nian’s guardian. She’s here herself and so is the guardian. The school should give us an explanation for her violation of the school rules, right?”","“About this...” Principal Yu quickly glanced at the silent man standing at the side and said, “We haven’t investigated this matter clearly yet. Besides, we just called a few students from Class A over. They all said that Qiao Nian did not bully anyone in the class. We haven’t seen her fight anyone, either. It was all Wu Jie talking about it. We still don’t know the specifics...”","The woman sitting there suddenly raised her voice and questioned unhappily, “Principal Yu, are you saying that my daughter is lying? I know my daughter the best. She’s good at her studies and has a good personality. She has been one of the top students in the school since she was young. Her grades are also among the top in your school. She can’t be lying.","“Since she said it, she must have been bullied by this hooligan a lot! Since her classmates don’t dare to say it, it means that she’s used to being domineering in class. No one dares to make a sound.”"]},{"number":575,"title":"Chapter 575 - Finally Here","paragraphs":["Shameless and unreasonable!","Shen Hui was furious. She stood up and spoke up for Qiao Nian. “Madam Liu, I’m their form teacher. I’ve never heard of Qiao Nian bullying anyone. The students in her class are not threatened, either. They’re just telling the truth!”","“Haha.” Liu Linuo folded her arms and looked at her coldly. “I didn’t believe Wu Jie when she said your school would cover for her. I’ve finally seen it for myself!","“Alright, you said she didn’t bully her classmates. I’ll believe it. Then, what about her breaking the school rules? It can’t be that my daughter is slandering her.”","“This...” Shen Hui had yet to ask Qiao Nian about the fight. She hesitated and did not answer immediately.","A mocking expression appeared on the middle-aged woman’s face as she sneered and said, “Don’t say you haven’t investigated clearly! You can find out about this at the police station. Besides, she beat someone up. The patient must still be lying in the hospital. You can find out if you want to.","“I’ll represent the Home Committee to ask you now. How is your school going to handle her violation of the school rules?”","Without waiting for Shen Hui and the others to speak, she continued, “According to the school rules, she must definitely be punished. Her offense is so serious, and us parents have the same intention. We want her to be expelled!”","The other members of the Home Committee who had come to the office also spoke up. In the end, it meant that they wanted the school to expel Qiao Nian.","Principal Yu was annoyed. When he looked at the young master’s eyes that were gradually turning cold, he felt like he was being sandwiched between them. He ignored the parents and turned to ask Qiao Nian gently, “Qiao Nian, have you seen Wu Jie’s post on the forum?”","Qiao Nian had her hands in her pockets and her eyes were dark. She admitted bluntly, “I have.”","“Then, about the beating...”","Qiao Nian looked up at him and did not answer directly. Instead, she looked at the aggressive woman. Without any expression on her face, she said calmly, “You all asked to expel me if I broke the school rules. If your daughter broke the school rules, would you also get the school to expel her?”","“...What do you mean?” Liu Linna was shocked by the coldness in her eyes and did not answer immediately. After her heart palpitated, she slowly came back to her senses and frowned. She replied, “Of course...”","“Okay.” Qiao Nian nodded and looked at the girl standing in the corner. Her eyes were very calm as if she was looking at a stranger. She said calmly, “I don’t need the school to expel her, either. The college entrance examination is in three months. I’ll just give her the punishment she deserves.”","She spoke indifferently as if Wu Jie had already been punished.","The girl in the corner with thick glasses suddenly looked up. Her eyes were red as she clenched her fists tightly and said indignantly, “Qiao Nian, you don’t have to scare me. It’s a fact that you sent him to the hospital. I’m not framing you!”","“Tsk.” The girl who had been criticized looked sloppy. She pushed down the brim of her hat, and her exquisite face looked quite evil. She smiled faintly and did not continue to look at Wu Jie. Instead, she said calmly, “Whether you’re telling the truth or not, we’ll know when she comes.”","...","Shen Jingyan arrived faster than expected.","Qiao Chen followed him all the way to the principal’s office. The closer she got to the office, the more nervous she became. Her heart was beating rapidly and she kept feeling uneasy."]},{"number":576,"title":"Chapter 576 - Second Wave of Humiliation","paragraphs":["Seeing that Shen Jingyan had already arrived at the entrance of the Principal’s office, Qiao Chen’s hands and back tensed. She entered with him.","“Apologies for the wait. There was a jam on the way.”","Shen Jingyan started with the civilities.","The atmosphere in the office was rather heavy. Wu Jie’s mother and the other committee members were unhappy with how the school had handled the matter and had been pushing the Principal to punish Qiao Nian before they arrived.","Qiao Nian casually leaned against the seat and used her cell phone after talking to Wu Jie.","She didn’t say anything now, and Ye Wangchuan was calm as well. He was sitting not too far from her with an unreadable expression. He wasn’t using his phone, but rather leisurely sipping the water that the Class C Form Teacher had handed him.","Shen Jingyan saw his imposing presence the moment he entered. His heart sank right away...","With Ye Wangchuan around, he couldn’t have been called to the office for anything good!","But as of now, he had no idea what exactly he was here for.","Shen Jingyan felt extremely uneasy. His gaze landed upon the slender figure leaning on the seat not too far away.","It was October and almost winter in Rao City. The temperature difference each day was huge, and it was chilly today as the clouds had veiled the sun.","The girl on her cell phone was wearing a thin hoodie and an outer jacket that hung loosely by her shoulders. Her cap was on, and only half her face was revealed. Her lips were rather pale-colored but beautifully shaped, even when slightly pursed. She looked extremely easy in her own place.","“Oh, I was wondering who you called. He’s your parent?”","Wu Jie’s mother’s expression darkened slightly. She immediately made snide remarks once Shen Jingyan entered.","“You asked us to wait for him, and we waited. Now that he’s here, shouldn’t you give us an explanation?”","Wu Jie was actually a little flustered and even nervous when she saw Qiao Chen enter with a middle-aged man. But she did not appear that way on the surface. Although she was slightly tense when she first entered the Principal’s office, she eventually managed to hold it together. Besides the one time she lost her cool when Qiao Nian angered her, she had presented herself as a good student with her glasses on and few words. She looked quiet and gentle, which made Qiao Nian appear more disobedient in contrast.","So, even though Wu Jie panicked a little when she saw Qiao Chen coming in, she simply bit her lip and lowered her head. She didn’t make any eye contact with Qiao Chen, nor did she say hello, as if she wasn’t too close to her.","However, given her tender age, no matter how calm she was, she would still show tension. Wu Jie’s hands on her knees unconsciously gripped her clothes, and the knuckles of her fingers turned white.","Others might not have noticed this detail, but Ye Wangchuan was different. All her changes since Qiao Chen’s appearance were captured in his bright and clear eyes.","Ye Wangchuan did not expose her. He continued sipping his water every once in a while, waiting for Qiao Nian to deal with it.","Qiao Nian had kept her cell phone when Shen Jingyan entered. She looked up expressionlessly and greeted him. “Uncle Shen, you’re here.”","“The roads were a little congested, so I was held up.” Shen Jingyan was confused by the scene. He looked at her and asked, “Nian Nian, what’s going on?”"]},{"number":577,"title":"Chapter 577 - Sister Nian Is Not to Be Trifled With","paragraphs":["He wanted to ask the teachers and parents what was going on. What explanation was the parent asking for?","He genuinely had no idea.","But Qiao Chen, who was standing behind him obediently, knew exactly what was going on. Her face went pale and she lowered her head, biting her lip. She tried her best not to attract any attention.","Her heart was racing and almost jumping out of her chest.","It seemed like Wu Jie had successfully blown up the matter of Qiao Nian hitting someone. She was even smart enough to get the parents to create trouble at school... As she guessed, the school dared not defend Qiao Nian so openly, and the time had finally come for the school to settle the issue.","She dug her fingernails into her palms. Her eyes were flickering, and she was excited but also uncertain. She had no idea why Qiao Nian called her here.","Also, Shen Jingyan’s attitude towards Qiao Nian made her feel even less confident about the situation.","Qiao Nian had beaten Wei Qi up and then pulled strings to settle the matter. Even if Uncle did not want to hold it against Qiao Nian on the account that they were relatives, he shouldn’t be acting like he was afraid of her.","Having spent a month in Beijing, Qiao Chen was very clear about the Shen Family’s status. She knew how capable her uncle was and how many high-profile figures were in touch with the Shen Family on a daily basis.","No matter how good Qiao Nian was, which meant that even if she did well enough to enter Qing University and had a rather well-to-do biological family... all of these added up would still not allow her to surpass the Shen Family. She had no idea why Shen Jingyan had to be so nice to her.","Qiao Nian saw the girl behind Shen Jingyan and her hands balled up into fists.","She smiled almost evilly and put her arms akimbo as she glared coldly at Shen Jingyan, who had asked her the question. Her voice was slightly hoarse and threatening as she said, “It’s nothing much. Qiao Chen told my classmates that I beat someone outside until he became crippled. Now they’re asking me for an explanation, wanting to make things public.”","Qiao Chen looked up and widened her eyes. She couldn’t believe that Qiao Nian said it so plainly and directly in front of everyone!","She was saying that Qiao Chen instigated Wu Jie!","Was she not afraid that Qiao Chen herself would not admit it?!","Qiao Nian glanced at her calmly and with indifference as if she did not know fear.","“You said you beat someone...” Shen Jingyan doubted his hearing and subconsciously repeated what Qiao Nian said. Then, he stopped himself and turned to Qiao Chen hiding behind him. Although he was trying to suppress his anger, his tone was not too pleasant. “Chen Chen, what exactly is going on!”","Qiao Chen hadn’t expected him to ask her about it instead of Qiao Nian. Seeing how angry he looked, her heart pumped wildly and her face went pale. She opened her mouth, shook her head, and denied it. “I- I didn’t.”","Then, she calmed herself down and looked aggrieved. She went on, “Uncle, you know that I spend all day practicing on the piano with Aunt. I didn’t even come to school, how could I find trouble with her...”","This was true.","Shen Jingyan furrowed his brows slightly, but his features had softened. He turned back to Qiao Nian and asked, “Nian Nian, did you get it wrong? I was at the Qiao household as well. She isn’t lying, she really spends all day practicing on the piano with Aunt Wei. She doesn’t even have time to be on her cell phone.”","Qiao Nian didn’t want to beat about the bush. Her gaze was piercing as she asked him, “Then, how does Wu Jie know about Wei Qi’s matter?”"]},{"number":578,"title":"Chapter 578 - Slapping Evidence on Her Face","paragraphs":["“Chen Yuan isn’t back in school yet and even my friends don’t know about this. Only Wu Jie had lunch with her yesterday.”","Qiao Nian sounded calm and indifferent, but also extremely piercing. “I don’t think there’s a need to blow things up this way! Do you think I told Wu Jie this, or she did?”","Shen Jingyan’s political ups and downs all these decades were not for nothing.","He already knew what had happened after she said that.","His expression sank as he tried to hide the fury in his eyes. He didn’t say anything as he turned to face Qiao Chen with eyes as cold as ice.","Qiao Chen looked extremely anxious. She could barely stand still and her tears were about to fall. She tried explaining, “I... I did talk about Wei Qi’s matter. But I was just chatting with my classmates and accidentally spilled it. I didn’t join in the conversation and didn’t mean to blow this up.”","She was sniffling and sobbing, looking very pitiful indeed.","Qiao Nian had run out of patience long ago. After hearing what she said, she took her cell phone out and tossed it in front of Shen Jingyan.","“This is regarding the post on the school’s forum. I’ve deleted the post itself, but I kept the IDs of a few people involved. They’re all close friends of Qiao Chen’s, you can have a look. Also, there’s a screenshot at the back. It’s a chat between her and someone with the ID name Sun Ascension. It was sent at eight in the morning, and she had forwarded the post to get her to check it out.”","Qiao Chen never expected her to be able to get hold of this. Her face went pale and her eyes were full of fear. Her fists had long been clenched.","How did Qiao Nian get hold of her chat records?!","Qiao Nian couldn’t be bothered to look into her eyes. She had one hand on her hip and pulled her cap slightly lower. With just a cold side profile, she said, “You can say that you spilled it accidentally when chatting with your friends in person, but did you also accidentally send this message? You were on the phone with Wu Jie for over 10 minutes last night, was that also an accidental call?”","Every last bit of color faded from Qiao Chen’s face. Her eyes were wide with panic, and she felt like she was losing her balance.","“I...”","Faced with Shen Jingyan’s stern look, she opened her mouth, but not a word escaped.","As the fear gripped her, she gripped Shen Jingyan’s elbow and hurriedly explained, “She called me to ask about the examinations. We didn’t talk about much before her mother went to her and she hung up. That post... I stumbled upon it this morning and just forwarded it to my friend. I didn’t get them to create trouble on that post...”","She looked at the girl in the corner and gave her a warning side-eye. She then tightened her grasp on Shen Jingyan’s elbow and said sadly, “Uncle, trust me, I really had no idea about this. You can ask Wu Jie, we were just talking about the examinations last night.”","“There’s no need to ask her.” Shen Jingyan was expressionless. He didn’t blame her, but the coldness in his eyes already sent a chill down Qiao Chen’s spine.","She was as pale as could be and sobbing so pitifully. Her vulnerability could even tug at your heartstrings. “Uncle, I...”","Shen Jingyan didn’t look at her. He shook her off and turned towards Principal Yu sitting solemnly at the side. “Principal, regarding the rumors about Qiao Nian fighting going around school...”"]},{"number":579,"title":"Chapter 579 - Qiao Chen Being Pinned to the Ground","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Principal Yu watched how it unfolded and had some idea where things were headed. He politely said, “Yes, please go on.”","“This is all a misunderstanding. There was no fight between the two of them. My brother-in-law slipped and fell down the stairs, breaking his ribs. I’m not sure where Chen Chen heard this from. Actually, Qiao Nian just happened to be at the scene, but it wasn’t her doing. It was my brother-in-law’s carelessness...” Shen Jingyan spoke in a calm and collected manner, evidently not an ordinary figure.","Qiao Chen’s face contorted into a strange expression of disbelief.","She knew very well that Wei Qi couldn’t have fallen down the stairs and broken three ribs. It was surely Qiao Nian’s doing.","They were in Beijing back then, and Wei Ling had called him but could not get through. It was Wei Qi’s subordinate who said that Wei Qi had been beaten up by Qiao Nian.","Shen Jingyan had also rushed back with her because of this.","Why did her uncle lie for Qiao Nian?","Shen Jingyan said seriously but steadily, “Chen Chen blabbered to her friends without being sure of the actual matter, causing the school such inconvenience. I’m very sorry about that. I will educate her properly when we go back.”","He immediately called out to Qiao Chen.","“Chen Chen, apologize to the principal!”","Everyone present was surprised by how he had handled the matter so swiftly and coldly. They weren’t expecting such a turn of events.","Qiao Chen inched forward and felt the glares from all directions. It was so humiliating, almost as if someone had stripped her from top to bottom. All the blood had been drained from her face, and she was biting her lip so hard it was almost torn. When she spoke, it was soft as a mosquito buzzing. “I’m sorry, Principal Yu. It’s all my fault. I didn’t get things right...”","I-It wasn’t like this!","Qiao Nian had beaten someone up. Why was she the one apologizing now?","Shen Jingyan’s face was cold and stern. After she was done apologizing to the principal, he ordered, “Qiao Nian as well, you should apologize to her too.”","Qiao Chen felt her brain tumble, and all of a sudden, her face flushed. Her head snapped up, but once her gaze met Shen Jingyan’s, she quickly lowered her eyes. Her fingernails dug into her skin.","She walked towards Qiao Nian and, between clenched teeth, said, “Sister, I’m sorry, I didn’t know I’d gotten it wrong. I didn’t intend for Wu Jie to frame you on the forum. I just mentioned it casually. Also, the message this morning... I really did not mean anything by that, they might have understood me wrongly... that’s why they commented inappropriate things on the forum. I didn’t know it would cause you so much trouble.”","She put it so nicely. Qiao Nian didn’t expect her to try to push the blame even at a time like this. Between the lines, she was mentioning everyone else’s faults and not her own!","She mentioned it casually, not expecting Wu Jie to post about it online.","She sent the message casually, not expecting the Class B students to stand up for her.","As such, she was the most innocent person. She had obviously “done nothing”, but was being made to apologize for no rhyme or reason now.","This just made Qiao Nian appear unreasonable.","While she remained the ever-innocent Qiao Chen!","“Tsk..” Qiao Nian’s glance was cold as she side-eyed her in annoyance. She asked, “Qiao Chen, you’ve used this trick for over 10 years, aren’t you tired?”"]},{"number":580,"title":"Chapter 580 - Social Behaviour Disorder, Its an Illness","paragraphs":["Qiao Chen’s teeth almost shattered under the pressure she was clenching them at. But with Shen Jingyan’s eyes on her, she could only pretend not to get what Qiao Nian was saying. She bit her lip and said, “Sister, I’m sincerely apologizing to you. I don’t know why it turned out like that...”","“Huh.” Qiao Nian lowered her cap slightly with a look of annoyance. She turned to her and said coldly, “Enough, I’m tired of this even if you’re not. Do you think you’re still in primary school? Qiao Chen, at 10 you said you didn’t know this, everyone believed you. Now you’re 18, you’re an adult, and you’re still telling me you don’t know anything. There are only two possibilities. The first is that you’re feigning ignorance. If it’s the alternative, I suggest you look for a neurologist!”","She was genuinely frustrated and irritated by Qiao Chen, and she didn’t even try to hide it. She raised a brow and widened her eyes that were filled with anger. “Social behavior disorder, it’s an illness. The earlier you get treated, the better. You might still have a chance at recovery. This way, you wouldn’t still be using the same excuse at 30. I’d be tired of it even if you aren’t. Otherwise, just stay away from me, don’t appear in front of me so much!”","Qiao Chen went red. She could barely keep her face together. If not for Shen Jingyan eyeing her every move from the side, she might have just erupted herself.","But now, she could only lower her head and take all the humiliation without rebuking.","Wu Jie’s mother had watched the drama unfold this whole time, not understanding what the fuss was about. She furrowed her brows and interrupted the rest of them, raising her voice. “You’ve been talking among yourselves for so long, but none of you has given us an explanation. She’s beaten someone up, how is the school going to handle this? I’m going to make this clear right now, we parents will not agree to have a student like her remain in this school. A hooligan like her will influence our children...”","Shen Jingyan could feel the atmosphere in the room go cold.","He dared not look at the man sitting at the side.","The moment he thought about how the young man of the Ye family was still seated there, he felt all prickly in his heart and could barely keep still.","Especially because this involved Wei Qi, this frustrated him further!","Hence, when he heard this unknown parent speak up to cause more trouble, he quickly stepped forward before the principal even had a chance to explain things. He looked at Wu Jie’s mother and said, “I’ve already explained this to the principal. It’s Chen Chen’s fault. She heard it wrongly and went around telling her classmates about it, causing a misunderstanding. I’ve already gotten her to apologize. You should’ve seen it just now!”","Wu Jie’s mother raised a brow and sneered. “Hmph, she called you here. Just because you say it’s a misunderstanding, it stays as a misunderstanding?”","Her gaze landed on the pale girl. Without any sympathy for her, she remarked sharply, “She’s a grown-up. Can’t she tell the difference between falling down the stairs and being beaten up?”","Qiao Chen had been pampered all her life. Back then, before the Qiao Family fell from grace, Shen Qiongzhi and Qiao Weimin treated her like a gem. She never had to deal with so many grievances.","Now, she could only clench her teeth and bear with the insults. Her mind was a mess.","She couldn’t figure out why things had turned out this way.","After being found out by the school, Qiao Nian should be in huge trouble for having beaten someone up. Why was she the one in trouble now?","Shen Jingyan was not as patient as Principal Yu. Seeing how she was still not over this matter, his eyes turned cold and he said, “Madame, the person who’s landed in hospital is my wife’s brother. Why would I be defending anyone here? I said there was no fight, and there’s that. He accidentally fell down the stairs. As to why Chen Chen heard it wrongly, I don’t think I need to give you an explanation.”"]},{"number":581,"title":"Chapter 581 - Shen Jingyan Finally Regrets","paragraphs":["He was in a suit, and given the cut and design, it was evidently a luxury brand. The aura he exuded was extraordinary as well, signaling his status.","Wu Jie’s mother dared not go overboard, but she was frustrated and anxious at this point. Her shrill voice rang out again. “Alright, if you say there wasn’t a fight, then so be it. But how can your child go around telling her friends such untrue stories? Wu Jie only caused such trouble in school because she heard stories from her. As a parent, you’re trying to just get past this by apologizing? Dream on.”","She pointed at Qiao Chen and yelled, “Such a young lady, pretty good-looking at that. But causing so much trouble behind people’s backs. How did your parents raise you? Huh!”","Qiao Chen’s face was like a sheet of paper, about to be ripped into pieces.","In the face of accusation, she felt unbearably aggrieved. Yet, she dared not defend herself, and hence took it all in and simply cried.","But this time, nobody cared about her tears.","Shen Jingyan’s expression turned awful, and he said succinctly, “Chen Chen is in the wrong for spreading falsehoods without checking it first. But she only talked about it, the person who posted it online was Wu Jie, not her.","“She’s about Wu Jie’s age, and she has already apologized for spreading rumors. Wu Jie should take responsibility for her own faults, too.”","This statement was true, as a matter of fact.","The woman who wanted to push the blame could not find anything to rebuke.","Wu Jie was trembling with fear as she turned towards Qiao Chen with a panicked look. She bit her lip for a while and eventually chose to spill it. “Uncle, I was the one who put up the post. But if Qiao Chen had not told me that the school would surely discipline Qiao Nian if they found out about it, I would not have posted it either.”","Shen Jingyan had believed in Qiao Nian from the start. But Qiao Chen had always been so sensible and obedient before him, and she was also his biological niece. Blood was thicker than water. He found himself intuitively defending Qiao Chen, even now. He wanted to believe that she was innocent, that she had made a casual statement mindlessly.","But what Wu Jie had just said completely revealed Qiao Chen’s true colors.","Disappointment took over his face and his features stiffened.","Qiao Chen was scared by the coldness of his expression and rebutted frantically, “Don’t talk rot! I only told you that Qiao Nian was in a fight. I didn’t get you to post anything on the forum. This was all your own doing, don’t pin it onto me!”","With that, she looked up a little worriedly. She was about to burst into tears again as she tugged at Shen Jingyan’s elbow. “Uncle, I really just mentioned it to her...”","“We’ll talk about this when we get home!”","Right after he said that Wu Jie’s mother intervened again. “The trouble has gotten so big and you’re still trying to shirk responsibility. This was all caused by you, why should Wu Jie bear the consequences alone? If there’s punishment, everyone should be punished together. Nobody gets to evade it.”","Qiao Chen started sweating profusely at the thought of punishment.","“Uncle, I cannot be punished...”","She had taken such pains to qualify for Qing University, how could she go to school with a bad record?","Shen Jingyan shook her hand off and remained quiet, not wanting to speak up for her anymore.","That woman was just trying to scare her and she took it so seriously, even losing her composure over it. Her reaction was too different from Qiao Nian’s calm demeanor. At this point, he was really regretting picking Qiao Chen over Qiao Nian because of the unimportant blood ties...","So what if she didn’t make it into Qing University? The Shen Family had the network and financial means, and that child had favorable looks and personality. She wouldn’t do too badly in life.","He must have been blind back then to have chosen Qiao Chen!"]},{"number":582,"title":"Chapter 582 - Knowing to Regret Now","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","“This...” Shen Jingyan just started to say something.","At this point, the man who had been sitting casually and quietly by the side placed his glass on the table. The sound it made wasn’t particularly loud or soft.","The atmosphere in the office was almost chaotic initially. This sound should have gone unnoticed.","Yet, besides Principal Yu who turned towards him, even Shen Jingyan who was about to speak also went quiet. He turned around intuitively as well.","Ye Wangchuan was in a shirt and pants today. The pants made him look especially tall, and his long legs caught the eyes of those present. His black coat accentuated that effect, highlighting his figure.","He was good-looking as it was.","Even someone like Gu San knew about the comment that went around: there were three beautiful views in Beijing—the skies, the seas, and Ye Wangchuan. That was how incredibly handsome he was! His eyes were squinted, and the high nose bridge showed off in his side profile was especially attractive as well. Even Qiao Chen’s gaze was turned to him...","He pursed his lips as his cold eyes exuded a strangely leisurely feeling. “Mr. Shen, how you educate your child is your personal matter. Since this case has been clarified, can we leave now?”","The first sentence was meant for Shen Jingyan, while the second was for Principal Yu.","Principal Yu reacted instantly and quickly got out of his seat. He smiled politely and said, “Oh yes, I almost forgot about this altogether, silly me.”","He was a smart person. He turned around and, instead of speaking to Ye Wangchuan, addressed Qiao Nian. “Qiao Nian, since this has been clarified, you may return first. I’ll get your Form Teacher to inform you about how this matter will be handled by the school.”","He paused as he looked up at Wu Jie who was scared by now. He looked away sympathetically, then said quietly, “Don’t worry, the school will definitely give you a fair explanation.”","For students like Wu Jie who maliciously spread rumors, a punishment was definitely going to be imposed. This was according to the school rules and regulations.","If it wasn’t for Qiao Nian saying that the College Entrance Examinations were upcoming soon and that Wu Jie should not be expelled because of such a matter since she had good grades, the school would really have considered expulsion in order to please Ye Wangchuan.","Wu Jie heard every word Principal Yu said and suddenly looked up at him. Her eyes behind those glasses turned red and she clenched her fists in fear.","She turned to look at Qiao Chen, who had had no qualms about shoving all responsibility to her. She then looked at the other girl who appeared cold and distant, but who had never once treated her badly or bullied her. Eventually, she mustered the courage to call out to her. “Qiao Nian.”","Qiao Nian stopped in her tracks and turned around.","Wu Jie looked extremely pathetic at this moment, and her tears finally fell.","She choked on her words as she said, “That day, after you, Liang Bowen, and the rest left, it was really Qiao Chen who deliberately told me about it. She said that you’d beaten someone up and caused that person serious injuries. She even told me that as long as I blew this matter up, the school would surely punish you. I wasn’t thinking right at that moment and hence put it up on the school forum... I know I did wrong. I shouldn’t have been jealous of you. But if it wasn’t for Qiao Chen instigating me over the phone, telling me that it would be pointless if I just went to the teacher since the teacher would defend you for your good results, I wouldn’t have thought of posting on the forum. I’m sorry...”","She was guilty and regretful all at once, but more than that, she was fearful of being punished.","Covering her face, tears dripped down her fingers.. She was evidently upset."]},{"number":583,"title":"Chapter 583 - Qiao Chen Really Caused Huge Trouble","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian saw how upset she was. She was squatting on the ground, tugging at her own sleeves aggressively as she cried uncontrollably. And yet, Qiao Nian was not moved. She eyed her coldly and simply said, “You’re from Class A, and you’ve been in this class since the first year. Let’s ignore what you posted about me on the forum. For the sake of blowing this matter up, you deliberately mentioned that our classmates ostracized you. Did you even consider how others would feel?”","Wu Jie stopped crying. She looked up at Qiao Nian, almost stunned. Tears still filled her face and she was now biting her lip, unable to say anything.","She thought about how Jiang Tingting had changed seats for her in class.","And how they would always invite her along when they were having gatherings or meals.","She remembered how she was having very bad cramps when her period came during physical education classes, and how the girls in class would hurry to the store to get her pads, while the guys would help her to apply for leave with the male teacher. Qiao Nian had even taken her to the school clinic to get some medicine...","This time, her tears were genuine.","She covered her face, too ashamed to face anyone. “I’m sorry, I’m sorry.”","Qiao Nian looked at her with annoyance, her eyes deeper than one could tell. She said calmly, “You shouldn’t be apologizing to me, but to the classmates and teachers who’ve always cared for you!”","However, when it came to apologies, they often came too late. It was meaningless now.","Nobody would forgive another unconditionally. Even the deepest relationships would not tolerate insincere acts. Some things, once lost, were gone for good.","Wu Jie cried miserably.","Her mother was worried that she’d cry too hard that she would be out of breath. Not bothering to find fault with Shen Jingyan and Qiao Chen at a time like this, she quickly went over to pat Wu Jie on the back.","Ye Wangchuan stopped in his tracks momentarily when he walked past the middle-aged man in a suit. He looked at him without much expression, but with an incredibly oppressive look in his eyes. “Since you’re not intending to settle Wei Qi’s matter privately, then we’ll go public.”","“Young Master Ye, didn’t we agree on...” Shen Jingyan was taken aback.","“Back then, I did tell Old Master that I’d take a step back so we won’t make things too ugly.” He paused for a second and glanced past Qiao Chen with his beautiful eyes as he fiddled with the bead bracelet on his wrist. His eyes were slightly red with ferocity. “But since you guys are not worried about things becoming ugly, then there’s no need for me to go on with my wishful thinking and save you the embarrassment.”","Shen Jingyan went pale, unable to say a word.","It was embarrassing enough that Wei Qi was to be jailed!","It was precisely because they found his incarceration to be such an embarrassment that they pulled some strings to settle this. They contacted Old Master Ye and made use of the connections with him to negotiate for a private settlement of Wei Qi’s matter.","Wei Qi would still have to be imprisoned, but his trial and sentence would not have to be made public. After all, for a family like theirs, it was best to keep such news under wraps.","And yet, because of Qiao Chen’s mess, the agreement that they fought so hard to come to was entirely ruined!","They were in the wrong in the first place, so even if the other party did not want to do them a favor, there was nothing they could say!","Ye Wangchuan didn’t see how he reacted. He said, “I will be contacting Cai Gang. When the sentence is out, the news that has to be reported will be reported as usual, and the procedures will be carried out as expected.”","Shen Jingyan didn’t expect this matter to make it onto the news. He got flustered and wanted to give it one last shot by talking it out with Qiao Nian. He walked towards her, but when he looked up, he was faced with her back view. She had left..."]},{"number":584,"title":"Chapter 584 - Getting His ‘Wife’ to Receive His Call","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","In the car.","Qiao Nian pulled out her cell phone the moment she got into the car and started typing away, seeming to be very focused on chatting with someone.","Ye Wangchuan had one hand on the steering wheel while the other arm rested by the window. He appeared carefree, unlike his domineering presence just now. He asked the girl beside him, “Where are we going later?”","Qiao Nian had just replied to Liang Bowen’s messages and looked up upon hearing his question. She thought for a moment before saying, “Home. I want to check on something.”","She had gone to the hospital to visit Uncle Chen in the morning. Uncle Chen’s legs weren’t in good condition, and she had spoken to the specialist about it. The specialist said that Uncle Chen had been bedridden all this time, and his bones were starting to degenerate. If this went on, it would be impossible for Uncle Chen to undergo surgery in the future even if technology was sufficiently advanced by then.","She had looked through the information about muscle and bone degeneration from being bedridden long-term. Uncle Chen’s situation was rather complicated, so many case studies that she had found were not actually applicable.","Qiao Nian wanted to look for other similar cases online.","“Mm.” Ye Wangchuan singlehandedly reversed the car. The Phaeton was rather spacious on the inside, and he saw that Qiao Nian was not wearing very thick clothing today. It was cold out, and she was only in a simple hoodie and a cap. She didn’t look cold, but she was curled up slightly, so he was unsure if she was.","He raised a brow and retracted his arm resting by the window, rolling the window back up. Then, he discreetly turned on the air-conditioning.","This car model of Jiang Li’s was specially modified by a 4S store. Everything in the car was of the best and latest edition.","Even the air-conditioning!","The air was warm and comfortable, not the least bit stuffy.","Qiao Nian initially had not noticed his little gestures. But all of a sudden, she realized that her neck wasn’t feeling as cold anymore, and when she looked up, she saw that the window had been rolled up. She pursed her lips and did not say a word, but deep down she felt something.","Suddenly.","The cell phone that he’d placed by the side rang.","Qiao Nian saw that he was driving and held the cell phone up to see who was calling. She handed it to him and said, “Gu San’s call, are you picking it up?”","Ye Wangchuan didn’t reach out to get it, and instead naturally said, “I’m driving, help me get it.”","Qiao Nian furrowed her brows subconsciously. She saw that his right hand was obviously free. Anyway, she turned the car Bluetooth on and picked up the call.","“Hello, Master Wang!” Gu San’s energetic voice reverberated in the car.","The Bluetooth speaker in the car was rather loud, and with Gu San’s energy-packed voice, it sounded even louder.","She reached out to lower the volume before going back to using her cell phone.","“Hello? Master Wang? Why’s there no sound? Hey, did it not get through?”","She was looking down on her phone, but she could hear the background noise from the other end and Gu San’s confused questioning every once in a while.","“This is strange, it’s through. Why is there no sound?”","“Hey, Master Wang, can you hear me?” After talking to himself for a bit, he spoke into the cell phone again.","Ye Wangchuan was looking straight at the road ahead. He was driving while listening to Gu San revealing his IQ through all that he was saying. Ye Wangchuan didn’t really want to respond to him, but he was afraid that he would continue showing Qiao Nian how silly he was. Hence, he eventually replied, “I hear you. Speak.”","“Master Wang, you heard me. Why didn’t you make a sound?” Gu San immediately asked. He sounded slightly despondent.","Ye Wangchuan was speechless.","Because you never gave me a chance to speak!","Gu San wasn’t really asking for his actual answer though.. He thought about the news he had just received and excitedly said before Ye Wangchuan had a chance to respond, “I just received news that they’ve managed to check that batch of goods. They got the sea customs to stop it for now!”"]},{"number":585,"title":"Chapter 585 - Gu San: I Think Sun Is at Least 40 Years Old","paragraphs":["He had no idea that his phone call was being broadcast via the car Bluetooth and that Qiao Nian was listening to him as well. He excitedly reported to Ye Wangchuan, “Young Master Qin got someone to check the goods. The findings are pretty huge this time.”","Ye Wangchuan turned the steering wheel singlehandedly, showing off his strong wrist. On his wrist was a simply beaded bracelet, and next to the bracelet was a Seven silver bangle, eye-catching and alluring. He wasn’t as excited as Gu San. Instead, he didn’t seem surprised at all as he said, “Mm, I got it.”","Gu San was too excited and did not notice the calmness in his voice. He still couldn’t mask his enthusiasm. “We’ve tracked this batch of goods for so long. Everyone worked overtime for one month without being able to find these goods. Young Master Qin is so smart to have thought of the Red Alliance.”","The person who thought about going to the Red Alliance was Ye Wangchuan. Qin Si was simply following his orders.","Gu San wasn’t aware of the internal workings and thought that it was Qin Si who came up with this idea and managed to get the connections. He exclaimed, “This Red Alliance is too impressive! The tech department of the Ninth Branch had been looking so hard for it without managing to find a clue. How do you think the Red Alliance managed to get it? Tsk! What a pity they’re just being hackers with this technology!","“If only they were willing to join the Ninth Branch.” He lowered his voice, sounding regretful. “What a pity, I heard that everyone in the Red Alliance never bows down to anyone. They do things as they wish without rules and regulations, and they have always been high and mighty. They won’t easily work under anyone. Moreover, they would be indignant at receiving orders from us. I wonder what kind of people would ever be able to manage people like Sun from the Red Alliance.","“That person must be really impressive. Only then could this entire group listen to ‘him’!”","Ye Wangchuan turned to look at the girl who was still on her cell phone. Her cap was pulled down low, revealing only her cold and exquisite jawline. He couldn’t see her expression, but given how she was typing away every once in a while, he figured that she was replying to messages.","He looked back on the road and smiled, saying, “Mm, it’s a very impressive person.”","Sun was definitely related to Qiao Nian!","But he couldn’t conclude with certainty whether she was Sun!","This was because she was simply too calm. Hearing Gu San talk about the Red Alliance, she could still ignore him entirely, as if she was not involved.","He was almost 100% sure at first, but given her reaction, he was a little unsure now.","But he was still about 80% confident.","His getting Qin Si to look for the Red Alliance was also a way of sounding her out. The Red Alliance hardly ever took up requests. Regarding requests like tracking orders, they had practically never accepted any. Hence, they taking this one up... Ye Wangchuan’s eyes deepened. He didn’t think further.","Gu San was still excitedly saying, “... Young Master Qin said that the Red Alliance hasn’t taken up any order from the black market in half a year. We’re lucky that ours was the first one they’ve taken up after all this time. And, it’s by their most impressive Sun! Young Master Qin said this is the first time he’s encountered someone this incredible. In the past, the Ninth Branch would only give him a rough idea of where the things were, but this Sun sent him a map with the precise location, and with four words—the goods are here! Tsk... this person is insane!","“Daring to meddle with illegal goods and such a risky request, ‘he’ really lives up to the name of the Red Alliance! Seeing how ‘he’ handles things, this person must be at least 40. Without the experience of someone of that age, nobody could have such drive and capability!”"]},{"number":586,"title":"Chapter 586 - Earning Two Million Yuan and Losing 200 Million Yuan","paragraphs":["“Master Wang, what do we do with those goods?”","Ye Wangchuan’s eyes were dark and his voice was deep. “Leave it there for the time being. Let Qin Si watch it. We’ll talk when I get back.”","“Alright, I’ll let Young Master Qin know.”","There was no music playing in the car, and Qiao Nian did not have her earbuds on. Upon hearing Gu San say that she must be at least 40 years old, she raised a brow then lowered her cap again. She was curled up comfortably in her seat, and just as her gaze landed on her cell phone, it vibrated again.","She looked at it.","Slim Waist Control’s notification.","Qiao Nian tapped it open.","[Slim Waist Control: Big boss, what’s with you tracking your own goods?]","Qiao Nian’s eyes were extremely dark as she typed slowly.","[Sun: Didn’t notice when I was tracking them.]","[Slim Waist Control: That counts as a reason?!!!]","Qiao Nian’s eyelashes fluttered slightly as she considered his question, then replied—","[Sun: I think it does.]","[Slim Waist Control: ...]","[Slim Waist Control: You’re good!]","Qiao Nian saw the two messages that came in right away and did not reply, but another one was sent.","[Slim Waist Control: That batch of ores is worth a few hundred million yuan. Someone said that the goods have been stopped...]","A lot of people thought that the Red Alliance was just a hacker group. Even those in the illegal business assumed so. But he, the Fox, and Guan Yan knew that Sun was also into ores.","The ores were imported from Continent F and resold to the rest of the world.","Some others had tried out this business too, and they did it pretty menacingly. They basically paid the peasants from Continent F for the ores that the people practically fought for to dig up. It was a bloody exchange.","Sun’s ore business, on the other hand, was more like a typical transaction.","They collaborated with the peasants in Continent F. They took the ores, worked on them as needed, and resold them, then gave the peasants 35% of the profits.","The profit margin was smaller, but a lot more humane. Hence, he was always willing to work for this big boss.","Although their ore business was not much different from a usual business transaction, they were working with an illegal, restricted area, after all. Given that an illegal area was involved, it was considered illegal goods at every custom.","This batch of goods was practically doomed.","[Slim Waist Control: Big boss, I know you’re rich and not lacking money. But before you take up any requests in the future, please take a look at what it’s about. If we continue to make losses, we’ll go bankrupt soon!! I don’t want to sell my body in a bar in the illegal area to pay for my debts.]","Qiao Nian looked at the last sentence and couldn’t help but smile.","She replied.","[Sun: Don’t worry, nobody would want you even if you sold yourself. There’s no point in you selling your body if there are no takers. I’m more inclined to sending you to work in a mine in Continent F. You can earn your wages by the day, and won’t go jobless.]","[Slim Waist Control: ...]","[Slim Waist Control: Damn, you’re heartless!]","[Slim Waist Control: I think about selling my body all the time, alright. I think I have what it takes! I’m especially good-looking, but I can’t outdo you, Boss. You’re selling things in the hundreds of millions. I... can’t do that. You’re only earning two million yuan for taking up an order, but you’re paying a few hundred million yuan in return... What sort of business model is this? What are you after?]","Qiao Nian replied rather seriously.","[Sun: For a smile?]","[Slim Waist Control: ... Big boss, I love to smile too, can you take me into consideration? I’ll smile for you every day, until you go broke.]"]},{"number":587,"title":"Chapter 587 - Worried That Qiao Nian Would Hear It","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian was supporting her chin. Upon hearing Gu San talk to Ye Wangchuan about the ores and the Red Alliance, she replied him seriously.","[Sun: This time was an accident. Don’t worry, there shouldn’t be a next time.]","Back then, she was unsure how she could return the favor. Perhaps this batch of ores would help her repay part of it.","Qiao Nian exited the app after replying, not intending to reply any further. Slim Waist Control was the most talkative of the few of them. They had no idea what he usually did during the day, but it appeared that he had a lot of time to chat in the group. No matter who was replying him, he could manage to drag on the conversation for two hours. Since she knew that this was his unique ability, she couldn’t be bothered to go on chatting with him for now.","The moment she exited the Red Alliance app, a call came in.","Qiao Nian took a look at the caller ID. Her carefree expression faded, and she was more serious now as she answered the call. “Hello.”","Her voice wasn’t gentle and girly like Qiao Chen’s and Wu Jie’s. For some reason, her voice was slightly hoarse.","But it was a nice kind of hoarse. When she spoke slowly, it sounded like the alluring tune of a cello.","Ye Wangchuan was on the phone with Gu San initially. But he was getting distracted while listening to him talk about the batch of goods.","“Master Wang, I hear Miss Qiao’s voice. Are you with her?” Gu San was extremely vigilant, since he was talking about something so confidential. He immediately stopped talking about the Red Alliance, Ninth Branch, and the restricted area, and instead said, “I’ll wait for you to be back, then.”","He wasn’t guarded against Qiao Nian. It was just that Qiao Nian was, at best, slightly better than an ordinary high school girl. He didn’t think much of it.","He would assume that what they were discussing—the Red Alliance, Ninth Branch, restricted area—was unheard of to her.","He wasn’t looking down on Qiao Nian, either. He just didn’t think that she would be exposed to this sort of information.","These affairs were also very confidential, and a lot of larger and more powerful households in Beijing wanted to get hold of it. He was afraid that Qiao Nian would accidentally talk about it when chatting with her classmates, leading to consequences that would be too much to handle...","Ye Wangchuan understood his worries the moment he sensed Gu San’s alertness. He himself was not fully certain of how Qiao Nian and Sun were related. Even if he knew, he couldn’t reveal it without their permission. Hence, he did not ask Gu San to go on and instead said a quiet ‘Mm’ before hanging up.","The car quietened all of a sudden.","So, he could hear the person on the line with her.","“Now? Nothing much now, actually. I went to see Uncle Chen today, he’s not really in a very good state. I spoke a little to his doctor and plan to take a look at some overseas data to see if there are any similar to his... Oh, it’s very serious? Oh... I can go over. What time?”","Ye Wangchuan heard her discuss the time with the other party in a very close and familiar manner before she hung up.","When she was done with the call, he raised his brow but asked neutrally, “What happened?”","Qiao Nian put her cell phone down and turned to look at him with her beautiful face. She said with some frustration, “An elderly in my friend’s family is ill, I heard it’s very serious. They want me to have a look at him. I’ll be going to Beijing tomorrow.”","Her friend was from Beijing?","Ye Wangchuan looked surprised, but not especially so. He just found it strange that she did not ask that friend out for a meal when she took her examinations in Beijing.","“Do you want me to book you the flight tickets?”"]},{"number":588,"title":"Chapter 588 - Wei Ling Really Wanted to Slap Qiao Chen","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian looked up at him and her features softened. She seemed to be getting used to the way they interacted and was no longer as resistant to him as if he was an outsider. She shook her head and said, “No need, there are many flights to Beijing from Rao City, I’ll get it myself.”","She paused for a while before saying, “He might’ve bought it for me already. We’ll see.”","In order to purchase someone else’s flight tickets, one needed their full name and identity card number. Ye Wangchuan had no idea how close this ‘friend’ was to her that he would even know her identification card number. He squinted a little threateningly but said gently, “If you need help, just let me know. Gu San is familiar with this, he sometimes manages to get tickets for even the sold-out flights.”","Qiao Nian thought about the last time she and Liang Bowen returned from Beijing. This was exactly what had happened—there were no longer any seats in the first-class cabin, but he had managed to change her economy seat ticket to a first-class one. She had only found out that he’d done this privately when she got the ticket.","Qiao Nian felt her heart go warm and fuzzy. She cut the civilities and said rather naturally, “Okay, I’ll let you know if I can’t get it.”","Ye Wangchuan looked at how she no longer seemed guarded against him and couldn’t help but smile. He didn’t say a word.","The car drove on quietly.","...","The atmosphere in the Qiao Family was exceptionally heavy now.","Wei Ling pulled a long face as she sat on the couch quietly.","With her not talking, Qiao Weimin and Shen Qiongzhi dared not say a word, either. After all, it was really Qiao Chen who made a grave mistake out of selfishness this time. It was their fault that Wei Family’s brother was going to be reported on the news. What made things worse was that Qiao Chen would require Wei Ling’s help for her development in Beijing in the future.","Shen Qiongzhi had always made impulsive comments without much thought, just because she was the elder sister-in-law. But even she was quiet now.","Meanwhile, it was Shen Jingyan who adjusted his collar and spoke up first to the lady on the couch. “Alright, what’s happened has happened. There’s no point in you being angry now. That Ye fellow doesn’t want to give us the face, and we can’t possibly go to Old Master Ye for help again. We can only accept it.”","He said to “accept it” like it was an easy matter. But Wei Ling felt the fury in her heart rise with no outlet to vent.","If it was some outsider who implicated her brother, she wouldn’t possibly let it go.","But Qiao Chen was Shen Jingyan’s biological niece. Could she really hold onto grudges for long!","But her brother was in a terrible state as it was. He was already in the juvenile center initially. Now, because of Qiao Chen’s mess, he not only had to be incarcerated for three years, he even had to be on the news.","In a social circle like theirs, how was Wei Qi ever going to regain his pride and dignity in the future?!","She wanted to strangle Qiao Chen and give her two tight slaps.","Wei Ling was heaving angrily, her expression awful.","“Don’t be too angry now. At least the Ye fellow only said he’d get Cai Gang to do what was needed, he did not say how long Wei Qi would be in there for.”","Shen Jingyan had been her husband for so many years now, he knew what she was thinking. He was also furious with what Qiao Chen had done, but as he said, there was no going back. They could only accept it and move forward.","“He still isn’t making things too ugly for now. Don’t think too much about the news, most people don’t follow this sort of social affairs. As for the social media news, I’ll get someone to mask it and make sure it won’t circulate too much. There won’t be many people knowing about Wei Qi.”"]},{"number":589,"title":"Chapter 589 - I Heard That Wei Lou Got Someone as Well","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","He lowered his voice and spoke in a deep and quiet tone. He sounded convincing, but he knew just how untrue this was.","This was deception.","In a social circle like theirs, nobody really cared what the majority population thought. What mattered was whether there was any blemish on the individual.","Any blemish that did not make it to the news could be washed over.","But once it became public, Wei Qi’s future would be greatly affected!","That Ye fellow was more hard-hearted than he looked. He was also cruel enough to trample over them easily, leaving them with no guts to fight back.","“Chen Chen has made it into Qing University and Professor Cheng Wu favors her, she has a bright future. She didn’t do things right this time, and I’ve already told her off. She’s not silly, she knows her mistake. You...” Shen Jingyan inhaled sharply as he turned to look at her.","“I know.”","Of course, Wei Ling knew that Qiao Chen had made it into Qing University. If it wasn’t for the fact that Qiao Chen made it into Qing University but not Qiao Nian, she would have slapped her already. She held back simply because she knew that Qiao Chen had a bright future.","Wei Ling slowly calmed herself down and turned to Shen Jingyan and the Qiao Family coldly. “She needs to stop acting as she wishes in the future. Discuss things with us before doing anything. If this happens again, I can’t even help her as an aunt!”","“Of course, of course. I’ll tell her off when we get back.” Shen Qiongzhi knew that Qiao Chen had caused huge trouble this time. Upon seeing that Wei Ling was willing to let things go, she quickly smiled and nodded submissively.","Wei Ling couldn’t be bothered with her. She was still furious and was better off not looking at Shen Qiongzhi. She turned to the man and said seriously, “Mom told me that Old Master might not make it.”","Shen Jingyan felt his heart sink. He frowned and asked, “When was this?”","“Yesterday,” Wei Ling said softly, but she sounded stressed out by it. “Old Master has been slipping into unconsciousness every now and then since yesterday. The doctor said there’s some internal bleeding, and he was in critical condition at one point last evening. But in the morning, he was conscious and clear again. His blood pressure rose again just now and he was going into a coma again, it could be a stroke.”","Strokes were common among the elderly.","They differed in severity. Some stroke patients recovered perfectly fine if the stroke wasn’t serious and if it was treated in time.","But if the stroke happened to be serious and was not attended to in time, the consequences could be dire.","The worst-case scenario was instant death.","A slightly better case would result in partial paralysis and affected cognition among others... in other words, even a better case might mean losing the ability to live and function independently.","Wei Ling was in a cheongsam and a shawl today. She didn’t avoid Qiao Weimin and Shen Qiongzhi as she said to Shen Jingyan slowly and seriously, “My grandpa’s health hasn’t been good all along. And these two years, he’s been... in bed most of the time. If it’s a stroke, the situation is probably bad. I’d planned to return to Beijing today, but now Wei Qi...”","Her tone wasn’t too pleasant as she brought this up.","Shen Qiongzhi and Qiao Weimin stood by the side like students who’d misbehaved.","The good thing was that Wei Ling did not have the energy to bother about them at this point. She inhaled deeply and said, “My mom intends to get Liang Lu to operate on Old Master. I heard that Wei Lou had gotten someone as well, but I’m not sure who. I doubt there’s another local surgeon as skilled as Liang Lu. I wonder if he’s gotten a specialist from overseas?”","A flash of disgust and annoyance shone in Wei Ling’s eyes as she mentioned her cousin."]},{"number":590,"title":"Chapter 590 - Sister Nian Has Arrived in Beijing","paragraphs":["Shen Jingyan was calmer than her. After some thought, he said, “I doubt it’s an overseas specialist. The elderly usually don’t trust foreign doctors, and have always insisted on turning to local doctors. The best neurologist in the country is none other than Liang Lu. Since Mom has contacted Liang Lu, I believe they couldn’t have gotten a better doctor than her...”","“That’s true, too.”","Wei Ling nodded but still felt unsettled. She looked up at him. “I’ll still have to make a trip down tomorrow. This is a crucial moment for Old Master, I can’t let Mom face this alone.”","If it was a stroke, then the splitting of assets would come into the picture.","The Wei Family’s business was huge and many people were involved. Splitting the family assets was a serious and important matter. Whoever spent more time by Old Master’s hospital bed now might just manage to get a larger share.","Wasn’t everybody rushing back from other states and countries just because of this?","Shen Jingyan had been in the industry for so long and knew the thoughts that went on in their heads. He nodded solemnly. “Mm, it’d be good for you to return this time.”","It wouldn’t be helpful for her to face Qiao Chen all the time, anyway.","If it wasn’t for Wei Qi’s case, Wei Ling could have returned to Beijing today already. Now, he was also stuck in this city and unable to fly to Beijing until Wei Qi’s sentence was finalized.","...","The next day.","Qiao Nian’s flight arrived at the capital airport.","She had just gotten off the plane and was walking out. She had one hand in her pocket and the other holding onto her black cell phone. Her white earphones were plugged in, leaving the dangling wire that seemed to accentuate her jawline.","“Hello.”","Qiao Nian arrived at 10:00 AM in Beijing. It was a 7:00 AM flight, and she had gotten up at 5:00 AM to prepare for departure. She took the pills and other handy items, and Jiang Li sent her to the airport. She had to collect her air tickets and queue for the security checks, leaving her with no time to rest. She was now exceptionally tired, and her beautiful eyes were squinted. The tips of her eyes were a faint red from the lack of sleep, making her appear slightly threatening.","She purchased a canned coffee from the vending machine when she passed by one. After conveniently scanning the QR code to make payment, she picked her coffee up, pulled the tab, and started sipping.","It was October now, and Beijing was colder than Rao City. Here in the North, the air was slightly drier, and she realized that she was dressed too thin for the weather here.","Fortunately, the warm coffee from the vending machine allowed her to warm her hands, and Qiao Nian felt much more comfortable with that. She was leaning against the wall, watching the people in the airport. Soon enough, she found herself looking at her cell phone.","The caller ID showed Ye Wangchuan.","The man’s voice was deep and alluring, and the background was rather noisy. “You’re off the plane?”","“I just got off.” Qiao Nian looked up again and took another sip of coffee. Her slender fingers were wrapped around the can as she twisted the can casually. Her lush lashes and dark eyes were exceptionally beautiful. After remembering something, she asked a little unnaturally, “You?”","“Ha.” The man chuckled genuinely. “Is this reciprocal concern?”","Qiao Nian didn’t think too much when she asked him. Now that he responded this way, she was unsure of what to say.","Fortunately, Ye Wangchuan saved her the trouble by going on. “I just got off the plane as well, and I’m preparing to go over now. I checked the time and thought you’d have landed about now, so I called to ask.”","He and Gu San had already left the previous night.","Qiao Nian didn’t have to ask to know where they were headed.","It should be the customs where the goods were held.","Well, it was worth a few hundred million yuan, after all...","She acknowledged what he said softly and blinked her eyes tiredly."]},{"number":591,"title":"Chapter 591 - The Other Partys Voice Was Too Young","paragraphs":["Ye Wangchuan could tell that she was still sleepy. He told the people around him to be quiet for the time being and said gently, “Be careful when you’re there. If there’s anything, call my aunt. She’s in Beijing. I told her that you were coming over today. Her phone is switched on 24 hours a day. She’ll be waiting for you to call her anytime.”","Qiao Nian didn’t expect him to tell Ye Lan that she was coming over. She was silent for a moment, not knowing how to answer. She said softly, “I might not have time to eat with Aunt Ye.”","“I know.” The man on the other end of the line seemed to have arranged everything. “I told her that you came to Beijing for something, so you might not have time to eat with her. She won’t disturb you. Go busy yourself with your friend first. If you have time, ask her out. If you don’t have time, then forget it. I only said that you can look for her if you have anything. She has some connections in Beijing and can help you settle ordinary matters.","“In addition, I got Gu San to book a hotel for you. You can stay in the previous apartment if you want. I’ll send you the passcode for the door. The auntie inside will prepare fresh fruits and vegetables every day and place them in the fridge. If you don’t want them, you can call delivery.”","Qiao Nian agreed and did not reject his arrangement. She looked up at the time and said to him, “I’m hanging up.”","“You can still find someone if it’s urgent. I’ll send you his number. He’ll be returning to the capital today as well.”","“Okay.”","After hanging up, Qiao Nian put down her phone and saw that he had sent a message.","On it was the location and room number of the hotel that Gu San had booked. There was also the district number and password for the house in the Rhine Apartment along with a string of phone numbers.","A name followed behind.","Qin Si.","Qiao Nian’s eyes swept over the two words. She recalled how Gu San had called him Young Master Qin in the car yesterday and roughly knew who this Qin Si was.","It seemed like if he went over to investigate the goods personally, this Young Master Qin would temporarily return to the capital.","Her eyes were quite roguish. She saved the number and clicked on a phone number in her contacts. She was about to call Wei Lou.","An unknown number from Beijing called.","Qiao Nian narrowed her eyes and picked up the call. An unfamiliar male voice came from the other end.","It was someone Wei Lou had called to pick her up. He said that he had already arrived outside the airport. Seeing that her flight had arrived, he asked her roughly when she would be leaving.","After asking for his specific location, Qiao Nian hung up and walked out of the terminal with her phone.","Outside the airport, a black Mercedes-Benz was parked on the roadside. It was especially eye-catching.","It wasn’t that the car was expensive.","Beijing was bustling. Any random car on the road was worth 30 million yuan. No one would especially look at cars like Mercedes or BMWs on the roadside.","But this car was different.","The car plate was too eye-catching.","The Beijing.00089 car plate pushed to the side of the road, directly suppressing the Maybach’s limelight beside it. Basically, everyone who came out of the airport would look over, curious to see who this car was picking up.","Beside the car, a man in his sixties with white hair was holding a phone and making a call. He looked anxious and spoke quickly.","“...Yes, the plane is here. Miss Qiao hasn’t come out yet. I just called her. She said that she just got off the plane and is coming over to look for me. Young Master, from her voice, Miss Qiao seems to be very young. Did I make a wrong call?”","The old butler of the Wei family was anxious as he reported to the person on the other end hesitantly.","It was not that he doubted anything. It was just that when he made the call earlier, the other party’s voice was too young. He was really worried that this miracle doctor who had come from Rao City would be unreliable."]},{"number":592,"title":"Chapter 592 - The Wei Family Is Going to Be in Chaos","paragraphs":["Old Master Wei’s illness was imminent. It would be too late if he didn’t undergo surgery.","However, Young Master Lou insisted on not letting Professional Liang operate on Old Master Wei. If anything happened to him, the elders in the family would definitely not let Young Master Lou off.","In the past, Old Master Wei doted on Young Master Lou the most. He had also watched Wei Lou grow up. Naturally, he was on his side.","However, this matter could not be messed up. They could only hope that the divine doctor who came from Rao City had some ability!","He had just put down his phone when he saw a girl walking towards him.","At his age, he had long become indifferent to the matters between men and women. He didn’t care much about appearances, either. But that woman was too eye-catching.","The black hoodie made her fair skin look dazzling. Her neck was very long, and there was a red mole on it. Probably because of the weather, her hands were in her pockets. She had her earphones in as she walked over slowly.","Finally, she stopped in front of him.","Lifting the brim of his hat, the old butler saw an overly beautiful face. Her clear eyes looked at him and she asked politely, “Hello, were you the one who called me earlier?”","The old butler was stunned and could not react for a moment. He looked at the girl in front of him, who was definitely not older than 20 years old, in astonishment. Looking at her overly young face, he couldn’t help but cry out, “You are... Miss Qiao?”","This...","The miracle doctor who came from Rao City was so young?!","Qiao Nian raised her eyes and looked at his white hair. She nodded politely. “Hello, I’m Qiao Nian. Just call me by my name.”","The old butler was speechless.","It wasn’t a question of how he should address her now. He couldn’t imagine the reaction of his family when he brought this divine doctor back.","The Wei family was going to be in chaos!","On the way to the Wei family’s house, Qiao Nian sent a message to Wei Lou and told him that she was already in the car.","Afraid that she would fall asleep, she yawned and started a game.","At this moment, people were coming and going in the Wei family’s residence. There were many cars with license plates starting with 0 parked at the entrance of the green tiles and white walls. Not all of the cars were good, but those who knew the industry knew that the owners of cars with 0 license plates in Beijing were usually big shots in the business world.","They were people on the news.","Qin Si had also arrived today. He arrived at the airport at nine and did not go home. When he received a call from home, he rushed over immediately.","At this moment, he was sleepy and exuded a forbidding aura.","Zhang Yang came over with him and saw him yawning non-stop. There was even a bluish-purple ring under his eyes. He joked, “Young Master Qin, why do you look like you haven’t slept all night? Don’t tell me...”","“Don’t f*cking think nonsense!” Qin Si kicked him and said impatiently, “I had something on and flew overseas. I just came back. It would be the same if you took a plane for more than ten hours. How energetic are you?”","Zhang Yang touched his nose. He was smart enough not to ask him why he had gone overseas.","Qin Si and Master Wang were from the same circle, and he was still lacking. What was the point of their circle? It was best not to ask around. If he did, it would be easy to be hated.","He didn’t need to be kicked out of the industry for gossip.","At this moment, he saw a tall figure passing by and whispered, “Young Master Qin, it’s Miss Jiang. She must have followed Professional Liang over. I’ll ask her about Old Master Wei.”"]},{"number":593,"title":"Chapter 593 - Only 30% Confidence, and He Might Still Be Paralyzed","paragraphs":["Qin Si and the Wei family were distant relatives. The two families had been moving around, so he did not rush over after getting off the plane.","However, he wasn’t very interested in this matter. The elder was old and not in good health. It was normal for him to be sick.","The Qin family did not want to reap any benefits from this mess, and they did not bother to stand with the others. Naturally, they were not friendly.","However, since Zhang Yang wanted to ask Jiang Xianrou about the situation, he didn’t mind listening. After all, they were elders, and it was not as if he did not care.","Not long after Jiang Xianrou arrived with Liang Lu, she was about to head to the inner courtyard when Zhang Yang stopped her.","When she saw Zhang Yang and Qin Si, she reluctantly stopped and roughly revealed the situation inside.","“Old Master Wei’s condition isn’t very good. He showed signs of being unconscious half an hour ago. Now that others are calling out to him, he doesn’t have much of a reaction. He only answers occasionally and is clearly not conscious...”","The Wei family had kept Old Master Wei’s condition a secret, and not many people knew about it. Hearing her serious tone, Zhang Yang was stunned. “It’s that serious?”","Jiang Xianrou had followed Liang Lu’s team over and was now considered one of the most anticipated members. She nodded. The person who had asked her was clearly Zhang Yang, but she looked up at Qin Si and said, “Anyway, Old Master Wei’s condition this time is very dangerous. I’m afraid it’s a stroke that will cause cerebral hemorrhage and blood clots in his skull. He has to undergo surgery immediately.”","Qin Si hadn’t woken up yet, and his eyelids were almost glued together. After hearing this, he woke up, frowned, and asked her softly, “How confident are you?”","Jiang Xianrou knew that he was asking about her confidence in the surgery. After some thought, she raised three fingers. “30%.”","“So low?” Qin Si couldn’t help but look surprised.","She pursed her lips and her eyes were arrogant. She said softly, “We still have to undergo the surgery immediately. My mentor said that there is a 30% chance that the patient might have hemiplegia. At this time, Young Master Wei insisted against the surgery. He said that the surgery is too risky and that the Old Master is too old. He’s afraid that he wouldn’t be able to hold on and insisted on waiting for someone to come. He insisted that that person might have a way to treat the patient even without surgery.”","At this point, Jiang Xianrou’s tone was filled with disdain. She said disapprovingly, “A stroke has always been solved by surgery. I’ve never heard of a way to treat it without surgery. He’s just a layman. Don’t be deceived by others! There isn’t an expert in the field of neurosurgery in the country who is better than my mentor. If he continues to drag this on, it will only delay Old Master Wei’s treatment and worsen the situation!”","Zhang Yang nodded and said confidently, “Indeed, there’s no doctor in the country who is more professional than Professional Liang in the field of neurosurgery...”","As one of Liang Lu’s personal disciples, Jiang Xianrou did not say anything. She pursed her lips, but her expression was filled with arrogance.","Qin Si glanced at her and did not retort.","Liang Lu was indeed very good in the field of neurosurgery. There were not many people in the country who could compare to her. Mr. Huang might be able to compare, but he had stopped doing so long ago. Another reason was... Mr. Huang was a master of Traditional Chinese Medicine, after all. No matter how good he was, he was still a Traditional Chinese Medicine practitioner. When a person’s life was at stake, he couldn’t compare to Western Medicine!","He heard that Wei Ying had paid a huge price to hire Liang Lu this time. He had agreed to help Liang Lu with her research project this year.","In the past, Cheng Feng Corporation had always been the one making money on the projects Liang Lu was working on. For some reason, Cheng Feng Corporation suddenly rejected Liang Lu’s team’s proposal this year and chose another project related to medical research. It even caused quite a stir in the medical world.","If Liang Lu didn’t lack money, she probably wouldn’t have dared to take over Old Master Wei’s tricky operation. After all, ruining it would ruin her own reputation!"]},{"number":594,"title":"Chapter 594 - Master Wangs Younger Sister from Rao City","paragraphs":["He hadn’t slept the entire night. Thinking that he didn’t know how long it would be before he could go back, he slid his hand into his pocket and said gloomily, “Let’s go and take a look first.”","They’d know if the person Wei Lou called was a mule or a horse when he came!","After the matters here were over, he still had to spend time eating with Master Wang’s sister who had come all the way from Rao City. He might even be responsible for arranging a hotel for the other party as a guide.","Qin Si’s head hurt at the thought of the number Ye Wangchuan had sent.","He wasn’t in the reception business. Anyone could do such a small matter. He didn’t understand why he had to ask him to go personally.","Gu San said that she was quite young. The girl was only 18 and had not gone to university yet. Why did she come out instead of staying in school to study? She was probably someone with poor grades again!","Qin Si was very impatient with this kind of thing, but since Master Wang had personally asked, he still took it to heart.","However, he didn’t understand what kind of person his sister, who came from such a small place, was!","It would be better if she wasn’t a bumpkin. Beijing was only so big, and there were acquaintances everywhere. He didn’t want the news of him bringing a bumpkin around Beijing’s major attractions to spread in the circle in a few days.","“That’s true. I wonder what kind of expert she is. Why don’t we go in and take a look?”","Zhang Yang had no objections.","Jiang Xianrou had originally wanted to look for Liang Lu, so she had no objections. She shrugged and looked up. “Let’s go together.”","...","The atmosphere in the inner courtyard was heavy. Many people with business bags were here.","Liang Lu was also there.","She kept a straight face and tried to suppress her anger. This was not an occasion for her to lose her temper. She could only forcefully suppress her anger. However, she didn’t want to speak and sat there with a long face.","Wei Ying was the first to lose his cool. He said coldly, “She’s not here yet? When exactly is the person you mentioned arriving?”","Wei Lou was leaning against the wall. He was tall and had his arms around his neck as he looked at his phone. He had just seen the message Qiao Nian had sent him on the way. Thinking about the time, she should be arriving soon.","When he heard Wei Ying’s words, he put away his phone and stood up straight. His hand slipped into his pocket and he looked cynical. “She’s almost here.”","Wei Ying couldn’t stand his idling and disrespectful attitude the most and said angrily, “You said she would be here soon. It’s been an hour and she’s still not here! Wei Lou, are you done fooling around? This is a matter of life and death. It’s not a place for you to fool around! You said you know a miracle doctor in Rao City. I’ve never heard of any expert in the country who is more powerful than Professional Liang!”","“Oh, that’s because you’re inexperienced.”","Wei Ying was aggressive, but he said lightly that he was inexperienced and directly let Wei Ying punch cotton. Wei Ying was so angry that his expression changed on the spot.","When Qin Si and the others came over and saw such a fiery scene, he couldn’t help but smack his lips. He turned to Zhang Yang and said, “Tsk, this Young Master Wei has a terrible temper.”","Liang Lu was still here, but he was already so direct. No matter what, he still had a personality.","However, Qin Si did not agree with him.","After all...","No matter how high his status was, it was hard to guarantee that he would not fall sick in the future. After all, Liang Lu was a top expert in the medical industry in the country. If he offended her with one sentence, it would be difficult to look for her when he needed her in the future...","Jiang Xianrou’s face was as calm as water as she looked at the young man coldly. Her eyes were filled with disdain as she said softly, “I heard that he has been holed up in Rao City and hasn’t returned to the capital for a long time. He might have stayed in a small place for too long and can’t figure out the situation. What kind of powerful doctor in a small place can compare to my mentor?”"]},{"number":595,"title":"Chapter 595 - A Little Ignorant","paragraphs":["“That’s true. I also think Young Master Wei is a little too impulsive.”","As they were arguing.","The old butler led someone in.","Wei Lou placed his hands behind his head in a sloppy manner. He looked past Wei Ying and the others and raised his thin lips. “She’s here.”","She’s here?","Everyone followed his gaze.","The girl who had walked in with the butler of the Wei family walked in slowly. She was wearing a black sweater and a cap. Probably because the weather was cold, she had even pulled the cap of her hoodie over it. Her hands were in her pockets, and there was an earpiece wire stuffed into her ears along the cap. She was wearing a pair of canvas shoes and was walking steadily but casually.","Qin Si’s first impression was that she was young!","When Jiang Xianrou told him that Wei Lou had found a miracle doctor who had come all the way to the city, the image that appeared in his mind was that of an old man in his 80s. He was skinny and wore a Chinese tunic suit, just like the image of the martial arts doctor on television.","However, when they really saw this “divine doctor” from Rao City, not to mention the older generation, even he, a young man who bragged about his new era, could not accept it.","He looked at the girl walking in curiously.","How old was this girl?","She looked like she was not even 20 years old.","Mr. Huang became the honorary president of the Medical Association at 68 years old. When Liang Lu entered the Medical Association at 35 years old, she was regarded as a miracle by the Chinese medical community.","This ‘divine doctor’ was at most 18 or 19 years old...","Qin Si’s lips curled into an amused smile. Previously, he did not think that Wei Lou would be deceived. However, he now agreed with Jiang Xianrou’s point of view. Wei Lou might have been deceived this time!","The female cheat was quite pretty.","Qin Si’s gaze swept across the girl’s long and straight legs wrapped in her jeans. Then, it swept across the cold profile under the brim of her hat. He clicked his tongue and realized that this type seemed to be the type that Young Master Wang liked!","It was the best of this kind!","He was wondering if he should take out his phone and secretly take a photo to send to the group when he heard Jiang Xianrou’s despondent voice. “Qiao Nian?”","Zhang Yang, who had been watching the show, turned to ask her, “Miss Jiang, do you know her?”","“...” A complicated expression appeared on Jiang Xianrou’s face. She clenched her fists and looked at the girl who was gradually approaching. She lowered her voice and said, “Yes, she’s my cousin.”","She really did not want to admit that she had such a cousin! She didn’t understand why Qiao Nian would come with the Wei family’s butler. She added in frustration, “She’s ignorant and incompetent. She just fought someone some time ago. I don’t know why she came here again.”","Qin Si turned his head to look at the girl she said was “ignorant and incompetent.” Her wild and unruly aura was indeed a little uneducated!","“What is she doing here...” Jiang Xianrou stomped her feet in frustration. She didn’t want to have anything to do with Qiao Nian at the moment and did not want to stand out.","...","Everyone gradually returned to their senses.","Whispers began to sound in the courtyard.","“Is she the miracle doctor that Young Master Wei said came all the way here? She’s so young. Did she graduate from high school? What kind of medical skills does she have? Isn’t this ridiculous?”","“Didn’t you see that Professional Liang’s face has turned green? Young Master Wei insisted on saying that this young girl is better. It’s too humiliating. No matter what, Liang Lu is someone who entered the International Medical Association. If they were to compare, she would be at Mr. Huang’s level. This... is a little too much.”","“I don’t think she even memorized all the ABCDs. She’s too ridiculous.”"]},{"number":596,"title":"Chapter 596 - Hidden Boss, Chen Chens Leg Was Cured by Her","paragraphs":["The outsiders were still discussing among themselves, and the expressions of the Wei family members were all ugly. The Wei family had blocked Liang Lu outside and asked them to wait for so long, but the person who came was actually a young girl. This was not fooling around. This kind of behavior made the Wei family lose face in the circle!","If news of this got out tomorrow, they would laugh their heads off!","How could a high school girl compare to Professional Liang?","What miracle doctor?!","Bullsh*t doctor!","In a relatively spacious corner of the courtyard, when someone saw Qiao Nian, they reacted like Jiang Xianrou and recognized her immediately.","“Nian Nian?”","Wei Mingxuan didn’t expect the miracle doctor his son had called over to be a high school girl. He was in a daze when he heard her voice. He turned his head and asked, “President Ye, do you know the doctor Lou’er found?”","Ye Lan was wearing a black cloak and coat today. The shape of the coat was excellent, and she had a white shirt with lotus leaves on it. Her overall appearance made her look cool and elegant. She was already past fifty years old. With her outstanding clothing, one couldn’t tell how old she was.","Ye Lan was also very surprised to see Qiao Nian at the Wei family’s residence. After a while, she figured it out a little. It was said that Wei Mingxuan’s son had stayed in Rao City for a few years. Gu San had said that Nian Nian knew many people who sold pills on the black market. It wasn’t strange for the two of them to know each other.","She nodded immediately and said, “Yes, she treated my grandson’s leg.”","“She’s so young, but her medical skills are so good?” Wei Mingxuan was stunned.","Ye Lan nodded without hesitation. “No matter what, she’s more powerful than you think! I didn’t expect Wei Lou to call her over, and she’s even willing to help. I think Old Master Wei will probably be able to survive this time.”","So powerful?","Wei Mingxuan opened his mouth and was momentarily speechless. He subconsciously looked in Qiao Nian’s direction. It was still that overly young face. “...”","Everyone in Beijing knew that there was a little devil in the Ye family who was pampered by the entire family. He was Ye Lan’s eldest grandson.","That child’s background was heartbreaking. Not long after he was born, his mother died. His biological father was also unreliable. He had been raised in the Ye family since he was young. However, when he was more than a year old, he realized that he had not gotten enough nutrients in the womb. His left foot had congenital leg disorders, and he was no different from a little cripple.","From then on, the little devil’s leg became an indescribable pain in the Ye family. Over the years, they had found many experts.","Both domestically and overseas.","The outcome was not optimistic.","Some time ago, he had heard that Ye Qichen’s leg had been cured. He was still trying to find who the doctor was, but Ye Lan did not reveal it.","He didn’t expect her to be so young!","Qiao Nian heard the whispers around her. Many people were questioning her ability.","She took off her earphones and walked to the man who had welcomed her. She pulled on her hat with her fair and slender hands, looked up, and said hoarsely, “...You didn’t tell me there were so many people.”","There was no accusation in her tone. She simply did not like crowds.","Wei Lou, on the other hand, had changed his cynical attitude when he was talking to Wei Ying earlier. His peach blossom eyes were dark as he looked at the girl in front of him and explained softly, “I haven’t found the time to tell you yet. My family’s situation is more complicated, and I can’t explain it in a short time. Help me see my grandfather first?”","Qiao Nian saw that his hair had been cut short and he had become much more energetic. However, the ear studs on his left ear were sparkling brightly, and he still had the arrogant look from before. She didn’t say anything else and took off the earpiece wire. “Okay,” she said and prepared to enter."]},{"number":597,"title":"Chapter 597 - Never Compared Liang Lu With Qiao Nian","paragraphs":["“Wait!”","Suddenly.","A woman in her fifties suddenly spoke up and blocked their path. Her expression was so dark and gloomy that it was as if water could be squeezed out of her face. She looked Qiao Nian up and down with a sharp gaze and said bluntly, “Wei Lou, is this the miracle doctor you found? How can she compare to Professional Liang? Aren’t you fooling around?”","She had said this several times.","Wei Lou’s temper was average and he had always said whatever he wanted. Previously, she had been insistent on giving face to her elders, but he couldn’t be bothered to give face either. He sneered. “Liang Lu?","“When did I say I would compare them? The two of them can’t even be compared!”","The pills that Qiao Nian casually made could be sold crazily on the black market. Each pill was worth five million yuan. The overseas people were fighting over them like they were treasures.","Liang Lu had been doing research every day for so many years. Apart from publishing a few articles in medical journals, what else had she done?","He didn’t understand how these specialists could act so sanctimoniously like doctors and do things that were beneficial to the patients.","These words were a little too unpleasant.","Liang Lu’s face was so red that it almost dripped blood.","Wei Ying had paid a huge price to invite her over. What was the difference between a slap to Liang Lu’s face and a slap to his face?","He immediately said with a dark expression, “Professional Liang is a member of the International Medical Association! On the other hand, if you randomly find someone to treat your grandfather and something happens to him, who will be responsible?”","“Tsk.” Wei Lou knew that he wanted to use this matter to make things difficult for him. He raised his chin and said without hesitation, “I’ll be responsible, okay?”","“You’re responsible. Can you afford this responsibility?” Wei Ying was clearly unwilling to let go.","At this moment, Qiao Nian heard a relaxed male voice say, “Our eldest branch is in charge. If Dad’s treatment is really delayed because of Wei Lou, I’m willing to give up everything about the Wei family!”","She raised her eyebrows.","Did he trust her so much?","Wei Lou whispered in her ear, “My dad.”","Qiao Nian rubbed her brows and whispered, “I haven’t seen the patient yet. Don’t be too confident. If it doesn’t work...”","A doctor was not omnipotent. Life and death depended on fate. If he was at the end of his rope, she couldn’t guarantee that she could save him.","Wei Lou was actually as surprised as she was that Wei Mingxuan would stand up for Qiao Nian at this moment. After all, she was such a young “miracle doctor.” If he hadn’t known her for a few years, he probably wouldn’t have believed it when he first met her.","However, he didn’t have time to care why his father trusted Qiao Nian so much. He said frivolously, “If you can’t do it, no one in the country can.","“Qiao Nian, my billions and my grandfather’s life are in your hands, anyway. If you can’t do it, I can only follow you to the streets to ask for money.”","If it was in the country, he still believed that someone could cure his grandfather. One was Mr. Huang, and the other was the girl in front of him.","If even this hidden big boss couldn’t do it, then he really didn’t know who could!","Liang Lu?","Sorry, he really did not believe it!","“Hehe.” Qiao Nian smirked and couldn’t be bothered with him. She placed her hands in her pockets and was even more cynical than him. “I’ll take a look first. Maybe the trash can on Rao City will be yours!”","Seeing the confidence in her eyes, Wei Lou was slightly relieved. He smiled and followed her in without saying anything.","If Qiao Nian wanted to treat someone, she had to see the patient first.","The lighting in the room was dim.","The moment she entered, she saw a few doctors in white coats gathered around the bed.","When they saw her enter, they were clearly stunned.","Someone frowned and asked, “Where’s Professional Liang? Isn’t she preparing for surgery? Old Master Wei can’t hold on much longer.”"]},{"number":598,"title":"Chapter 598 - You Also Know Chinese Medicine?","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian looked over and saw an old man lying on the bed. He was thin and had his eyes closed. His lips were also black and blue.","He was the same age as Nie Mi, but he looked much older than him. She didn’t need to look carefully to see the signs of exhaustion on his body.","Wei Lou approached her and ignored the doctors. He asked softly, “How’s my grandfather?”","“He’s not doing well.” Qiao Nian shook her head and walked over. She restrained her expression and said seriously, “I’ll check him first.”","“Okay.” Wei Lou took a deep breath. He was actually very nervous. He clenched his fists and pursed his lips as he said to the doctors, “Move aside first.”","“Young Master Wei, who is she? Where’s Professor Liang?” a doctor raised his chin and asked.","These were all specialists his father had found at the military hospital in Beijing. Wei Lou controlled his temper and said, “They’re outside. This is the doctor I found. Please make way and let her take a look at my grandfather.”","“She’s a doctor?”","A few people in white coats looked at each other and saw the astonishment on each other’s faces.","How old was this girl?","She looked like an ordinary high school student.","Young Master Wei actually said that she was a doctor? It was too ridiculous!","Qiao Nian didn’t care how others looked at her. To be precise, she had never been surprised by how others looked at her. She walked to the bed and pulled a chair to put down the shoulder bag. Then, she sat down and took the elder’s left hand from under the blanket. Her slender fingers rested on the elder’s pulse.","Her movements were natural and smooth, and her actions were very professional.","The doctors from the military hospital were even more surprised. They didn’t expect the other party to know Chinese medicine?","Qiao Nian took the pulse very quickly. It took almost a minute.","Her black eyelashes moved as she raised her head and asked Wei Lou, “The patient fainted because of an emergency fire. It’s not considered a stroke, but there is clotted blood in his skull pressing against the vascular nerves, so the symptoms look more like a stroke. Did he suffer some trauma this morning?”","Wei Ying and the others had also entered and were standing at the door.","Hearing Qiao Nian’s question, guilt flashed across her face.","In the morning, the Old Master had learned from Wei Dongshan that Wei Qi had caused trouble in Rao City. He had called her in for questioning and fainted not long after.","Not many people knew about this matter. Even Wei Lou didn’t know, but she knew very well.","As expected, Wei Lou shook his head. “I wasn’t around this morning. I’m not sure, either.”","“Okay.” Qiao Nian didn’t look at the large group of people behind her. After taking his pulse, she unzipped her bag and took out a set of acupuncture needles.","With her sharp eyes narrowed, she whispered, “I can use acupuncture to draw out the blood clot in his head. When the blood clot dissipates, he will wake up.”","She didn’t finish her sentence.","Old Master Wei’s condition wasn’t just a result of blood clots. When she’d first taken his pulse, she’d discovered that his pulse was weak and his blood and Qi were severely damaged. His internal organs more or less had some problems. It was probably an illness left behind when he was young. After he got older, his chronic illness relapsed, causing him to be bedridden all year round. His body lacked exercise and his organs had aged.","Even if she resolved the blood clot this time, Old Master Wei’s body would encounter other problems in the future.","To put it bluntly, he was already old.","At the age where he knew his fate.","However, if he took good care of himself, it wouldn’t be a problem for him to live for another three to five years.","If something went wrong after three to five years, even Hua Tuo[1] wouldn’t be able to save him!","[1] a Chinese physician who lived during the late Eastern Han dynasty."]},{"number":599,"title":"Chapter 599 - Tsk, Slap Liang Lu in the Face","paragraphs":["Qiao Nian sighed but did not say anything. At this age, she believed that Wei Lou knew what to do.","“How confident are you?” Wei Lou lowered his eyelashes and rarely put away his cynical expression. He tilted his head and asked her seriously.","Qiao Nian thought about it and answered, “70%.”","“The Old Master is old. I can’t guarantee 100% success,” she explained.","Wei Lou looked at the unconscious old man on the bed and then at the girl beside him. The girl was still wearing a cap. Her facial features were very prominent, and she looked cold and not to be trifled with. However, her expression was very serious. It could be seen that she was 70% confident!","Wei Lou knew her for a long time.","He knew very well that Qiao Nian’s 70% confidence was at least 90% for people like Liang Lu.","His grandfather was 70 years old. At the age of an old man who understood the heavens, it was already not bad if she had 70% confidence!","“Do I go ahead?” Qiao Nian was in no hurry to open her acupuncture bag and waited for him to make a decision.","Wei Lou’s tense back relaxed. He looked at her and raised his hand to touch his earlobe. The ear studs shone charmingly. He smiled and said loudly, “Of course. Why not? I already invited you over. It’s not a loss if we don’t do it. Anyway, at most, I’ll sink with you.”","His father had given Wei Ying a military order.","The elders of the family were all gathered here. To a certain extent, he was already tied to Qiao Nian. If they were going to cause trouble, they could just do so together.","Qiao Nian glanced at him with a fierce gaze. She opened the acupuncture bag and revealed a row of acupuncture needles of different lengths. The corners of her lips twitched wildly. “Don’t worry, I’ll try my best not to let you sink. If you really fall, I can only say that you’re unlucky.”","Before Wei Lou could speak, Liang Lu, who had followed them in, snorted coldly and mocked softly, “Hah, I’ve never heard of a technique that can use acupuncture to draw out blood clots!”","Her voice was not loud, but she was an expert in this aspect.","Many people looked at her when she spoke.","Qiao Nian heard it too and looked up. When she saw Liang Lu, she thought for a moment and remembered her face. She matched it with the person in her mind and replied impatiently, “If you haven’t heard of it, read more!”","— She had never heard of a technique that could draw blood with acupuncture.","— Read more if you haven’t heard of it.","“Pfft.” Qin Si couldn’t help but laugh from behind.","After laughing, he held back his laughter and looked at Liang Lu, whose face was turning green and red. Then, he looked at the arrogant girl who was holding down the brim of her hat. He lowered his voice and said to Jiang Xianrou with a faint smile, “Your cousin has quite the personality.”","“...She’s ignorant and ill-mannered!”","Jiang Xianrou’s delicate face was almost dripping blood from anger. With that, she pulled a long face and disregarded her previous thoughts of not getting involved with Qiao Nian. She said angrily, “Qiao Nian, you’re only in your third year of high school. You don’t even know any medical skills in university. Do you know Old Master Wei’s identity? Why are you acting so recklessly?”","With Old Master Wei’s identity, she could become famous after treatment.","If anything went wrong, the consequences would be severe.","At Liang Lu’s level, she was still unwilling to take over this troublesome mess in the beginning.","Qiao Nian was only a high school student. She had never even learned basic medical knowledge systematically. What did she know? How dare she appear on such an occasion?","If Old Master Wei died, their Jiang family would be implicated by her!","Qiao Nian raised her eyes and saw Jiang Xianrou in the crowd. A hint of surprise appeared in her eyes as she looked at Wei Lou with a headache. It seemed like he was looking for trouble."]},{"number":600,"title":"Chapter 600 - Your Sister Nian Is a Hidden Boss","paragraphs":["Wei Lou didn’t expect Jiang Xianrou to be here, either. He gave her a sorry look and shrugged his shoulders, looking helpless.","Qiao Nian retracted her gaze and said slowly, “His identity is not a patient?”","What she said was right. Jiang Xianrou choked on her question.","“Ha.” Qin Si found this girl more and more interesting. She was wild, arrogant, cold, and had a vicious mouth.","Young Master Wang really liked that type.","If not for the fact that there were many people around, he would have taken a photo immediately.","After saying that, Qiao Nian didn’t want to waste any more time. She turned her head and placed the acupuncture needles on the bed. She casually said to the young man beside her, “I’m preparing to start. When are you planning to clear the area?”","“Clear the scene now.”","Wei Lou knew that he had caused her a lot of trouble. He didn’t delay and quickly urged everyone in the room to leave.","Wei Mingxuan was taking responsibility.","Wei Ying was speechless.","As the second branch, she did not say anything. Even if the other elders of the Wei family were angry at the eldest branch for causing trouble, they were not willing to stand out.","Although the second family was very active, and Wei Mingxuan was more capable than Wei Ying all these years, most of Old Master Wei’s connections were in Wei Mingxuan’s hands.","It was just that Wei Mingxuan was more concerned about his family and was soft-hearted. Therefore, after Wei Ying divorced, he brought the two children back to their parents’ house and changed his surname to Wei. He then jumped up and down to fight for the inheritance.","These people were all smart. No one would provoke Wei Mingxuan at such a sensitive time.","The group went out and waited for two hours.","For two hours, Old Master Wei’s door was tightly shut. There was no movement at all.","There was no movement inside, and the people outside could not leave either.","As Qin Si was quite interested in the person inside, he restrained his temper and waited calmly with his arms crossed.","Zhang Yang, who had come with him, was a little impatient. He turned back and saw that this person, who was usually the most impatient, was able to keep his cool today. He leaned over curiously and said, “It’s been two hours and she’s still not out. Young Master Qin, do you think Miss Jiang’s cousin is capable?”","“It’s hard to say.” Qin Si glanced at Jiang Xianrou, who had been pacing back and forth with an ugly expression since two hours ago.","Looking at her messages and who she was calling, he shook his head with an unclear meaning. “From the looks of it, this cousin of hers has never studied medicine before.”","Zhang Yang opened his mouth in surprise. “Then how come she still dares to chase everyone out and perform acupuncture on Old Master Wei alone?”","If someone died here, she would probably have to go to jail!","The kind where she would sit in prison for the rest of her life.","Qin Si was tired from standing. He changed his position and pouted, letting him look to the other side. He said softly, “But look at Wei Lou and Wei Mingxuan’s attitudes. They don’t seem to have randomly found someone.”","Zhang Yang looked up at the two people he was talking to. Indeed, he was very calm.","“Then...”","“Don’t ask me.” Qin Si’s shoulders drooped. He didn’t feel responsible at all as he said irresponsibly, “I just don’t know if the person inside is a mule or a horse, so I can’t say for sure.”","If Gu San was here, he would definitely not be able to help but pull his ear and shout, “She’s not a mule or a horse. The one inside is a big boss! A hidden big boss!!”","Wei Ying and Liang Lu had been standing together for two hours and were already a little impatient. She lowered her eyebrows and kept looking at the time."]}]);
